1
00:00:07,810 --> 00:00:10,780
(Tae Gyun reads the rulebook again...)

2
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:13,690
(before they begin competing
as individuals.)

3
00:00:28,330 --> 00:00:29,830
We competed as a team,

4
00:00:29,830 --> 00:00:31,340
so we built a strong bond together.

5
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:33,240
So if people were to lie,

6
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:34,410
they'd worry...

7
00:00:34,410 --> 00:00:36,740
it would backfire on the team...

8
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:38,910
which made it hard for anyone to lie.

9
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:40,810
We couldn't act rashly...

10
00:00:40,810 --> 00:00:43,780
that would prevent us
from earning their trust.

11
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:46,550
But when we're competing as individuals,

12
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:49,250
we're more willing to lie
and betray others.

13
00:00:49,250 --> 00:00:50,860
We'll see more of that happening.

14
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:54,590
Sang Min set up the environment,
so that I could solely focus...

15
00:00:54,590 --> 00:00:55,890
on the games.

16
00:00:55,890 --> 00:00:57,430
Without Sang Min,

17
00:00:57,930 --> 00:00:59,930
I didn't know what to do.

18
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:03,540
(Last night)

19
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:04,770
So we're competing individually now?

20
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:05,940
Strictly?

21
00:01:06,070 --> 00:01:08,740
Then can I say something to the group?

22
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:10,580
Sure. Go ahead, Sang Min.

23
00:01:10,910 --> 00:01:12,980
I was a bit worried
that I might be putting...

24
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:15,010
my team in a difficult spot.

25
00:01:16,010 --> 00:01:17,080
Why?

26
00:01:19,620 --> 00:01:20,790
Well,

27
00:01:20,790 --> 00:01:22,090
I'm sorry about this.

28
00:01:24,790 --> 00:01:26,490
But something came up with my family.

29
00:01:26,490 --> 00:01:27,960
So I have no choice but to withdraw.

30
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:30,060
What? Why?

31
00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:31,260
- I...
- What?

32
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,500
I'm not allowed to answer phone calls,

33
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:38,040
but my manager must have called the staff.
And they must've talked to him.

34
00:01:38,170 --> 00:01:42,070
I must accompany my wife to the hospital.

35
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:46,410
To go into detail,

36
00:01:46,850 --> 00:01:47,910
my wife...

37
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:50,150
and I...

38
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:52,280
need to go to the hospital tomorrow.

39
00:02:10,870 --> 00:02:13,100
It happened so suddenly.

40
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:18,480
I feel bad for everyone
in the competition.

41
00:02:19,410 --> 00:02:21,150
But there's nothing I can do.

42
00:02:23,050 --> 00:02:24,320
My goal was...

43
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:26,450
to make it to the final.

44
00:02:26,450 --> 00:02:28,750
So I had cleared everything
on my schedule.

45
00:02:28,750 --> 00:02:30,760
I prepared myself to compete...

46
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:32,820
and did my best during the games too.

47
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:36,290
Something happened that made it
impossible for me to keep competing.

48
00:02:36,790 --> 00:02:39,460
It drove me crazy. Seriously.

49
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:41,730
I knew I could do better moving forward.

50
00:02:41,730 --> 00:02:43,330
I wanted to prove it to everyone.

51
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:46,070
It would've been great
if I had stayed a little longer.

52
00:02:46,570 --> 00:02:51,180
Actually, I got this chance
to compete again after 11 years.

53
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:56,280
I was scared and confused.

54
00:02:59,020 --> 00:03:00,420
I was flustered.

55
00:03:03,220 --> 00:03:05,290
Sang Min, you have a long way to go.

56
00:03:06,190 --> 00:03:08,130
I experienced a dopamine rush too.

57
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:15,500
- That was great. Well done.
- Sang Min.

58
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:17,470
- Well done.
- Great job.

59
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:21,170
I went through
a series of shocking moments...

60
00:03:21,170 --> 00:03:22,340
here.

61
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:25,610
What is this? Seriously.

62
00:03:28,310 --> 00:03:31,880
(He was the most passionate player.)

63
00:03:32,180 --> 00:03:35,320
Being here made me feel that I was...

64
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:36,720
alive.

65
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:39,720
I would've missed out on a big experience
if I hadn't come.

66
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:41,130
It was one of the best decisions...

67
00:03:41,330 --> 00:03:43,230
I ever made in my life.

68
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:45,130
I'm so glad I said yes to this.

69
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:47,630
This is where my journey ends
in this season.

70
00:03:47,630 --> 00:03:49,830
But this is just the beginning for me.

71
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:52,800
People said I was a toothless tiger.

72
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:54,240
They said all sorts of things about me.

73
00:03:54,740 --> 00:03:57,810
But I'll be a tiger, showing real teeth.

74
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:01,650
I'm really grateful...

75
00:04:01,650 --> 00:04:03,480
that I had this chance in my life...

76
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:05,050
to challenge myself on this show...

77
00:04:06,050 --> 00:04:07,490
because I could make...

78
00:04:07,490 --> 00:04:08,690
a difference during games.

79
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:13,490
It's not an easy decision
to leave the game midway.

80
00:04:13,890 --> 00:04:16,560
So this was something
he had no control over.

81
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:18,260
He must have given a lot of thought
before telling us.

82
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:20,530
I know that,
and I'm sure that was the case.

83
00:04:20,630 --> 00:04:23,430
I was just so happy to see him...

84
00:04:23,430 --> 00:04:25,400
on this show.

85
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:27,640
I'd love to keep seeing him if possible.

86
00:04:27,670 --> 00:04:29,710
I'm always rooting for Sang Min.

87
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:33,240
Sang Min, Keun Woo, and I...

88
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:35,210
shared a room together.

89
00:04:35,210 --> 00:04:37,120
We were like a family here.

90
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:39,680
He was the anchor of our team.

91
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:42,050
He played such a big role in our team.

92
00:04:42,290 --> 00:04:45,090
Losing Sang Min...

93
00:04:45,590 --> 00:04:46,990
out of the blue like this...

94
00:04:47,730 --> 00:04:50,060
made me incredibly sad.

95
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:51,630
It was so sad.

96
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:56,330
I was a bit worried...

97
00:04:56,430 --> 00:04:57,800
about the rest of the competition.

98
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:00,670
A lot of thoughts crossed my mind.

99
00:05:03,070 --> 00:05:05,980
I could sense that
his departure might weaken our team a bit.

100
00:05:06,210 --> 00:05:08,950
He brought stability to our team.

101
00:05:08,950 --> 00:05:10,820
We'll be competing individually,

102
00:05:10,820 --> 00:05:12,980
but the other teams might perceive us...

103
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:15,620
as easy targets because...

104
00:05:15,650 --> 00:05:17,190
our anchor is gone.

105
00:05:17,190 --> 00:05:19,420
I thought our team might crumble.

106
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:22,860
- I'm going now.
- Good work, Sang Min. Bye.

107
00:05:23,030 --> 00:05:24,130
Take care.

108
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:35,040
(Only 10 players remain now.)

109
00:05:36,610 --> 00:05:37,980
It got so empty all of a sudden.

110
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:39,010
Right.

111
00:05:39,010 --> 00:05:40,110
It got so empty.

112
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:47,590
(The morning
of the first individual competition)

113
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:55,760
How can I tell
if someone I've never met before is lying?

114
00:05:57,330 --> 00:06:00,360
I know the dispositions
of the players on my team.

115
00:06:00,530 --> 00:06:04,270
But I don't have a good understanding
of the players from other teams.

116
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:06,170
After hearing
that we were playing individually,

117
00:06:06,670 --> 00:06:08,570
I became more anxious.

118
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:16,810
(Another player is preparing
for the individual competition.)

119
00:06:16,810 --> 00:06:19,750
("Mensa Test")

120
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:21,520
This is too hard.

121
00:06:24,420 --> 00:06:25,890
I'm glad we're competing individually now.

122
00:06:27,460 --> 00:06:29,090
Why do you think
we'll be playing individually?

123
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:31,600
- We're still playing as a team.
- Stop lying.

124
00:06:31,830 --> 00:06:33,970
If you say
that we're playing individually again,

125
00:06:33,970 --> 00:06:35,330
I'll punish you.

126
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:36,770
We just switched...

127
00:06:36,770 --> 00:06:39,100
from playing as a team
to playing individually today.

128
00:06:39,140 --> 00:06:41,870
I thought it was better to play...

129
00:06:41,870 --> 00:06:44,510
with familiar players,
so we could buy some time...

130
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:46,680
while getting adjusted to the new system.

131
00:06:47,780 --> 00:06:50,620
Please gather in the main hall.

132
00:06:52,050 --> 00:06:54,250
- Hello.
- Good morning.

133
00:06:54,250 --> 00:06:55,720
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

134
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:56,890
- Hello.
- Good morning.

135
00:06:56,890 --> 00:06:58,120
- It's a great morning.
- Hello.

136
00:06:58,190 --> 00:06:59,560
- Good morning. Are you all right?
- Good morning.

137
00:07:00,190 --> 00:07:01,890
Good morning, everyone.

138
00:07:01,890 --> 00:07:03,030
Did you sleep well?

139
00:07:03,690 --> 00:07:05,230
Whom should we send home today?

140
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:07,570
Let's discuss it.

141
00:07:08,270 --> 00:07:09,700
- I...
- I'm wearing red today.

142
00:07:10,170 --> 00:07:12,200
It means there will be a bloodbath.

143
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:14,940
So half of us are gone now?

144
00:07:14,970 --> 00:07:16,670
- Half of us are gone. Exactly 10.
- So 10 people are gone?

145
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:18,810
- It's nice and spacious now.
- Right.

146
00:07:18,810 --> 00:07:21,350
- A part of me misses them too.
- Let's kick one of them out.

147
00:07:21,350 --> 00:07:22,350
Let's take over.

148
00:07:23,010 --> 00:07:24,280
Should I switch this out?

149
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:26,480
What if I end up with a question
I can't solve?

150
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:28,520
- That's always been the case for you.
- Exactly.

151
00:07:28,590 --> 00:07:29,590
- Today...
- What are you talking about?

152
00:07:29,590 --> 00:07:31,160
You're pointing out the obvious today.

153
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,460
Today, I can't...

154
00:07:32,460 --> 00:07:33,560
So far, I could rely on my team.

155
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:35,030
I'm on my own now.

156
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:39,130
You must now...

157
00:07:39,130 --> 00:07:42,270
split the team funds among yourselves.

158
00:07:43,170 --> 00:07:46,140
A representative from each team
will enter the Voting Room...

159
00:07:46,140 --> 00:07:48,410
and collect the fund registration slips.

160
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:53,510
(They will begin splitting up the funds
among themselves.)

161
00:07:53,510 --> 00:07:56,150
The funds will be rounded up
to the nearest thousand dollars.

162
00:07:56,150 --> 00:07:57,520
It will be rounded up?

163
00:07:57,820 --> 00:07:59,080
It will be rounded up
to the nearest thousand dollars?

164
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:01,250
- That's right.
- That's amazing.

165
00:08:01,250 --> 00:08:03,290
Your team currently has...

166
00:08:03,290 --> 00:08:05,190
a total of 360,000 dollars.

167
00:08:05,260 --> 00:08:08,390
- Submit the slips in the Voting Room.
- Okay.

168
00:08:08,390 --> 00:08:11,630
Your team currently has a total
of 60,000 dollars.

169
00:08:11,630 --> 00:08:15,100
Your team currently has a total
of 230,000 dollars.

170
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:17,640
(The remaining team funds:
Team P1: 230,000 dollars,)

171
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:20,140
(Team P3: 360,000 dollars,
Team R: 60,000 dollars)

172
00:08:20,140 --> 00:08:21,610
We have 60,000 dollars left.

173
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:24,240
- How come we don't have much money left?
- What?

174
00:08:24,510 --> 00:08:26,540
But the items we got yesterday...

175
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:27,850
Yesterday, we bought...

176
00:08:27,850 --> 00:08:29,950
- We bought a lot of items. Oh, right.
- Did we buy them?

177
00:08:29,950 --> 00:08:31,620
Didn't we buy all the items?

178
00:08:31,820 --> 00:08:32,850
We did.

179
00:08:32,850 --> 00:08:34,890
We didn't even get the funds from Team C.

180
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:36,320
We didn't.

181
00:08:36,350 --> 00:08:38,060
Gosh, they left before we could get it.

182
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:41,530
How much was the hidden item yesterday?

183
00:08:41,630 --> 00:08:43,330
- It was 20,000 dollars.
- It was 20,000 dollars?

184
00:08:43,330 --> 00:08:44,530
- Then we spent 30,000 dollars.
- We did?

185
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:47,030
My gosh, we were so stupid yesterday.

186
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:48,430
- Right.
- Why?

187
00:08:48,430 --> 00:08:50,870
We were working as an alliance,
but we bought everything.

188
00:08:50,870 --> 00:08:51,970
We never got the money from them.

189
00:08:51,970 --> 00:08:53,270
- You didn't?
- No.

190
00:08:53,270 --> 00:08:54,510
So you paid for everything.

191
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:56,470
But the other team had to go home.

192
00:08:56,610 --> 00:08:58,740
Just think
that you were paying for your survival.

193
00:08:59,140 --> 00:09:01,150
Should I consider it
as paying for their journey home?

194
00:09:01,950 --> 00:09:03,110
- Their journey home.
- But I was too generous.

195
00:09:03,110 --> 00:09:05,080
You guys wasted a lot of money
if you lost 30,000 dollars.

196
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:09,150
Since we have 60,000 dollars,
we'll each get 20,000 dollars.

197
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:10,820
Seung Yong can get some more from others.

198
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:11,920
- Seung Yong.
- Okay.

199
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:13,060
This is how much we have?

200
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:14,630
We have 360,000 dollars.

201
00:09:14,790 --> 00:09:17,900
We decided to split the money evenly
among ourselves.

202
00:09:21,900 --> 00:09:28,470
(The team funds have been split
into personal shares.)

203
00:09:28,470 --> 00:09:29,940
(Park Ji Min: 80,000 dollars,
Lee Tae Gyun: 80,000 dollars,)

204
00:09:29,940 --> 00:09:31,010
(Jeong Keun Woo: 70,000 dollars)

205
00:09:31,010 --> 00:09:32,380
(Hong Jin Ho: 90,000 dollars,
Xitsuh: 90,000 dollars,)

206
00:09:32,380 --> 00:09:33,740
(Choi Hye Seon: 90,000 dollars,
Heo Seong Beom: 90,000 dollars)

207
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:34,950
(Kwak Beom: 20,000 dollars,
Hyun Sung Joo: 20,000 dollars,)

208
00:09:34,950 --> 00:09:35,950
(Shin Seung Yong: 20,000 dollars)

209
00:09:36,380 --> 00:09:38,550
- I wonder how much money Team R has.
- What?

210
00:09:38,550 --> 00:09:40,150
I wonder how much money Team Rookie has.

211
00:09:40,450 --> 00:09:41,720
I bet they don't have much money.

212
00:09:41,790 --> 00:09:43,250
I don't even have 10,000 dollars.

213
00:09:43,550 --> 00:09:44,720
I see. Are you broke?

214
00:09:44,720 --> 00:09:46,060
Let me explain.

215
00:09:46,060 --> 00:09:48,760
We can't tell you how much we have.

216
00:09:49,030 --> 00:09:50,460
I guess they don't have a lot of money.

217
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,460
We can't tell you that.

218
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,700
- There's an announcement.
- What?

219
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:58,540
Starting today,
you will compete as individuals.

220
00:09:58,870 --> 00:10:01,210
- Yes.
- The number of surviving players...

221
00:10:01,670 --> 00:10:02,940
is...

222
00:10:02,940 --> 00:10:04,440
- twelve.
- What?

223
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:05,610
- What?
- There are ten of us.

224
00:10:05,610 --> 00:10:07,550
- I see.
- Darn it. They're outside.

225
00:10:07,550 --> 00:10:09,510
- I got goosebumps.
- Come on.

226
00:10:09,610 --> 00:10:12,880
Players who will participate
in the Money Challenge will enter now.

227
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:14,590
- Oh, my gosh.
- What is this?

228
00:10:14,690 --> 00:10:15,720
Who are they?

229
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:17,320
No way!

230
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:18,320
I got goosebumps!

231
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:19,960
- What?
- My gosh.

232
00:10:19,990 --> 00:10:21,130
- What?
- Hello.

233
00:10:21,590 --> 00:10:22,590
- My gosh.
- What's going on?

234
00:10:22,590 --> 00:10:23,590
- What?
- I'm here.

235
00:10:23,590 --> 00:10:25,430
- What is this?
- What happened?

236
00:10:49,690 --> 00:10:52,220
Team P2 is eliminated...

237
00:10:52,220 --> 00:10:53,790
from Bloody Game X.

238
00:10:54,430 --> 00:10:55,890
Everyone on Team P2...

239
00:10:55,890 --> 00:10:58,130
must leave the Bloody Mansion.

240
00:11:08,270 --> 00:11:10,240
Gosh, the weather is great today.

241
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:12,340
What was that?

242
00:11:12,340 --> 00:11:14,650
Your team lost the Deathmatch...

243
00:11:14,650 --> 00:11:16,010
and was eliminated.

244
00:11:16,610 --> 00:11:18,380
You must survive here...

245
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:20,480
until the next announcement.

246
00:11:21,390 --> 00:11:24,490
I gave up on trying to predict
what could happen on this show.

247
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:26,860
This is so typical
of the Bloody Game series.

248
00:11:26,860 --> 00:11:28,260
"Our time on the show is over."

249
00:11:28,990 --> 00:11:30,760
That's what we thought.

250
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:33,060
Then we suddenly got a second chance.

251
00:11:33,100 --> 00:11:34,430
I was so happy.

252
00:11:34,430 --> 00:11:37,330
Actually, I was really bummed out
that we got eliminated.

253
00:11:39,770 --> 00:11:43,270
Please gather in the game zone.

254
00:11:43,270 --> 00:11:45,210
Come on.

255
00:11:47,610 --> 00:11:48,650
- What's going on?
- Come on.

256
00:11:48,650 --> 00:11:50,550
They were eliminated a long time ago.

257
00:11:50,550 --> 00:11:51,580
But when I saw them there,

258
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:53,480
I realized it wasn't over yet.

259
00:11:53,550 --> 00:11:54,850
I was incredibly happy.

260
00:11:54,850 --> 00:11:55,990
I thought it was over.

261
00:11:55,990 --> 00:11:57,120
I was really sad about it.

262
00:11:57,150 --> 00:11:58,890
But I had another chance to get back.

263
00:12:00,860 --> 00:12:05,060
All of you have been eliminated
from Bloody Game X.

264
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:08,970
As of tomorrow,
all teams will be disbanded.

265
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:12,570
The Money Challenge will become
an individual competition.

266
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:15,070
Had I lasted one more day,

267
00:12:15,070 --> 00:12:18,110
I could have competed individually
against my chatty teammate.

268
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:19,340
The Revival Match...

269
00:12:19,340 --> 00:12:22,150
will begin now.

270
00:12:23,310 --> 00:12:26,250
You will compete individually
in the Revival Match.

271
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:30,250
Only the top two contenders will return
to the Bloody Mansion...

272
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:32,960
and participate
in tomorrow's Money Challenge.

273
00:12:33,090 --> 00:12:36,230
When I heard only 2 of the 7 players...

274
00:12:36,230 --> 00:12:38,500
could make it back to the game,

275
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:39,730
I thought that...

276
00:12:39,730 --> 00:12:41,570
I was doomed considering the probability.

277
00:12:41,770 --> 00:12:43,430
It was my last chance.

278
00:12:43,430 --> 00:12:46,340
I was determined to win no matter what
and return to the Bloody Mansion.

279
00:12:46,340 --> 00:12:49,170
The Revival Match will be revealed now.

280
00:12:49,870 --> 00:12:51,640
The Revival Match is called...

281
00:12:52,210 --> 00:12:54,040
(Memory Maze)

282
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:56,410
Memory Maze.

283
00:12:57,620 --> 00:12:58,780
In Memory Maze,

284
00:12:58,780 --> 00:13:01,390
you must memorize the game board
within the time limit...

285
00:13:01,390 --> 00:13:03,790
and look for the correct answers.

286
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:06,690
The game consists of five rounds.

287
00:13:06,790 --> 00:13:09,890
The game board consists
of columns A through E...

288
00:13:09,930 --> 00:13:11,960
and rows 1 through 5.

289
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:14,530
It's a 5 by 5 grid.

290
00:13:14,630 --> 00:13:16,100
At the start of the round,

291
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:18,140
the game board will be revealed
for three minutes.

292
00:13:18,140 --> 00:13:19,770
Once the time to memorize the board is up,

293
00:13:19,770 --> 00:13:22,710
fifteen questions will be presented
in order.

294
00:13:23,070 --> 00:13:24,880
Players must guess the answer...

295
00:13:24,880 --> 00:13:26,980
within five seconds
of pressing the buzzer.

296
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:30,880
An incorrect answer will forfeit
their turn to answer.

297
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:32,920
The player with the correct answer...

298
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:35,520
will be safe from elimination
in that round.

299
00:13:35,790 --> 00:13:38,590
The last player
without a correct answer...

300
00:13:38,590 --> 00:13:41,160
will be eliminated from the show.

301
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:44,830
The surviving players will move on
to the next round.

302
00:13:45,230 --> 00:13:48,130
Here are the movement rules
within the questions.

303
00:13:48,670 --> 00:13:51,200
If you land on an arrow box
after moving in the specified direction...

304
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:53,470
and by the given number of boxes,

305
00:13:53,470 --> 00:13:56,540
you must move one more box
in the indicated direction.

306
00:13:57,010 --> 00:13:58,480
When there are three players remaining,

307
00:13:58,480 --> 00:14:00,180
the final round will take place.

308
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:04,520
In the final round, two players
with the highest scores...

309
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:06,950
out of ten questions will advance.

310
00:14:07,850 --> 00:14:10,190
The Revival Match,

311
00:14:10,190 --> 00:14:12,520
Memory Maze, will begin shortly.

312
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:15,690
For this game, we have
to memorize the 5 by 5 grid...

313
00:14:15,690 --> 00:14:17,730
in order to answer the questions.

314
00:14:18,100 --> 00:14:20,560
I played a memorization game
when I was on "Elite League."

315
00:14:20,630 --> 00:14:21,930
I tried to memorize the whole thing,

316
00:14:22,330 --> 00:14:23,500
but I only ended up memorizing nothing.

317
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:25,070
For games
that require the use of the brain,

318
00:14:25,070 --> 00:14:26,940
even if you lose focus during the game,

319
00:14:26,940 --> 00:14:28,310
you can lock in again and move on.

320
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:29,770
For memorization games,

321
00:14:29,870 --> 00:14:31,180
even if you get yourself together,

322
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:32,740
you won't have anything left.

323
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:33,980
So...

324
00:14:33,980 --> 00:14:36,610
I would blow my chances
if I lose my focus even for a second.

325
00:14:36,610 --> 00:14:38,250
I experienced that on another show.

326
00:14:38,250 --> 00:14:39,520
I decided not to be ambitious.

327
00:14:39,620 --> 00:14:42,250
Instead, I decided to drill down
to memorizing only ten boxes.

328
00:14:43,020 --> 00:14:44,890
When I see questions
about the boxes I memorized,

329
00:14:44,890 --> 00:14:46,460
I'll answer them faster than anyone
and survive.

330
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:49,690
Kyoung Hoon was my biggest threat...

331
00:14:49,690 --> 00:14:51,960
because I knew
that he had a good memory...

332
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:53,800
from watching him on "The Genius."

333
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:56,600
Memory games are my strong suit.

334
00:14:56,930 --> 00:14:59,570
Even if I were
to go against all 20 players,

335
00:14:59,740 --> 00:15:02,940
not just these seven players,

336
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:04,410
no one could beat me.

337
00:15:05,640 --> 00:15:08,750
So it was a done deal that I'd advance.

338
00:15:10,350 --> 00:15:11,480
A memory game.

339
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:12,480
I'm not bad at it.

340
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:14,350
I must win and I can.

341
00:15:14,620 --> 00:15:17,120
Round One will begin.

342
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:18,960
The game board will be revealed.

343
00:15:25,330 --> 00:15:26,600
- Gosh.
- Goodness.

344
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:35,910
I'm used to memorizing just numbers.

345
00:15:35,910 --> 00:15:38,210
I've never memorized animals before.

346
00:15:38,210 --> 00:15:39,980
I didn't know how to go about it.

347
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:41,780
My strategy was memorizing ten boxes.

348
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:43,450
I gave up on memorizing
columns A through C.

349
00:15:43,450 --> 00:15:45,580
I made sure I memorized columns D and E.

350
00:15:45,650 --> 00:15:46,920
They were the last two columns.

351
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:49,050
I thought not that many people
would memorize them, so I chose them.

352
00:15:50,890 --> 00:15:52,790
I first memorized the locations
of the arrows.

353
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:55,160
It was easy to memorize the arrows.

354
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:57,330
The problem was memorizing the animals.

355
00:15:57,590 --> 00:15:58,900
I memorized the first syllables...

356
00:15:58,900 --> 00:16:00,630
starting with the top row.
Lion, rabbit, and bear.

357
00:16:00,860 --> 00:16:02,570
That's how I memorize the board.

358
00:16:07,740 --> 00:16:10,170
The game board will be revealed
for one more minute.

359
00:16:11,280 --> 00:16:14,350
Memorizing by association
is the easiest way.

360
00:16:14,580 --> 00:16:16,750
Let me take the first row for example.

361
00:16:16,780 --> 00:16:18,750
A lion was on a hopping toy.

362
00:16:18,750 --> 00:16:20,120
And rabbits also hop.

363
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:21,520
They were playing together.

364
00:16:21,520 --> 00:16:23,290
Then a bear showed up. And they ran away.

365
00:16:23,290 --> 00:16:25,320
I made a story with the keywords.

366
00:16:25,560 --> 00:16:27,760
It doesn't take much time...

367
00:16:27,760 --> 00:16:29,530
to come up with these stories.

368
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:32,230
It would be very easy to memorize
all five rows with this method.

369
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:37,770
You have 30 seconds left.

370
00:16:45,910 --> 00:16:48,110
You have ten seconds left.

371
00:16:56,590 --> 00:16:58,590
Your time with the board is up.

372
00:16:59,260 --> 00:17:01,630
Here's the first question.

373
00:17:01,990 --> 00:17:05,230
(Start from the lion,
move one box to the right,)

374
00:17:05,230 --> 00:17:06,730
(and move one box up.)

375
00:17:06,730 --> 00:17:13,100
(Start from the lion,
move one box to the right,)

376
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:18,610
(and move one box up.)

377
00:17:22,350 --> 00:17:23,510
A hedgehog.

378
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:29,750
YunB.

379
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:31,320
That's correct.

380
00:17:31,390 --> 00:17:33,460
You have survived this round.

381
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:35,090
Please turn around.

382
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:41,500
I watched YunB play in his season,

383
00:17:41,500 --> 00:17:44,070
so I knew he didn't have a good memory.

384
00:17:44,070 --> 00:17:45,500
He probably got lucky this time.

385
00:17:45,840 --> 00:17:47,640
Honestly, I was really surprised.

386
00:17:47,740 --> 00:17:50,570
I knew some people would be faster
than me.

387
00:17:50,570 --> 00:17:52,540
But I didn't think that would be YunB.

388
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:56,710
It's a short-term memory game.

389
00:17:56,810 --> 00:17:58,950
You shouldn't try to memorize everything.

390
00:17:59,180 --> 00:18:02,450
You have to memorize the key locations
of the board.

391
00:18:02,450 --> 00:18:03,990
A right arrow, an up arrow, and a lion.

392
00:18:03,990 --> 00:18:06,220
I repeated this combo in my head
ten times.

393
00:18:06,220 --> 00:18:09,260
Then I memorized these 3-box combos
10 times in my head.

394
00:18:09,260 --> 00:18:11,800
When I focused
on memorizing these patterns,

395
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:14,000
I ended up memorizing the corners.

396
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,270
Then I just need to know
what was in the center.

397
00:18:16,270 --> 00:18:18,640
That could be a reference point.

398
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,840
(YunB survives Round 1.)

399
00:18:20,840 --> 00:18:23,110
Here's the second question.

400
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:25,010
(Start from the monkey,
move one box to the right,)

401
00:18:25,010 --> 00:18:26,240
(and move one box down.)

402
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,480
(The correct answer is a tiger.)

403
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:30,580
A pig.

404
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:33,180
Kang Ji Hoo, that's incorrect.

405
00:18:33,180 --> 00:18:36,790
You can no longer submit your answer
for this question.

406
00:18:37,150 --> 00:18:39,060
If I were to make a random guess...

407
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:40,320
before the player who knows the answer,

408
00:18:40,320 --> 00:18:41,630
I could get lucky and get it right.

409
00:18:41,630 --> 00:18:43,860
So when it was about the area
I didn't memorize,

410
00:18:43,860 --> 00:18:45,900
I gave up immediately
and pressed the buzzer fast...

411
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:47,030
to make a random guess.

412
00:18:47,030 --> 00:18:50,030
Then I would go over whatever I memorized
for the next question.

413
00:18:50,230 --> 00:18:53,400
I tried to remember what I memorized
in the remaining time.

414
00:18:58,010 --> 00:18:59,140
A tiger.

415
00:18:59,410 --> 00:19:01,710
Kim Kyoung Hoon, that's correct.

416
00:19:01,950 --> 00:19:04,820
Kim Kyoung Hoon,
you have survived this round.

417
00:19:04,820 --> 00:19:05,920
That's correct.

418
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:07,350
It was a tiger.

419
00:19:07,920 --> 00:19:10,320
I just don't want to be the first one
to get eliminated.

420
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:12,390
With two players advancing
to the next round,

421
00:19:12,390 --> 00:19:14,690
that's when I began to get really anxious.

422
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:16,760
Here's the next question.

423
00:19:16,930 --> 00:19:18,930
(Start from the penguin, move one box up,)

424
00:19:18,930 --> 00:19:20,430
(move one box to the right.)

425
00:19:20,430 --> 00:19:21,670
(Start from the penguin, move one box up,)

426
00:19:21,670 --> 00:19:22,930
(move one box to the right.)

427
00:19:22,930 --> 00:19:24,070
Kim You Hyun.

428
00:19:24,070 --> 00:19:25,100
A tiger.

429
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:26,470
That's correct.

430
00:19:26,470 --> 00:19:29,110
Kim You Hyun,
you have survived this round.

431
00:19:31,510 --> 00:19:33,280
Here's the next question.

432
00:19:33,510 --> 00:19:34,710
(Start from the cat,
move one box to the left,)

433
00:19:34,710 --> 00:19:35,780
(and move one box up.)

434
00:19:35,780 --> 00:19:39,450
(Start from the cat,
move one box to the left,)

435
00:19:39,450 --> 00:19:41,290
(and move one box up.)

436
00:19:41,290 --> 00:19:42,320
Kang Ji Hoo.

437
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:43,350
A sheep.

438
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:44,820
That's correct.

439
00:19:44,920 --> 00:19:47,620
Kang Ji Hoo, you have survived this round.

440
00:19:49,030 --> 00:19:50,360
I was 1 of the last 3.

441
00:19:50,360 --> 00:19:52,100
I had a 33 percent chance
of moving forward.

442
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,770
Here's the next question.

443
00:19:54,770 --> 00:19:56,100
(3 players remain now.)

444
00:19:56,130 --> 00:19:59,240
(Start from the snake,
move one box to the left,)

445
00:19:59,240 --> 00:20:01,370
(and move one box up.)

446
00:20:01,370 --> 00:20:02,470
Lee Jin Hyeong.

447
00:20:02,470 --> 00:20:03,610
A pig.

448
00:20:04,070 --> 00:20:05,240
That's incorrect.

449
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:08,710
You can no longer submit your answer
for this question.

450
00:20:10,610 --> 00:20:11,620
Kim Nam Hee.

451
00:20:11,620 --> 00:20:12,780
The answer is a rabbit.

452
00:20:13,150 --> 00:20:14,250
That's correct.

453
00:20:14,250 --> 00:20:17,050
Kim Nam Hee, you have survived this round.

454
00:20:17,190 --> 00:20:19,760
Kim Nam Hee, please turn around.

455
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:24,860
"Is this the result
of spending one more day out here?"

456
00:20:26,230 --> 00:20:29,170
The anxiety and pressure were just insane.

457
00:20:29,270 --> 00:20:32,370
It felt like the water came up to my neck.

458
00:20:35,870 --> 00:20:37,840
When players from Team C moved on
with the correct answer,

459
00:20:38,210 --> 00:20:39,480
I was praying for Jin Hyeong.

460
00:20:39,480 --> 00:20:40,580
"Jin Hyeong, please get it right already."

461
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:42,110
I was praying.

462
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:45,150
"It can't be one of us
that gets eliminated."

463
00:20:45,750 --> 00:20:47,020
Then...

464
00:20:48,490 --> 00:20:50,750
Gosh, what a twist of fate.

465
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:54,020
Jin Hyeong and I were
the last two players.

466
00:20:54,390 --> 00:20:56,160
Here's the next question.

467
00:20:57,290 --> 00:21:02,670
(Start from the chicken, move one box up,
and move one box to the left.)

468
00:21:02,670 --> 00:21:06,640
(Start from the chicken, move one box up,
and move one box to the left.)

469
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:07,700
Lee Jin Hyeong.

470
00:21:07,700 --> 00:21:08,840
A rabbit.

471
00:21:09,570 --> 00:21:10,640
That's incorrect.

472
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:14,010
Lee Jin Hyeong, you can no longer submit
your answer for this question.

473
00:21:14,010 --> 00:21:15,180
(Lee Jin Hyeong gets it wrong.)

474
00:21:28,730 --> 00:21:30,060
If you have the answer, go for it.

475
00:21:30,330 --> 00:21:32,400
Actually, I knew what he was doing.

476
00:21:32,430 --> 00:21:33,930
He knew the answer,

477
00:21:33,930 --> 00:21:35,130
but he didn't answer it for my sake.

478
00:21:35,130 --> 00:21:36,700
I could sense it.

479
00:21:38,600 --> 00:21:40,000
The question was presented.

480
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:42,310
And I knew the answer.

481
00:21:43,410 --> 00:21:45,780
I wanted him to answer it before me.

482
00:21:46,340 --> 00:21:48,150
Your time is up.

483
00:21:48,150 --> 00:21:49,580
Ha Seung Jin, you can no longer...

484
00:21:49,580 --> 00:21:51,620
- submit your answer for this question.
- Gosh, I was thinking.

485
00:21:51,620 --> 00:21:52,680
(Seung Jin didn't answer the question
on purpose.)

486
00:21:52,750 --> 00:21:54,080
I was looking out for him.

487
00:21:54,080 --> 00:21:56,120
Not answering the question
when I knew the answer...

488
00:21:56,190 --> 00:21:58,290
could hurt Jin Hyeong's pride.

489
00:21:58,460 --> 00:22:00,490
I didn't want to survive like that.

490
00:22:00,490 --> 00:22:01,790
If Seung Jin knew the answer,

491
00:22:01,790 --> 00:22:03,230
he should have answered it.

492
00:22:03,230 --> 00:22:05,560
No one presented a correct answer
for this question.

493
00:22:05,700 --> 00:22:07,660
We'll move on to the next question.

494
00:22:09,070 --> 00:22:10,270
Lee Jin Hyeong.

495
00:22:10,270 --> 00:22:11,440
Ha Seung Jin.

496
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:14,270
The eliminated player from Round One...

497
00:22:15,840 --> 00:22:17,470
is Lee Jin Hyeong.

498
00:22:17,510 --> 00:22:21,410
You can never return to Bloody Game X.

499
00:22:21,510 --> 00:22:24,150
Please leave immediately.

500
00:22:28,050 --> 00:22:29,150
My gosh.

501
00:22:29,320 --> 00:22:31,560
Honestly, I didn't see this coming.

502
00:22:31,590 --> 00:22:33,690
Jin Hyeong was really good
at memory games.

503
00:22:33,690 --> 00:22:35,360
I thought he had a better memory than me.

504
00:22:35,360 --> 00:22:37,460
Watching him get eliminated
in Round One...

505
00:22:37,460 --> 00:22:39,100
made me think anything could happen here.

506
00:22:39,300 --> 00:22:41,000
Other players did better than me.

507
00:22:41,830 --> 00:22:44,170
I deserved to be eliminated...

508
00:22:44,170 --> 00:22:45,300
based on my performance today.

509
00:22:45,670 --> 00:22:46,900
That's why...

510
00:22:46,900 --> 00:22:49,670
I'm a bit more relieved
that I got eliminated as an individual.

511
00:22:49,670 --> 00:22:52,880
I can leave the show without any regret
or lingering disappointment.

512
00:22:53,710 --> 00:22:56,210
Round Two will begin now.

513
00:22:56,380 --> 00:22:58,120
The game board will be revealed.

514
00:22:58,580 --> 00:23:00,120
(Fire truck, bicycle, bus, boat,
train, motorcycle, taxi,)

515
00:23:00,120 --> 00:23:01,620
(airplane, truck, subway, cruise,
kickboard, police car, helicopter,)

516
00:23:01,620 --> 00:23:02,620
(ambulance, cargo truck, yacht, tram)

517
00:23:02,620 --> 00:23:07,160
(Fire truck, bicycle, bus, boat,
train, motorcycle, taxi,)

518
00:23:07,160 --> 00:23:11,530
(airplane, truck, subway, cruise,
kickboard, police car, helicopter,)

519
00:23:11,530 --> 00:23:14,530
(ambulance, cargo truck, yacht, tram)

520
00:23:14,530 --> 00:23:16,370
Your time with the board is up.

521
00:23:16,370 --> 00:23:18,400
Here's the first question.

522
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:20,100
(Start from the fire truck,
move one box to the right,)

523
00:23:20,100 --> 00:23:21,200
(and move one box down.)

524
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:22,370
Kim Kyoung Hoon.

525
00:23:23,970 --> 00:23:25,040
Train.

526
00:23:25,310 --> 00:23:26,410
That's correct.

527
00:23:26,410 --> 00:23:28,950
Kim Kyoung Hoon,
you have survived this round.

528
00:23:29,780 --> 00:23:31,450
Here's the next question.

529
00:23:31,450 --> 00:23:33,380
(Start from the cruise,
move one box to the left,)

530
00:23:33,380 --> 00:23:34,520
(and move one box up.)

531
00:23:34,520 --> 00:23:35,550
A motorcycle.

532
00:23:35,550 --> 00:23:37,320
Kang Ji Hoo, that's correct.

533
00:23:37,320 --> 00:23:39,060
Here's the next question.

534
00:23:39,620 --> 00:23:41,260
(Start from the yacht, move one box up,
and move one box to the left.)

535
00:23:41,260 --> 00:23:42,290
A police car.

536
00:23:42,290 --> 00:23:44,160
YunB, that's correct.

537
00:23:44,460 --> 00:23:45,630
That's correct.

538
00:23:45,630 --> 00:23:48,030
Kim Nam Hee, you have survived this round.

539
00:23:48,030 --> 00:23:49,600
Here's the next question.

540
00:23:49,830 --> 00:23:54,000
(How many watercraft options are
on the board?)

541
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,240
Ha Seung Jin.

542
00:23:55,940 --> 00:23:57,010
Three.

543
00:23:58,980 --> 00:24:00,240
That's correct.

544
00:24:00,340 --> 00:24:03,180
The eliminated player from Round Two
is Kim You Hyun.

545
00:24:03,410 --> 00:24:07,320
Kim You Hyun,
you can never return to Bloody Game X.

546
00:24:07,680 --> 00:24:10,390
I never imagined that You Hyun
would get eliminated this early on.

547
00:24:14,590 --> 00:24:16,990
Round Three will begin now.

548
00:24:18,130 --> 00:24:20,130
Kim Kyoung Hoon, that's correct.

549
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:22,870
Kim Nam Hee, that's correct.

550
00:24:23,370 --> 00:24:25,270
Kang Ji Hoo. YunB.

551
00:24:25,270 --> 00:24:26,300
That's correct.

552
00:24:26,300 --> 00:24:29,840
The eliminated player of Round Three
is Ha Seung Jin.

553
00:24:30,110 --> 00:24:32,910
The eliminated player of Round Four
is Kim Nam Hee.

554
00:24:33,340 --> 00:24:36,050
The final round will begin now.

555
00:24:45,890 --> 00:24:48,690
The Revival Match has ended.

556
00:24:51,390 --> 00:24:54,660
Players who will participate
in the Money Challenge will enter now.

557
00:24:54,660 --> 00:24:56,430
- Oh, my gosh.
- What is this?

558
00:24:58,340 --> 00:24:59,770
No way!

559
00:25:00,700 --> 00:25:02,170
- What is this?
- I got goosebumps!

560
00:25:05,840 --> 00:25:07,010
- What?
- Gosh.

561
00:25:07,010 --> 00:25:08,110
Yes, sir.

562
00:25:08,140 --> 00:25:09,350
What happened?

563
00:25:10,110 --> 00:25:11,720
- Nice to see you again.
- What happened?

564
00:25:12,250 --> 00:25:13,320
We had the Revival Match.

565
00:25:13,620 --> 00:25:15,090
- The Revival Match?
- Hey, cutie.

566
00:25:15,090 --> 00:25:16,850
Everyone was surprised to see us.

567
00:25:16,850 --> 00:25:19,260
Seong Beom and Xitsuh...

568
00:25:19,520 --> 00:25:21,520
Their faces turned sour for a second.

569
00:25:21,520 --> 00:25:22,560
Then they pretended to be okay.

570
00:25:22,560 --> 00:25:24,030
They said they were happy that I was back.

571
00:25:24,190 --> 00:25:26,000
"After everything we did
to get rid of him,"

572
00:25:26,060 --> 00:25:29,370
"he came back like a cockroach."
That was the vibe I got.

573
00:25:29,370 --> 00:25:30,470
I'm glad you're back.

574
00:25:30,470 --> 00:25:31,800
My gosh, I'm happy for you.

575
00:25:31,800 --> 00:25:33,640
- Congratulations.
- How did you come back?

576
00:25:33,700 --> 00:25:35,670
Ji Hoo is my junior alumnus.

577
00:25:35,670 --> 00:25:37,670
We have a lot in common.

578
00:25:37,670 --> 00:25:40,480
You'd think that we would have a chance
to play on the same side.

579
00:25:40,480 --> 00:25:42,350
But we never had that chance.

580
00:25:42,350 --> 00:25:44,550
I was sad about that.

581
00:25:44,710 --> 00:25:45,820
Actually, not really.

582
00:25:45,820 --> 00:25:47,350
I never wanted to play with him,
from the beginning.

583
00:25:48,050 --> 00:25:49,790
It was Ji Hoo.

584
00:25:49,850 --> 00:25:51,690
"So Ji Hoo is back."

585
00:25:51,760 --> 00:25:53,820
Welcome back. I'm glad you're back.

586
00:25:53,820 --> 00:25:54,960
- Ji Hoo.
- Yes?

587
00:25:55,530 --> 00:25:56,860
As for Ji Hoo,

588
00:25:56,860 --> 00:25:59,200
I noticed several times that...

589
00:25:59,200 --> 00:26:02,030
he wanted to show off his intelligence
throughout the games.

590
00:26:02,030 --> 00:26:05,700
It would be difficult
to team up with Ji Hoo.

591
00:26:05,840 --> 00:26:07,270
So I wasn't thrilled.

592
00:26:07,840 --> 00:26:09,370
Gosh, I got goosebumps.

593
00:26:09,670 --> 00:26:10,740
That couldn't have been easy.

594
00:26:10,810 --> 00:26:12,280
He's such a snake.

595
00:26:12,340 --> 00:26:14,040
I never thought...

596
00:26:14,040 --> 00:26:15,450
he would crawl back in like a cockroach.

597
00:26:15,450 --> 00:26:18,780
YunB keeps on coming back
no matter how many times we crush him.

598
00:26:18,880 --> 00:26:20,550
What do we need to do to get rid of him
for good?

599
00:26:22,690 --> 00:26:24,320
It's crazy that YunB made it back.

600
00:26:24,350 --> 00:26:26,660
Gosh, it's been a while since I saw him.

601
00:26:28,430 --> 00:26:30,330
I don't underestimate YunB.

602
00:26:30,360 --> 00:26:32,560
It looks like he's always fooling around.

603
00:26:32,560 --> 00:26:34,860
He acts like he's a loose cannon.

604
00:26:34,860 --> 00:26:36,400
But once we start playing,

605
00:26:36,400 --> 00:26:38,030
he understands the games quite well.

606
00:26:38,030 --> 00:26:39,500
YunB made it back.

607
00:26:39,640 --> 00:26:40,800
This is good news for me.

608
00:26:40,800 --> 00:26:42,640
He's like my forever ally.

609
00:26:42,710 --> 00:26:44,070
Where have you been?

610
00:26:44,070 --> 00:26:45,510
- It was quite tough out there.
- Hey.

611
00:26:45,510 --> 00:26:46,880
What a cool way to come back.

612
00:26:47,580 --> 00:26:48,650
Did you win the game?

613
00:26:49,310 --> 00:26:50,480
Gosh, YunB.

614
00:26:50,480 --> 00:26:54,220
It felt like I came back from the dead
with a brand-new life.

615
00:26:54,280 --> 00:26:55,850
Now that I'm back,

616
00:26:55,950 --> 00:26:57,790
I will be ruthless.

617
00:26:57,850 --> 00:27:00,060
Forget about not burning bridges.

618
00:27:00,060 --> 00:27:01,320
I don't need excuses to play nice.

619
00:27:01,320 --> 00:27:04,260
I was the entertainer of the group
before I left.

620
00:27:04,260 --> 00:27:05,830
There's no more of that now.

621
00:27:05,830 --> 00:27:07,930
I'll use every means possible...

622
00:27:08,060 --> 00:27:09,270
to come out...

623
00:27:09,270 --> 00:27:10,570
on top.

624
00:27:11,070 --> 00:27:13,740
My team, Team C, was...

625
00:27:13,770 --> 00:27:15,870
wiped out by Team P1 and Team P3.

626
00:27:16,140 --> 00:27:17,540
It was a total annihilation.

627
00:27:17,540 --> 00:27:19,910
They thought I was gone with my team.

628
00:27:19,910 --> 00:27:21,540
It felt like my mother...

629
00:27:21,540 --> 00:27:23,210
had put me, her youngest son, on a leaf...

630
00:27:23,210 --> 00:27:26,220
and pushed me out on the river,

631
00:27:26,220 --> 00:27:28,180
so I could make it back here.
That's how I felt.

632
00:27:28,350 --> 00:27:30,250
I'm the only one...

633
00:27:30,250 --> 00:27:32,660
who can take revenge for my team.

634
00:27:33,360 --> 00:27:35,260
There are people who don't like me.

635
00:27:35,490 --> 00:27:37,160
Some people wanted to get rid of me.

636
00:27:37,160 --> 00:27:39,660
I'll beat them all and win no matter what.

637
00:27:44,470 --> 00:27:45,500
- I heard about the ambush.
- Hey.

638
00:27:45,500 --> 00:27:46,840
You should've been here during the heist.

639
00:27:46,840 --> 00:27:48,100
- Yes.
- You should've been here for it.

640
00:27:48,100 --> 00:27:49,140
Seung Jin should've been here.

641
00:27:49,140 --> 00:27:50,740
Right. You and Seung Jin
should've been here for it.

642
00:27:50,740 --> 00:27:53,740
It would've been crazy
if YunB had been here that day.

643
00:27:53,740 --> 00:27:56,280
We couldn't have won
if they had had Seung Jin and YunB.

644
00:27:57,280 --> 00:27:58,650
Before explaining the rules of the game,

645
00:27:58,650 --> 00:28:01,450
the benefits of the Money Challenge
for the winners will be revealed first.

646
00:28:01,450 --> 00:28:02,590
Benefits? Oh, for this Money Challenge?

647
00:28:02,590 --> 00:28:03,990
Today's Money Challenge...

648
00:28:04,120 --> 00:28:06,590
may have multiple winners.

649
00:28:07,090 --> 00:28:09,060
The winners of the Money Challenge...

650
00:28:09,060 --> 00:28:12,000
will receive 20,000 dollars each...

651
00:28:12,130 --> 00:28:14,200
and will not face elimination.

652
00:28:16,030 --> 00:28:17,770
Today's Money Challenge is...

653
00:28:17,770 --> 00:28:19,140
(Today's Money Challenge)

654
00:28:19,400 --> 00:28:21,000
(Killer Game)

655
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:23,640
It's Killer Game.

656
00:28:24,540 --> 00:28:25,640
"Killer Game?"

657
00:28:25,640 --> 00:28:27,210
It's the Mafia Game. I'm sure of it.

658
00:28:27,210 --> 00:28:28,240
Is it Lee Jin Hyeong Game?

659
00:28:28,240 --> 00:28:29,680
- Yes, it is.
- Definitely.

660
00:28:29,950 --> 00:28:31,150
That's a fun name.

661
00:28:31,850 --> 00:28:32,980
Killer Game will be...

662
00:28:32,980 --> 00:28:35,250
a 12-player individual competition,

663
00:28:36,220 --> 00:28:39,020
and it's a social deduction game
based on the mechanics of Mafia Game.

664
00:28:40,420 --> 00:28:43,860
There's a killer,
targeting the players in the game.

665
00:28:43,990 --> 00:28:47,430
Players must survive
the killer's attacks...

666
00:28:47,430 --> 00:28:49,430
through Night and Day Phases
in every round...

667
00:28:49,430 --> 00:28:52,070
while fulfilling their own win conditions.

668
00:28:52,670 --> 00:28:54,840
During the Day Phase,
players will confirm the casualties.

669
00:28:54,840 --> 00:28:56,670
Then they will have
a 30-minute discussion.

670
00:28:56,670 --> 00:28:59,240
During this time,
they can use their abilities or use items.

671
00:28:59,910 --> 00:29:02,010
During the Night Phase,
players will choose...

672
00:29:02,010 --> 00:29:05,250
one of the two randomly drawn cards...

673
00:29:05,250 --> 00:29:06,720
and enter the chosen room.

674
00:29:06,720 --> 00:29:07,720
(Prison)

675
00:29:07,950 --> 00:29:10,650
But they cannot find out
who else was in the room...

676
00:29:10,650 --> 00:29:11,890
with them.

677
00:29:12,520 --> 00:29:15,020
Once all players finish picking a room...

678
00:29:15,090 --> 00:29:18,360
and if a player shares the room
only with the killer,

679
00:29:18,460 --> 00:29:21,500
the player will be murdered by the killer.

680
00:29:21,500 --> 00:29:22,730
(Night Phase)

681
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:26,100
If the killer successfully murders
3 players within 10 rounds,

682
00:29:26,100 --> 00:29:27,670
the final vote will take place.

683
00:29:30,010 --> 00:29:32,340
The citizen faction wins
if they single out the killer.

684
00:29:33,540 --> 00:29:34,780
If they fail,

685
00:29:34,780 --> 00:29:36,710
the killer faction wins.

686
00:29:37,710 --> 00:29:41,250
Players will be assigned
to 1 of the 3 factions.

687
00:29:41,280 --> 00:29:42,990
Killer, citizen, and neutral.

688
00:29:43,520 --> 00:29:46,190
The killer must murder 3 players
within 10 rounds...

689
00:29:46,290 --> 00:29:48,490
and shouldn't be singled out
in the final vote.

690
00:29:48,730 --> 00:29:51,390
The killer can freely pick the room
to enter during the night.

691
00:29:51,490 --> 00:29:54,800
But the killer can't stay in the same room
from the previous round.

692
00:29:55,670 --> 00:29:58,200
A follower is the killer's assistant.

693
00:29:58,500 --> 00:30:01,740
The follower remains safe from attacks
when left alone with the killer at night.

694
00:30:01,840 --> 00:30:05,010
The follower must help the killer win
even at the expense of their own life.

695
00:30:05,740 --> 00:30:08,710
A dirty cop is the killer's accomplice.

696
00:30:09,110 --> 00:30:11,380
Like the follower, the dirty cop
remains safe from the killer.

697
00:30:11,410 --> 00:30:13,580
During the day,
the dirty cop can arrest a player...

698
00:30:13,580 --> 00:30:16,820
and remove a player
that may cause trouble for them.

699
00:30:17,250 --> 00:30:19,320
However,
when the dirty cop arrests a player,

700
00:30:19,320 --> 00:30:22,830
the dirty cop will also be excluded
from the game with the player.

701
00:30:23,560 --> 00:30:26,330
A cop can defend the killer's attacks...

702
00:30:26,330 --> 00:30:28,700
and will find out about the attacks.

703
00:30:28,930 --> 00:30:31,830
Arresting the killer during the day...

704
00:30:31,830 --> 00:30:35,310
immediately ends the game and results
in a victory for the citizen faction.

705
00:30:35,440 --> 00:30:37,910
However, if the cop makes a wrong arrest,

706
00:30:37,910 --> 00:30:41,780
they will be excluded from the game
along with the wrongly arrested player.

707
00:30:42,210 --> 00:30:43,810
A prison guard...

708
00:30:43,810 --> 00:30:46,180
can lock up one player
in prison every round.

709
00:30:46,580 --> 00:30:49,850
The imprisoned player can't pick a room
during the night.

710
00:30:49,850 --> 00:30:51,990
Their abilities will be locked.

711
00:30:52,260 --> 00:30:55,330
However, back-to-back imprisonment
for the same player...

712
00:30:55,330 --> 00:30:57,230
isn't allowed.

713
00:30:57,860 --> 00:31:00,300
Every time there's a murder,
a forensic doctor receives...

714
00:31:00,300 --> 00:31:01,900
a chance to investigate a clue.

715
00:31:01,900 --> 00:31:04,330
The forensic doctor can check
if a certain player is the killer...

716
00:31:04,330 --> 00:31:06,640
and obtain a crucial hint.

717
00:31:06,970 --> 00:31:09,470
However, the investigation result
will be revealed in the following round...

718
00:31:09,470 --> 00:31:11,440
after their ability is used.

719
00:31:11,840 --> 00:31:14,780
A psychic can figure out
how many players...

720
00:31:14,780 --> 00:31:16,810
were in their room last night.

721
00:31:16,810 --> 00:31:19,450
They can provide critical information
about players' movements.

722
00:31:20,350 --> 00:31:23,150
A witness can figure out
the exact location of the murder...

723
00:31:23,150 --> 00:31:24,450
when the murder takes place...

724
00:31:24,450 --> 00:31:27,090
in the next room by the victim's scream.

725
00:31:27,720 --> 00:31:30,530
A citizen doesn't have
any special abilities.

726
00:31:30,530 --> 00:31:32,400
Through sheer deduction
and strategic voting,

727
00:31:32,400 --> 00:31:34,230
they must track down the killer.

728
00:31:35,160 --> 00:31:36,900
A psychopath wins...

729
00:31:36,900 --> 00:31:38,740
if the killer murders three players.

730
00:31:39,040 --> 00:31:41,800
Even if the killer gets arrested
through the vote,

731
00:31:41,800 --> 00:31:43,710
the psychopath wins.

732
00:31:44,610 --> 00:31:47,180
A pickpocket can freely choose a room.

733
00:31:47,180 --> 00:31:49,210
When they're left alone
with another player,

734
00:31:49,210 --> 00:31:50,680
they can successfully steal
from the player.

735
00:31:51,150 --> 00:31:53,280
If a pickpocket survives
after stealing three times,

736
00:31:53,280 --> 00:31:54,450
the pickpocket wins.

737
00:31:55,180 --> 00:31:57,320
Before Round Five concludes,

738
00:31:57,320 --> 00:31:59,820
a gambler must predict the winning faction
and place their bet.

739
00:32:00,220 --> 00:32:01,820
If the chosen faction wins...

740
00:32:01,820 --> 00:32:04,030
and the gambler survives,
the gambler wins.

741
00:32:04,990 --> 00:32:07,260
All players excluding the follower...

742
00:32:07,260 --> 00:32:09,000
will lose the game...

743
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:11,200
once they're murdered even if
they have fulfilled their win conditions.

744
00:32:12,340 --> 00:32:15,470
There are three items in Killer Game.

745
00:32:15,710 --> 00:32:18,610
The first item is
the room selection ticket.

746
00:32:18,740 --> 00:32:21,980
Players can choose the room they want
during the Night Phase.

747
00:32:22,950 --> 00:32:25,180
The second item is
the get-out-of-jail card.

748
00:32:25,480 --> 00:32:28,080
Using this card grants immediate release
from prison.

749
00:32:28,450 --> 00:32:30,590
The third item is a hidden item.

750
00:32:30,750 --> 00:32:33,920
The hidden item will be revealed
before Round Six begins.

751
00:32:35,160 --> 00:32:38,960
Players can buy the items
during the Day Phase in the Voting Room.

752
00:32:39,700 --> 00:32:41,760
As for YunB and Kang Ji Hoo...

753
00:32:41,760 --> 00:32:44,670
who returned after the Revival Match,

754
00:32:44,670 --> 00:32:46,370
since their team funds are gone,

755
00:32:46,370 --> 00:32:48,500
they won't have any personal funds.

756
00:32:50,470 --> 00:32:52,540
Killer Game is very similar...

757
00:32:52,540 --> 00:32:55,210
to Mafia Game
which everyone is familiar with.

758
00:32:55,210 --> 00:32:57,710
But Killer Game goes one step further.

759
00:32:57,850 --> 00:32:59,950
There are a lot of occupations.

760
00:33:00,080 --> 00:33:01,720
There's a neutral faction too.

761
00:33:01,720 --> 00:33:03,790
Each occupation comes
with a special ability.

762
00:33:03,790 --> 00:33:05,860
I thought Killer Game was...

763
00:33:05,860 --> 00:33:09,760
a refined version of Mafia Game
after many iterations.

764
00:33:09,830 --> 00:33:11,960
I don't know about my winning rate,

765
00:33:11,960 --> 00:33:15,160
but I enjoy games like this.

766
00:33:15,300 --> 00:33:18,100
I have a bad memory about Mafia Game.

767
00:33:18,100 --> 00:33:21,170
I ended up losing Mafia Game
in my previous season.

768
00:33:21,170 --> 00:33:23,870
And I cried a lot that day.

769
00:33:24,470 --> 00:33:26,410
Today, I won't be crying no matter what.

770
00:33:26,410 --> 00:33:29,880
If you think about it,
a lot of body language...

771
00:33:29,910 --> 00:33:33,580
and psychological factors go
into this game.

772
00:33:33,680 --> 00:33:35,250
I feel pretty confident about it.

773
00:33:35,950 --> 00:33:37,550
They said we could transfer our funds.

774
00:33:37,550 --> 00:33:38,960
- Really? Let's go then.
- Yes.

775
00:33:38,990 --> 00:33:40,260
- Ji Hoo.
- Yes.

776
00:33:40,260 --> 00:33:41,720
He's going to give you some money.

777
00:33:41,720 --> 00:33:42,790
- Really?
- Let's go.

778
