I got busted. Good luck to the killer.

1030
00:43:44,830 --> 00:43:46,330
He's either a psycho, a pickpocket,

1031
00:43:46,330 --> 00:43:47,330
- or a gambler.
- Good luck, killer.

1032
00:43:47,330 --> 00:43:48,600
I guess we're all neutral.

1033
00:43:48,600 --> 00:43:50,700
What kind of role does a psychopath have?

1034
00:43:52,840 --> 00:43:55,770
Kang Ji Hoo,
please point to one Role Card.

1035
00:43:59,810 --> 00:44:00,940
Your role is...

1036
00:44:01,640 --> 00:44:02,880
Your role is...

1037
00:44:04,780 --> 00:44:06,750
Shin Seung Yong,
please head to the Voting Room.

1038
00:44:06,750 --> 00:44:08,080
- Good luck.
- Are you the last?

1039
00:44:08,680 --> 00:44:11,790
Tell us the plan
after you come back, okay?

1040
00:44:12,220 --> 00:44:13,260
Everyone picked one, right?

1041
00:44:18,790 --> 00:44:20,260
Your role is...

1042
00:44:20,860 --> 00:44:22,930
(Shocked)

1043
00:44:23,900 --> 00:44:25,470
Please leave the Voting Room.

1044
00:44:25,500 --> 00:44:31,210
(All 12 players have picked their roles.)

1045
00:44:31,310 --> 00:44:32,470
Okay, thank you.

1046
00:44:40,150 --> 00:44:43,950
I'm a citizen.

1047
00:44:47,220 --> 00:44:48,560
I have a proposal for you all.

1048
00:44:48,560 --> 00:44:50,460
- Good!
- Yes!

1049
00:44:50,460 --> 00:44:51,790
You know how we choose the room?

1050
00:44:51,790 --> 00:44:54,400
How about choosing a room besides Room F?

1051
00:44:54,800 --> 00:44:57,930
It'd be a loss for the killer.

1052
00:44:57,930 --> 00:44:58,930
In short, rule out one possibility?

1053
00:44:58,930 --> 00:45:00,100
Yes, rule out one possibility.

1054
00:45:00,100 --> 00:45:02,870
If we choose a room among Rooms A to E,

1055
00:45:02,870 --> 00:45:05,210
there's a higher chance
for citizens to live.

1056
00:45:05,210 --> 00:45:06,510
The probability of overlapping is high.

1057
00:45:06,510 --> 00:45:08,210
- Hear!
- Hear!

1058
00:45:08,340 --> 00:45:09,550
The one against it is the killer.

1059
00:45:10,610 --> 00:45:14,180
Probability-wise, I knew it was a plan
in favor of the citizens.

1060
00:45:14,480 --> 00:45:16,790
The plan will also help identify...

1061
00:45:16,790 --> 00:45:20,120
those who disagree with it,
indicating that they are not part...

1062
00:45:20,120 --> 00:45:22,060
of the citizen alliance team.

1063
00:45:23,390 --> 00:45:25,330
How about excluding Room A as well?

1064
00:45:25,360 --> 00:45:26,360
- Room A?
- Yes.

1065
00:45:26,360 --> 00:45:27,400
- Right.
- If we eliminate the rooms at the ends...

1066
00:45:27,400 --> 00:45:28,730
What if we get Rooms A or F?

1067
00:45:28,730 --> 00:45:31,970
We'll rule out the possibility...

1068
00:45:31,970 --> 00:45:33,400
of getting Rooms A and F.

1069
00:45:33,400 --> 00:45:34,870
If we pick one room
out of Rooms B, C, D, and E,

1070
00:45:34,870 --> 00:45:36,670
the probability goes down drastically.

1071
00:45:37,270 --> 00:45:39,010
It was far from what I had imagined.

1072
00:45:39,010 --> 00:45:41,710
Jin Ho even said we shouldn't choose...

1073
00:45:41,710 --> 00:45:43,250
Room A.

1074
00:45:43,310 --> 00:45:46,080
Not going into that room
was a plan only among us.

1075
00:45:46,080 --> 00:45:48,220
But Jin Ho brought it up.

1076
00:45:48,220 --> 00:45:49,850
His being a killer is very unlikely.

1077
00:45:51,290 --> 00:45:53,020
- I'm in.
- Rule out two rooms.

1078
00:45:53,020 --> 00:45:55,960
If we get Rooms A or F,
leave the decision to them.

1079
00:45:55,960 --> 00:45:56,960
Okay.

1080
00:45:57,430 --> 00:45:58,930
Is everyone in on it?

1081
00:46:00,800 --> 00:46:01,860
- Yes.
- Yes.

1082
00:46:02,600 --> 00:46:04,070
Of course, when my life is on the line.

1083
00:46:04,070 --> 00:46:05,130
Seung Yong.

1084
00:46:06,100 --> 00:46:08,100
You had a good look
at everyone's faces just now, right?

1085
00:46:08,800 --> 00:46:10,840
Someone looked a little unhappy about it.

1086
00:46:10,840 --> 00:46:12,910
- Exactly.
- Remember who it was.

1087
00:46:12,910 --> 00:46:14,940
- Remember that face.
- That's why we gave you time.

1088
00:46:15,610 --> 00:46:17,650
- I'd like to make a tip-off.
- Okay.

1089
00:46:17,650 --> 00:46:20,250
I'm a model citizen.

1090
00:46:21,250 --> 00:46:22,580
- So?
- I'm a model citizen.

1091
00:46:22,580 --> 00:46:25,050
As someone who has watched Bloody Game...

1092
00:46:25,050 --> 00:46:27,320
since Season One,

1093
00:46:27,460 --> 00:46:29,790
I've been seeing new expressions
from someone.

1094
00:46:29,790 --> 00:46:31,760
It's awkward for me to talk to.

1095
00:46:31,760 --> 00:46:33,830
- Who is it?
- It's Tae Gyun.

1096
00:46:33,830 --> 00:46:34,860
- Me?
- Yes.

1097
00:46:35,260 --> 00:46:36,900
Tae Gyun is making weird expressions.

1098
00:46:37,230 --> 00:46:39,200
- He's not good at poker faces.
- Tae Gyun is awfully quiet today.

1099
00:46:39,200 --> 00:46:40,770
That's because the others were talking.

1100
00:46:40,770 --> 00:46:41,800
He's shaking his leg.

1101
00:46:41,940 --> 00:46:43,040
It's a habit.

1102
00:46:43,740 --> 00:46:45,010
He sure looks weird.

1103
00:46:45,010 --> 00:46:46,810
I don't know what's weird,

1104
00:46:46,810 --> 00:46:48,080
but your current expression
does look weird.

1105
00:46:48,080 --> 00:46:51,410
Tae Gyun usually comes up with a plan
within 30 seconds.

1106
00:46:51,410 --> 00:46:52,450
But he's dead quiet.

1107
00:46:52,450 --> 00:46:54,620
- Exactly.
- I've never seen him like that before.

1108
00:46:55,020 --> 00:46:56,120
What an awkward expression.

1109
00:46:57,920 --> 00:46:59,020
Awkward, for real.

1110
00:46:59,020 --> 00:47:00,060
Hold on.

1111
00:47:00,060 --> 00:47:01,890
What is there to say right now?

1112
00:47:03,860 --> 00:47:04,860
What's wrong with you?

1113
00:47:05,560 --> 00:47:07,400
I'm loving this.
I love how we're ganging up on him.

1114
00:47:07,400 --> 00:47:08,600
- Yes.
- Ganging up on him is great.

1115
00:47:08,600 --> 00:47:11,000
Being good at even mind games is...

1116
00:47:11,630 --> 00:47:13,900
The role draw has ended.

1117
00:47:14,000 --> 00:47:17,540
We will now provide information
based on each role.

1118
00:47:17,610 --> 00:47:19,070
Since we need to know the killer?

1119
00:47:19,070 --> 00:47:21,280
The killer and follower
will trade information here.

1120
00:47:21,440 --> 00:47:24,250
(Revealing the identities to the killer)

1121
00:47:24,410 --> 00:47:25,880
Please check the information.

1122
00:47:25,880 --> 00:47:26,980
(Revealing the identities
to the follower and dirty cop)

1123
00:47:26,980 --> 00:47:31,790
(However, the follower and dirty cop
do not know each other's identities.)

1124
00:47:31,950 --> 00:47:34,860
(Follower, Dirty Cop)

1125
00:47:34,860 --> 00:47:37,430
Revealing your job to everyone...

1126
00:47:37,430 --> 00:47:39,430
isn't a bad idea.

1127
00:47:39,700 --> 00:47:40,730
Right?

1128
00:47:40,900 --> 00:47:43,670
It'd be weird if yours overlap
with another's.

1129
00:47:44,470 --> 00:47:46,700
Revealing it won't be a big deal.

1130
00:47:47,740 --> 00:47:48,770
What do you think?

1131
00:47:48,870 --> 00:47:49,940
Let me think about it.

1132
00:47:51,140 --> 00:47:53,410
Honestly, I didn't want to reveal mine.

1133
00:47:53,610 --> 00:47:55,040
It wasn't something we discussed earlier.

1134
00:47:55,040 --> 00:47:57,550
But bringing that up
after picking out our jobs...

1135
00:47:57,550 --> 00:48:00,850
made me wonder
if Seung Yong was a villain...

1136
00:48:01,280 --> 00:48:02,580
or part of the evil force.

1137
00:48:02,580 --> 00:48:04,920
But I also knew Seung Yong...

1138
00:48:04,920 --> 00:48:06,390
had a reason.

1139
00:48:06,390 --> 00:48:08,120
What do you think...

1140
00:48:08,120 --> 00:48:10,090
about disclosing our jobs?

1141
00:48:10,090 --> 00:48:11,930
- It's a bad idea.
- How come?

1142
00:48:12,660 --> 00:48:14,830
Some will lie about it.

1143
00:48:15,160 --> 00:48:16,730
But lying doesn't matter, does it?

1144
00:48:17,030 --> 00:48:21,200
The con of revealing our jobs is that...

1145
00:48:21,200 --> 00:48:22,940
the dirty cop on the killer's side...

1146
00:48:22,940 --> 00:48:25,010
might commit suicide with a citizen.

1147
00:48:25,010 --> 00:48:26,380
That would be unfavorable
for the citizens.

1148
00:48:26,380 --> 00:48:27,910
Reveal our jobs,

1149
00:48:27,910 --> 00:48:29,780
and the dirty cop might arrest the cop.

1150
00:48:30,310 --> 00:48:32,780
The citizens might lose a favorable card.

1151
00:48:33,020 --> 00:48:34,250
- The risks are too high.
- Right.

1152
00:48:34,250 --> 00:48:35,320
- The others don't have risks.
- Shin Seung Yong,

1153
00:48:35,320 --> 00:48:36,520
please head to the Voting Room.

1154
00:48:36,590 --> 00:48:39,720
(Seung Yong goes to the Voting Room.)

1155
00:48:39,720 --> 00:48:41,790
It's not something hard to grasp.

1156
00:48:41,790 --> 00:48:43,430
We should still doubt him
since Seung Yong...

1157
00:48:43,430 --> 00:48:45,190
- brought it up.
- What does Seung Yong want?

1158
00:48:45,630 --> 00:48:46,730
Disclose our jobs.

1159
00:48:47,030 --> 00:48:49,360
- Here's why it's absurd.
- Nonsense.

1160
00:48:49,360 --> 00:48:52,330
Without the forensic doctor
in the citizen team...

1161
00:48:52,330 --> 00:48:53,800
- It'd impact the citizens.
- Exactly.

1162
00:48:53,800 --> 00:48:56,510
- Winning would be impossible.
- Using that one special ability is...

1163
00:48:56,670 --> 00:48:59,010
"Let's reveal our jobs."

1164
00:48:59,410 --> 00:49:01,810
Even if we do that,

1165
00:49:01,940 --> 00:49:05,280
it'll only be hard to tell
who's telling the truth.

1166
00:49:05,280 --> 00:49:06,920
The killer and neutral teams...

1167
00:49:06,920 --> 00:49:10,050
will be able
to find out the citizen team's jobs.

1168
00:49:10,050 --> 00:49:12,320
Will trying hard from the start...

1169
00:49:12,320 --> 00:49:14,460
be of help to the game?

1170
00:49:14,460 --> 00:49:16,830
(The last player to exchange
the killer faction information is...)

1171
00:49:16,830 --> 00:49:18,190
(Shin Seung Yong.)

1172
00:49:21,560 --> 00:49:23,030
Please standby.

1173
00:49:29,970 --> 00:49:31,440
Your role is...

1174
00:49:32,010 --> 00:49:33,040
a citizen.

1175
00:49:34,140 --> 00:49:35,440
(Citizen)

1176
00:49:35,580 --> 00:49:38,880
As I'm a citizen without any ability,

1177
00:49:39,080 --> 00:49:40,780
it won't cause any trouble...

1178
00:49:40,820 --> 00:49:44,450
to the citizen faction
even if I get arrested.

1179
00:49:44,450 --> 00:49:46,290
That's why I disclosed my job.

1180
00:49:46,290 --> 00:49:49,060
I wanted to find the first person to lie.

1181
00:49:49,060 --> 00:49:52,630
There must be a reason
that person chose to lie.

1182
00:49:52,630 --> 00:49:54,430
Who is lying?

1183
00:49:54,430 --> 00:49:56,200
Who is acting out of the ordinary?

1184
00:49:56,200 --> 00:49:57,630
I wanted to figure that out the most.

1185
00:49:58,070 --> 00:50:00,640
What Jin Ho mentioned last is valid.

1186
00:50:00,740 --> 00:50:02,000
It's nothing tough,

1187
00:50:02,000 --> 00:50:04,740
but making such a proposal
is quite interesting.

1188
00:50:04,740 --> 00:50:07,680
Daytime for Round One has arrived.

1189
00:50:07,680 --> 00:50:09,640
- This is fun.
- You may...

1190
00:50:09,640 --> 00:50:11,550
freely move around for 30 minutes.

1191
00:50:11,750 --> 00:50:13,180
- You may...
- Buy an item.

1192
00:50:13,180 --> 00:50:14,580
- freely move around for 30 minutes.
- Let's go buy an item.

1193
00:50:16,320 --> 00:50:18,620
There's not a big difference, is there?

1194
00:50:18,620 --> 00:50:19,820
(An early rush for the item)

1195
00:50:24,890 --> 00:50:26,130
Are you going to buy the item?

1196
00:50:26,400 --> 00:50:28,060
Whatever, I'm not buying one.

1197
00:50:29,430 --> 00:50:31,430
- Item.
- I should've bought one.

1198
00:50:31,700 --> 00:50:33,870
I was spacing out. What an idiot.

1199
00:50:33,940 --> 00:50:35,240
A get-out-of-jail card is a must.

1200
00:50:35,240 --> 00:50:37,840
Those who didn't rush over are shady.

1201
00:50:38,010 --> 00:50:39,210
Those who don't need it...

1202
00:50:39,210 --> 00:50:40,940
could be killers or evil people.

1203
00:50:48,920 --> 00:50:50,420
How may I help you?

1204
00:50:50,790 --> 00:50:53,590
I'd like to get both a room selection
ticket and a get-out-of-jail card.

1205
00:50:53,890 --> 00:50:55,460
Park Ji Min,
20,000 dollars will be deducted...

1206
00:50:55,460 --> 00:50:56,860
- from your funds.
- Got it.

1207
00:50:56,860 --> 00:50:58,530
(Purchased a room selection ticket
and a get-out-of-jail card)

1208
00:50:58,830 --> 00:51:00,000
Were the items 3 and 2?

1209
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:01,760
- Three and three.
- Three and three?

1210
00:51:03,000 --> 00:51:04,730
- I'm sorry.
- Be careful.

1211
00:51:08,000 --> 00:51:10,410
From what I see, it's Tae Gyun for sure.

1212
00:51:10,410 --> 00:51:11,510
He's for sure on the evil team.

1213
00:51:13,110 --> 00:51:15,010
Tae Gyun looks incredibly uneasy.

1214
00:51:19,150 --> 00:51:21,980
Tae Gyun isn't the type
to get so discouraged.

1215
00:51:21,980 --> 00:51:23,590
But his face became grim,

1216
00:51:23,590 --> 00:51:25,150
and he started acting all awkward.

1217
00:51:25,290 --> 00:51:26,390
(Laughing)

1218
00:51:26,390 --> 00:51:27,620
He got one of the roles.

1219
00:51:27,760 --> 00:51:29,760
He got one of the evil roles.

1220
00:51:29,760 --> 00:51:33,560
I was certain Tae Gyun was
in the killer faction.

1221
00:51:33,560 --> 00:51:35,830
Dirty cop? Killer? Follower?

1222
00:51:35,830 --> 00:51:37,300
He must be one of the three.

1223
00:51:37,300 --> 00:51:39,100
But if he's that flustered,

1224
00:51:39,430 --> 00:51:40,540
is Tae Gyun the killer?

1225
00:51:42,170 --> 00:51:43,170
You startled me.

1226
00:51:43,170 --> 00:51:44,810
The run was worth it.

1227
00:51:45,510 --> 00:51:47,040
You sure were fast like a bullet...

1228
00:51:47,040 --> 00:51:49,310
now that we're in individual competition.

1229
00:51:51,250 --> 00:51:52,280
One of each, please.

1230
00:51:52,280 --> 00:51:55,420
Heo Seong Beom, 20,000 dollars
will be deducted from your funds.

1231
00:51:57,220 --> 00:51:58,250
I'd like...

1232
00:51:58,250 --> 00:52:00,320
one get-out-of-jail card.

1233
00:52:00,890 --> 00:52:02,120
(Hong Jin Ho purchased
1 get-out-of-jail card.)

1234
00:52:02,120 --> 00:52:03,390
Do I keep it?

1235
00:52:03,560 --> 00:52:04,660
Oh, dear.

1236
00:52:05,890 --> 00:52:07,330
What's on your mind?

1237
00:52:07,330 --> 00:52:08,530
You're being hilarious.

1238
00:52:08,560 --> 00:52:10,800
I'm in no way used to this game.

1239
00:52:10,800 --> 00:52:12,700
- It gives me a headache.
- He's bluffing.

1240
00:52:12,900 --> 00:52:14,200
No, for real. This is my first time.

1241
00:52:15,300 --> 00:52:17,210
I don't play Mafia Game over drinks now.

1242
00:52:17,210 --> 00:52:18,210
That's true.

1243
00:52:18,210 --> 00:52:19,270
Same here. It's been a while.

1244
00:52:22,580 --> 00:52:24,250
How may I help you?

1245
00:52:25,610 --> 00:52:27,120
I'd like to buy a get-out-of-jail card.

1246
00:52:27,280 --> 00:52:29,680
The get-out-of-jail card is sold out.

1247
00:52:30,850 --> 00:52:32,190
I won't be needing anything.

1248
00:52:32,320 --> 00:52:33,820
Do you still have
the room selection ticket?

1249
00:52:34,190 --> 00:52:37,160
Hyun Sung Joo, 10,000 dollars
will be deducted from your funds.

1250
00:52:42,200 --> 00:52:43,670
(Smiling)

1251
00:52:43,670 --> 00:52:44,870
Why are you smiling?

1252
00:52:46,400 --> 00:52:47,500
He's acting weird.

1253
00:52:49,270 --> 00:52:50,840
What's with him?

1254
00:52:51,540 --> 00:52:52,610
What's up with him?

1255
00:52:52,670 --> 00:52:54,310
- What?
- What's with that face?

1256
00:52:54,310 --> 00:52:55,310
Sung Joo is really weird today.

1257
00:52:55,310 --> 00:52:57,180
He's too hyper today.

1258
00:52:57,180 --> 00:52:58,180
- Right?
- Is he doing that on purpose?

1259
00:52:58,780 --> 00:53:01,250
(Sung Joo looks happier than usual today.)

1260
00:53:03,080 --> 00:53:05,020
- Sung Joo is acting...
- Yes?

1261
00:53:05,990 --> 00:53:07,160
really strange.

1262
00:53:08,420 --> 00:53:10,460
After picking out a Role Card,

1263
00:53:10,460 --> 00:53:13,500
Sung Joo's expression and behavior...

1264
00:53:13,700 --> 00:53:15,530
felt weird.

1265
00:53:15,530 --> 00:53:19,070
That flustered look he had
during the Deathmatch.

1266
00:53:19,070 --> 00:53:20,070
It was that kind of look.

1267
00:53:21,100 --> 00:53:23,340
With that,
I knew he was in the killer faction.

1268
00:53:25,210 --> 00:53:27,310
(Laughing)

1269
00:53:27,310 --> 00:53:28,340
What is it?

1270
00:53:28,580 --> 00:53:29,580
I'm just enjoying it.

1271
00:53:30,610 --> 00:53:31,980
Why are you so excited, Sung Joo?

1272
00:53:32,150 --> 00:53:34,280
- You know something, right?
- I know nothing.

1273
00:53:34,280 --> 00:53:35,820
- Stop lying.
- Which faction would I likely be in...

1274
00:53:35,820 --> 00:53:37,350
if I look excited?

1275
00:53:37,520 --> 00:53:39,420
Excited,
you wrote something down in that corner.

1276
00:53:40,020 --> 00:53:41,190
You're not usually like that.

1277
00:53:41,620 --> 00:53:43,960
It's nothing important,
but I can't tell you.

1278
00:53:44,330 --> 00:53:45,460
Is this guy the killer?

1279
00:53:45,960 --> 00:53:47,500
You have too much on your mind now.

1280
00:53:47,600 --> 00:53:49,900
I'm only getting the rules down.

1281
00:53:49,900 --> 00:53:52,230
- Look at him bluffing.
- Still on the rules?

1282
00:53:52,300 --> 00:53:54,900
He's been bluffing since yesterday.

1283
00:53:58,640 --> 00:53:59,940
Earlier when we lined up,

1284
00:53:59,940 --> 00:54:00,940
(Seong Beom and Jin Ho are talking alone.)

1285
00:54:00,940 --> 00:54:02,380
it was Ji Min, Seong Beom...

1286
00:54:05,450 --> 00:54:06,720
- Did you get one?
- It's super weird.

1287
00:54:06,780 --> 00:54:07,850
What is weird?

1288
00:54:07,850 --> 00:54:09,150
- I went in fourth, right?
- Yes.

1289
00:54:09,150 --> 00:54:10,590
You bought
the get-out-of-jail card, right?

1290
00:54:10,590 --> 00:54:11,690
- You bought one, right?
- Yes.

1291
00:54:11,690 --> 00:54:13,960
I knew that because I was the fourth.
They were sold out in my turn.

1292
00:54:13,960 --> 00:54:15,490
- And I met YunB.
- Okay.

1293
00:54:15,490 --> 00:54:17,060
I asked YunB what he bought.

1294
00:54:17,060 --> 00:54:18,260
I expected him to say nothing.

1295
00:54:18,260 --> 00:54:19,760
But he said
he bought the get-out-of-jail card.

1296
00:54:20,600 --> 00:54:25,170
(The get-out-of-jail card is sold out
because the 1st 3 people bought it.)

1297
00:54:25,430 --> 00:54:27,700
(Hye Seon went into the room 4th.)

1298
00:54:29,870 --> 00:54:30,870
What did you get?

1299
00:54:31,270 --> 00:54:33,070
This one.

1300
00:54:33,510 --> 00:54:34,540
The get-out-of-jail card.

1301
00:54:34,810 --> 00:54:36,650
(YunB lied
that he bought a get-out-of-jail card.)

1302
00:54:36,950 --> 00:54:38,880
- He lied.
- Here's what I wanted to tell you.

1303
00:54:38,880 --> 00:54:39,910
YunB is...

1304
00:54:40,750 --> 00:54:42,720
- Is he an idiot?
- No, I don't know what he is.

1305
00:54:43,420 --> 00:54:45,890
- You know.
- He might just be lying...

1306
00:54:46,120 --> 00:54:47,290
- so as not to tell you.
- Yes.

1307
00:54:47,290 --> 00:54:48,290
Maybe.

1308
00:54:53,800 --> 00:54:54,960
Why is Hye Seon acting out?

1309
00:54:56,060 --> 00:55:01,070
(10 minutes ago)

1310
00:55:06,840 --> 00:55:08,340
How may I help you?

1311
00:55:08,540 --> 00:55:09,840
I'm just bluffing.

1312
00:55:10,350 --> 00:55:12,010
I'll leave after another ten seconds.

1313
00:55:18,450 --> 00:55:21,020
I had to find who the cop was,
no matter what.

1314
00:55:21,020 --> 00:55:22,960
Or the psychic or forensic doctor.

1315
00:55:23,760 --> 00:55:26,730
YunB, please point to one Role Card.

1316
00:55:26,730 --> 00:55:27,800
(Drawing the Killer Game Role Card)

1317
00:55:27,900 --> 00:55:30,300
Your role is a dirty cop.

1318
00:55:30,300 --> 00:55:31,500
(Dirty Cop YunB)

1319
00:55:31,500 --> 00:55:35,140
I had the confidence to pull off my role
as a dirty cop well.

1320
00:55:35,140 --> 00:55:38,240
It was a role I was very comfortable with.

1321
00:55:38,270 --> 00:55:41,280
I already knew who the killer was.

1322
00:55:41,610 --> 00:55:44,610
Even if I were in the same room
with the killer, I wouldn't die.

1323
00:55:44,850 --> 00:55:47,720
To put it bluntly,
it was a role I could go all out with,

1324
00:55:47,720 --> 00:55:50,490
mess up the plan, and gain information...

1325
00:55:50,750 --> 00:55:52,590
more easily.

1326
00:55:52,590 --> 00:55:54,620
Without a question,

1327
00:55:54,620 --> 00:55:56,390
my first target is the cop.

1328
00:55:56,390 --> 00:55:59,330
I have the responsibility
to get rid of anyone...

1329
00:55:59,330 --> 00:56:02,000
who knows who the killer is...

1330
00:56:02,000 --> 00:56:05,070
or instigates others.

1331
00:56:13,940 --> 00:56:16,640
What kind of plans did the teams share?

1332
00:56:16,640 --> 00:56:18,010
That was it.

1333
00:56:18,010 --> 00:56:19,910
Whether or not to disclose our jobs?

1334
00:56:20,780 --> 00:56:23,890
- If we get into a fix...
- From your experience,

1335
00:56:23,990 --> 00:56:26,790
was Seung Yong the type...

1336
00:56:26,790 --> 00:56:29,320
to come up with plans and such?

1337
00:56:29,720 --> 00:56:31,030
- Yes, he was.
- Is that so?

1338
00:56:31,030 --> 00:56:32,760
And he did well,
including in the Deathmatch.

1339
00:56:32,760 --> 00:56:33,860
- Is that so?
- Yes.

1340
00:56:34,900 --> 00:56:37,270
The plan that Seung Yong came up with.

1341
00:56:37,830 --> 00:56:39,330
It was obvious that...

1342
00:56:39,330 --> 00:56:41,970
it'd play against the citizens.

1343
00:56:42,400 --> 00:56:45,010
What's more,
Seung Yong was being proactive.

1344
00:56:45,010 --> 00:56:46,270
He's proposing it...

1345
00:56:46,270 --> 00:56:48,680
despite the plan being a dangerous move...

1346
00:56:49,410 --> 00:56:51,550
Did he simply propose it...

1347
00:56:51,550 --> 00:56:52,950
because he didn't understand the game?

1348
00:56:53,350 --> 00:56:56,380
When he mentioned the plan was unfavorable
to the citizens...

1349
00:56:56,990 --> 00:56:59,020
"Just listen to him."

1350
00:56:59,190 --> 00:57:01,860
We already did the math...

1351
00:57:01,860 --> 00:57:03,390
and worked out the probability.

1352
00:57:04,930 --> 00:57:06,800
But to say it's unfavorable?

1353
00:57:06,860 --> 00:57:08,900
Shall I tell you what Tae Gyun just said?

1354
00:57:09,130 --> 00:57:12,030
You know how people tell you the room
they were just in?

1355
00:57:12,030 --> 00:57:14,300
He said it was a completely wrong move.

1356
00:57:14,300 --> 00:57:16,470
It's a rule made by someone
who doesn't know the rules.

1357
00:57:16,640 --> 00:57:17,670
That was what he said.

1358
00:57:18,110 --> 00:57:19,140
What do you think?

1359
00:57:19,140 --> 00:57:20,840
The probability of survival
was 25 percent, but now it's 38 percent.

1360
00:57:20,840 --> 00:57:24,380
- It went from 25 to 38 percent, right?
- Yes.

1361
00:57:24,610 --> 00:57:27,250
Tae Gyun is quick with numbers.

1362
00:57:27,650 --> 00:57:29,520
But he said...

1363
00:57:29,520 --> 00:57:31,490
the probability was bad,
which is the complete opposite.

1364
00:57:31,490 --> 00:57:33,120
It's as if
he was trying to mess things up.

1365
00:57:34,120 --> 00:57:37,330
Tae Gyun is also trying to gang up
on Seung Yong.

1366
00:57:38,260 --> 00:57:41,530
What can the psychic do right now?

1367
00:57:42,200 --> 00:57:43,200
The psychic?

1368
00:57:43,200 --> 00:57:45,430
Even if the psychic knows
how many are in the room, it's...

1369
00:57:45,430 --> 00:57:46,470
- Right.
- It's...

1370
00:57:46,470 --> 00:57:47,940
Knowing who the killer is and who is what.

1371
00:57:47,940 --> 00:57:49,440
Exactly. It's meaningless.

1372
00:57:49,440 --> 00:57:50,540
Figuring it out is impossible.

1373
00:57:51,170 --> 00:57:52,640
Even if we ask everyone...

1374
00:57:52,640 --> 00:57:54,510
where they were after the game,

1375
00:57:54,510 --> 00:57:56,310
some will lie about it.

1376
00:57:56,540 --> 00:57:58,010
It's too hard to verify
whether it's true...

1377
00:57:58,010 --> 00:57:59,750
and cross-check it with this.

1378
00:57:59,910 --> 00:58:02,580
Is there any reason to lie
if they're on the citizens' side?

1379
00:58:02,950 --> 00:58:06,750
The probability is close to 50-50.

1380
00:58:06,860 --> 00:58:08,390
There are 12 of us.

1381
00:58:08,390 --> 00:58:11,730
Three are neutral,
and three are in the mafia's faction.

1382
00:58:11,790 --> 00:58:13,800
Half is true,
while the other half is false.

1383
00:58:13,800 --> 00:58:15,560
- But distinguishing that is tough.
- Exactly.

1384
00:58:15,560 --> 00:58:17,970
Isn't it fine to be suspicious
if anyone lies at least once?

1385
00:58:17,970 --> 00:58:19,570
- How would you know that?
- Who lied?

1386
00:58:19,570 --> 00:58:20,700
The psychic would know.

1387
00:58:20,700 --> 00:58:23,870
The forensic doctor
can obtain information...

1388
00:58:23,870 --> 00:58:24,970
only when something happens,

1389
00:58:24,970 --> 00:58:27,640
but the psychic can obtain information
at any time.

1390
00:58:27,640 --> 00:58:28,680
It's a game where the psychic...

1391
00:58:28,680 --> 00:58:29,740
- must do well.
- Yes.

1392
00:58:29,740 --> 00:58:32,680
- Exactly.
- Someone will lie for sure.

1393
00:58:32,680 --> 00:58:35,120
They'd get busted in one of the rounds.

1394
00:58:35,120 --> 00:58:37,220
Either way, the psychic will know that.

1395
00:58:37,220 --> 00:58:39,150
If we keep asking around,

1396
00:58:39,320 --> 00:58:41,520
someone will keep changing their words...

1397
00:58:41,520 --> 00:58:43,490
or say something different.

1398
00:58:43,760 --> 00:58:46,790
I think it's best to give
all the information to the psychic.

1399
00:58:48,230 --> 00:58:50,200
- That startled me.
- Nighttime has arrived.

1400
00:58:50,270 --> 00:58:52,400
The more rounds we play,
