1527
01:05:00,870 --> 01:05:01,870
Room E.

1528
01:05:01,870 --> 01:05:02,870
(Room E: Jin Ho)

1529
01:05:02,870 --> 01:05:03,940
- Keun Woo?
- I...

1530
01:05:04,040 --> 01:05:05,070
Room B.

1531
01:05:05,140 --> 01:05:06,240
Sung Joo.

1532
01:05:06,610 --> 01:05:08,080
- Room B.
- Sung Joo in Room B.

1533
01:05:08,080 --> 01:05:09,810
Next, Ji Min.

1534
01:05:10,180 --> 01:05:11,410
Room C.

1535
01:05:11,410 --> 01:05:12,750
(Room C: Seong Beom, Ji Min)

1536
01:05:12,750 --> 01:05:14,350
- Next, Tae Gyun.
- I'm in Room B.

1537
01:05:14,980 --> 01:05:16,620
- Next, Beom.
- Room B.

1538
01:05:17,320 --> 01:05:18,450
It's packed.

1539
01:05:18,450 --> 01:05:20,520
- Next, Xitsuh.
- Room B.

1540
01:05:20,520 --> 01:05:21,690
What?

1541
01:05:21,690 --> 01:05:22,860
Next, Ji Hoo.

1542
01:05:22,860 --> 01:05:24,190
- Room B.
- What?

1543
01:05:24,830 --> 01:05:26,630
- Hye Seon?
- Room B.

1544
01:05:27,530 --> 01:05:28,960
- Next, YunB.
- Room D.

1545
01:05:30,530 --> 01:05:31,770
Seung Yong is in Room C.

1546
01:05:32,500 --> 01:05:33,830
Wait, I'm alone?

1547
01:05:34,140 --> 01:05:35,600
You could have gotten killed.

1548
01:05:35,940 --> 01:05:38,470
- You and YunB could have died.
- You and YunB.

1549
01:05:38,470 --> 01:05:39,540
(YunB and Jin Ho in danger)

1550
01:05:39,540 --> 01:05:40,710
YunB!

1551
01:05:41,640 --> 01:05:42,740
YunB is here.

1552
01:05:42,740 --> 01:05:45,810
It's totally crowded.
I'll tell you the result.

1553
01:05:46,080 --> 01:05:48,150
Room A, 0. Room B, 7.

1554
01:05:48,150 --> 01:05:50,480
Room C, 3. Room D, 1. Room E, 1.

1555
01:05:50,480 --> 01:05:51,550
Room F, zero.

1556
01:05:52,050 --> 01:05:54,760
For the psychic
to make their own decision,

1557
01:05:54,760 --> 01:05:58,060
I was trying to get ahead
and organize the information...

1558
01:05:58,060 --> 01:05:59,190
for them.

1559
01:05:59,260 --> 01:06:01,400
How many in Room C?

1560
01:06:02,300 --> 01:06:03,300
I'll repeat.

1561
01:06:03,300 --> 01:06:05,270
Room A, 0. Room B, 7.

1562
01:06:05,270 --> 01:06:07,340
Room C, 3. Room D, 1.

1563
01:06:07,340 --> 01:06:09,340
Room E, 1. Room F, 0.

1564
01:06:10,200 --> 01:06:11,210
That's 7, 3, 1, 1.

1565
01:06:12,070 --> 01:06:13,910
I don't think this is the right strategy.

1566
01:06:13,910 --> 01:06:15,880
Hold on. We need to stop.

1567
01:06:16,010 --> 01:06:18,410
The killer must be bummed out by now.

1568
01:06:18,550 --> 01:06:20,650
- I'm in danger.
- They must be so bummed out.

1569
01:06:23,080 --> 01:06:24,790
We were in the...

1570
01:06:28,590 --> 01:06:29,890
We told each other...

1571
01:06:29,890 --> 01:06:31,860
which rooms we went to after Round One.

1572
01:06:33,560 --> 01:06:35,560
And something felt off.

1573
01:06:39,300 --> 01:06:40,370
I'm a psychic.

1574
01:06:40,370 --> 01:06:41,400
(Psychic: Heo Seong Beom)

1575
01:06:41,400 --> 01:06:43,540
As the psychic,

1576
01:06:43,540 --> 01:06:45,870
I can find out how many people were
with me...

1577
01:06:45,870 --> 01:06:47,680
the night before.

1578
01:06:47,980 --> 01:06:50,410
So, if I were to do it,

1579
01:06:50,580 --> 01:06:53,150
I could ask everyone where they were...

1580
01:06:53,150 --> 01:06:56,050
and figure out who's lying.

1581
01:06:56,050 --> 01:07:02,090
(After Round 1)

1582
01:07:02,090 --> 01:07:03,160
Hello?

1583
01:07:03,490 --> 01:07:05,730
Last night, Room C was occupied...

1584
01:07:07,030 --> 01:07:08,630
- by two people.
- Okay.

1585
01:07:09,330 --> 01:07:12,000
I wasn't sure if anyone would lie
in Round One.

1586
01:07:12,270 --> 01:07:13,330
Room C.

1587
01:07:13,530 --> 01:07:14,870
Seung Yong is in Room C.

1588
01:07:15,340 --> 01:07:18,070
I found out
that either Seung Yong or Ji Min,

1589
01:07:18,070 --> 01:07:20,910
the ones who claimed to be in my room,

1590
01:07:20,910 --> 01:07:23,510
were lying.

1591
01:07:23,740 --> 01:07:26,250
Seung Yong plays...

1592
01:07:26,580 --> 01:07:28,620
like a citizen.

1593
01:07:29,280 --> 01:07:30,580
So, could it be Ji Min?

1594
01:07:31,820 --> 01:07:34,990
I decided to keep an eye on them.

1595
01:07:35,660 --> 01:07:38,260
Xitsuh, what's on your mind?

1596
01:07:38,860 --> 01:07:40,660
This is tough, YunB.

1597
01:07:40,660 --> 01:07:41,700
It's tough?

1598
01:07:43,100 --> 01:07:45,630
The citizens are in for it.

1599
01:07:46,570 --> 01:07:47,940
When you think about it...

1600
01:07:47,940 --> 01:07:50,940
I don't know
exactly what type Seung Yong is.

1601
01:07:50,940 --> 01:07:52,610
Do you think he's telling the truth?

1602
01:07:53,070 --> 01:07:55,140
His strategy works
in favor of the citizens.

1603
01:07:55,140 --> 01:07:58,280
It does, but is he an actual citizen?

1604
01:07:58,280 --> 01:08:00,550
At least, he has a say in this now.

1605
01:08:00,780 --> 01:08:02,950
There's a high chance that he's a citizen.

1606
01:08:02,950 --> 01:08:05,490
But if he's a normal citizen,

1607
01:08:05,490 --> 01:08:07,460
the opponents can tell right away.

1608
01:08:07,590 --> 01:08:09,120
It doesn't matter.
He can be exposed if he's a citizen.

1609
01:08:09,120 --> 01:08:10,890
I feel like he made the wrong choice.

1610
01:08:10,890 --> 01:08:14,930
- As soon as he came out...
- No, his plan might work.

1611
01:08:14,930 --> 01:08:16,000
Is that right?

1612
01:08:16,600 --> 01:08:17,700
I can't trust him, though.

1613
01:08:17,930 --> 01:08:20,200
This is...

1614
01:08:20,200 --> 01:08:21,340
But you get what I'm saying, right?

1615
01:08:22,040 --> 01:08:24,610
It's a plan
that a citizen can come up with.

1616
01:08:24,770 --> 01:08:26,640
But he did that...

1617
01:08:26,870 --> 01:08:29,040
as soon as we got our roles,
while we knew nothing.

1618
01:08:29,710 --> 01:08:30,880
Doesn't that seem weird?

1619
01:08:33,780 --> 01:08:34,880
No matter how hard I listened to YunB,

1620
01:08:34,880 --> 01:08:36,820
he wasn't making any sense.

1621
01:08:37,350 --> 01:08:38,990
Seung Yong's strategy was...

1622
01:08:39,720 --> 01:08:42,960
a typical plan, and it was logical.

1623
01:08:43,320 --> 01:08:45,030
I thought, "What is he obsessed with?"

1624
01:08:45,260 --> 01:08:46,760
"Did he get an evil role?"

1625
01:08:46,960 --> 01:08:50,130
"Why is he making illogical comments?"

1626
01:08:50,260 --> 01:08:51,770
Does that mean you and I were...

1627
01:08:51,770 --> 01:08:53,100
the only ones who were alone?

1628
01:08:53,100 --> 01:08:54,200
Right?

1629
01:08:54,200 --> 01:08:55,300
We almost died.

1630
01:08:55,300 --> 01:08:57,340
I don't like this plan.

1631
01:08:57,610 --> 01:08:59,710
It's too dangerous. It's wrong.

1632
01:09:01,810 --> 01:09:04,010
- Everyone.
- Let's pray.

1633
01:09:04,010 --> 01:09:06,210
Rooms B, C, D, and E.

1634
01:09:06,210 --> 01:09:07,520
If I were to pick among those four,

1635
01:09:07,520 --> 01:09:09,820
my number 1 pick is Room B,
and my number 2 pick is Room C.

1636
01:09:09,820 --> 01:09:11,220
- Stop saying weird stuff.
- Why are you...

1637
01:09:11,220 --> 01:09:12,620
- He's the pickpocket!
- He's the pickpocket.

1638
01:09:12,620 --> 01:09:15,760
- He's trying to manipulate us.
- I'm going to Room B or Room C.

1639
01:09:15,760 --> 01:09:17,660
Guys, I'll go to Room B or Room C.

1640
01:09:17,660 --> 01:09:20,390
Among Rooms B, C, D, and E,
I'm picking Room B or Room C.

1641
01:09:20,390 --> 01:09:23,130
- Why are you helping the killer?
- Because...

1642
01:09:23,130 --> 01:09:25,170
- the pickpocket is neutral.
- Yes.

1643
01:09:25,170 --> 01:09:26,630
- So?
- I need to share the information.

1644
01:09:26,630 --> 01:09:27,740
- Is that so?
- Yes.

1645
01:09:27,740 --> 01:09:29,440
- So, you're the pickpocket.
- I'm the pickpocket.

1646
01:09:29,440 --> 01:09:30,440
- You're the pickpocket?
- Yes.

1647
01:09:30,440 --> 01:09:32,770
The pickpocket can expose himself
whenever he wants to.

1648
01:09:33,010 --> 01:09:34,840
Guys, Jin Ho is the pickpocket!

1649
01:09:35,780 --> 01:09:37,210
But I'm the pickpocket.

1650
01:09:39,050 --> 01:09:40,110
What's his deal?

1651
01:09:40,480 --> 01:09:42,650
If you want to survive,
your number one pick...

1652
01:09:42,650 --> 01:09:43,750
should be Room B.

1653
01:09:44,080 --> 01:09:46,050
Or you can come to Room C.

1654
01:09:46,050 --> 01:09:47,590
Those are your priorities.

1655
01:09:47,590 --> 01:09:49,990
Rooms B, C, D and E.

1656
01:09:50,690 --> 01:09:53,290
I was alone there. I could have died!

1657
01:09:53,430 --> 01:09:54,900
We have to get together.

1658
01:09:55,300 --> 01:09:58,800
Jin Ho said
that he was in Room E by himself...

1659
01:09:58,930 --> 01:10:01,700
and that he could have been killed.

1660
01:10:01,700 --> 01:10:03,600
He was being a bit dramatic.

1661
01:10:04,200 --> 01:10:06,270
But I knew at the time...

1662
01:10:06,540 --> 01:10:10,610
that Jin Ho, who insisted that he was
in Room E, was not the killer.

1663
01:10:10,610 --> 01:10:11,910
If he's telling the truth, I mean.

1664
01:10:12,410 --> 01:10:13,950
(Xitsuh had pulled off a burglary
in Room E.)

1665
01:10:13,950 --> 01:10:16,520
You have chosen Room E.

1666
01:10:16,550 --> 01:10:19,490
But he could be a member
of the killer faction.

1667
01:10:19,750 --> 01:10:23,190
The psychopath or the dirty cop?

1668
01:10:23,660 --> 01:10:26,130
We have to split up randomly.

1669
01:10:26,760 --> 01:10:29,200
It's more dangerous to tell everyone
to go to Room B or Room C.

1670
01:10:30,300 --> 01:10:33,170
- Let's think about this again.
- It's like...

1671
01:10:33,170 --> 01:10:35,640
Jin Ho is leading everyone
to Rooms B and C.

1672
01:10:35,640 --> 01:10:37,710
Then, what happens to those
who didn't pick Rooms B and C?

1673
01:10:37,970 --> 01:10:39,410
- If we do...
- They'll split up.

1674
01:10:39,410 --> 01:10:41,640
You'll be in big trouble
if you go to Room B or Room C.

1675
01:10:42,580 --> 01:10:45,810
That puts those who couldn't pick
Rooms B and C in danger.

1676
01:10:45,810 --> 01:10:47,980
Then, the killer only has to pick...

1677
01:10:47,980 --> 01:10:49,520
between Rooms D and E.

1678
01:10:49,520 --> 01:10:50,550
You're being suspicious.

1679
01:10:50,720 --> 01:10:53,150
That means he's likely the follower.

1680
01:10:53,790 --> 01:10:55,560
He was sending a message to the killer.

1681
01:10:55,560 --> 01:10:57,560
- Exactly.
- It was a subtle message.

1682
01:10:57,960 --> 01:10:59,760
He's shouting to the killer...

1683
01:10:59,760 --> 01:11:00,930
to go to Room D or Room E and kill one...

1684
01:11:00,930 --> 01:11:02,930
because they'll look suspicious
if they talk alone.

1685
01:11:03,660 --> 01:11:05,800
The follower shouted it out...

1686
01:11:05,800 --> 01:11:09,040
because he couldn't talk to someone
in private.

1687
01:11:09,200 --> 01:11:12,940
We can be saved
if we all go to Rooms B and C.

1688
01:11:13,140 --> 01:11:16,140
Everyone, come to Rooms B and C
if you want to live eternally.

1689
01:11:16,210 --> 01:11:18,250
Come to Rooms B and C for eternal life.

1690
01:11:18,250 --> 01:11:20,050
There's a high chance...

1691
01:11:20,050 --> 01:11:22,280
that Jin Ho is in the killer faction.

1692
01:11:22,950 --> 01:11:24,180
- But...
- Room D or Room E.

1693
01:11:24,180 --> 01:11:26,450
This is an educated guess.

1694
01:11:26,450 --> 01:11:28,690
- What do you mean?
- No, it's just a guess.

1695
01:11:29,490 --> 01:11:33,090
I'm suspicious of Jin Ho and Sung Joo.

1696
01:11:33,460 --> 01:11:34,730
- Jin Ho and Sung Joo?
- Yes.

1697
01:11:34,730 --> 01:11:37,670
I've been suspicious of Sung Joo
since earlier.

1698
01:11:37,670 --> 01:11:39,630
- He's being so suspicious.
- Last night,

1699
01:11:39,830 --> 01:11:41,240
when we were playing Ring the Bell,

1700
01:11:41,240 --> 01:11:43,200
I said that he might not be
a poker player...

1701
01:11:43,200 --> 01:11:44,840
because it was written all over his face.

1702
01:11:45,140 --> 01:11:48,410
But it was also suspicious
when he bought that item.

1703
01:11:48,410 --> 01:11:49,780
He had no reason to buy one.

1704
01:11:49,780 --> 01:11:51,850
Why would he run off
while we were talking?

1705
01:11:52,350 --> 01:11:54,010
While he was being suspicious,

1706
01:11:54,780 --> 01:11:58,250
Jin Ho told everyone
to go to Rooms B and C,

1707
01:11:58,250 --> 01:12:02,220
and I think that was him telling
the killer to go there too.

1708
01:12:02,760 --> 01:12:04,690
Right after that, they went out...

1709
01:12:04,690 --> 01:12:06,330
- and talked...
- They talked?

1710
01:12:06,330 --> 01:12:07,530
by themselves.

1711
01:12:08,260 --> 01:12:10,600
I need a cigarette.
Let's go for a smoke break.

1712
01:12:10,600 --> 01:12:13,500
(5 minutes ago)

1713
01:12:14,270 --> 01:12:15,570
It's a reasonable strategy.

1714
01:12:15,570 --> 01:12:17,140
Why is everyone suspicious of me?

1715
01:12:19,870 --> 01:12:23,680
I think there's a chance
that Sung Joo is the killer.

1716
01:12:24,410 --> 01:12:27,080
Also, the killer doesn't have
to be so loud.

1717
01:12:27,080 --> 01:12:28,550
- So...
- Right?

1718
01:12:29,150 --> 01:12:30,550
Why are you two alone?

1719
01:12:30,650 --> 01:12:32,320
- You...
- We're on the same team.

1720
01:12:32,320 --> 01:12:35,260
I asked him, "Why did you buy an item?"
You know what he said?

1721
01:12:35,260 --> 01:12:36,660
"Which room were you in?"

1722
01:12:36,820 --> 01:12:38,990
What did you guys talk about? Tell me.

1723
01:12:39,130 --> 01:12:40,490
I asked him why he bought an item,

1724
01:12:40,490 --> 01:12:42,400
and he got all flustered and said,
"Which room were you in?"

1725
01:12:42,560 --> 01:12:44,330
I bought a red potion.

1726
01:12:44,600 --> 01:12:46,200
Sung Joo was so...

1727
01:12:46,970 --> 01:12:50,570
I caught him acting suspiciously.

1728
01:12:51,410 --> 01:12:53,270
- We need to make a move.
- Yes.

1729
01:13:00,410 --> 01:13:01,720
Nighttime has arrived.

1730
01:13:01,920 --> 01:13:04,720
The room selection will begin now.

1731
01:13:05,050 --> 01:13:07,190
Jin Ho, please head to the Voting Room.

1732
01:13:07,190 --> 01:13:08,320
Oh, the order changes.

1733
01:13:09,690 --> 01:13:11,330
Rooms B, C, D, and E!

1734
01:13:15,100 --> 01:13:16,160
B...

1735
01:13:18,400 --> 01:13:20,900
This is tough.

1736
01:13:21,870 --> 01:13:23,840
Please point to two cards.

1737
01:13:23,840 --> 01:13:24,910
Okay.

1738
01:13:30,440 --> 01:13:31,650
Are these cards new?

1739
01:13:33,280 --> 01:13:34,410
This one...

1740
01:13:36,580 --> 01:13:37,650
and this one.

1741
01:13:39,250 --> 01:13:41,090
Please choose one of the cards.

1742
01:13:41,490 --> 01:13:44,190
I'll go to Room F.

1743
01:13:44,190 --> 01:13:46,530
You have chosen Room F.

1744
01:13:47,160 --> 01:13:49,160
I put myself in the killer's shoes.

1745
01:13:49,260 --> 01:13:52,100
There are four options, B, C, D, and E.

1746
01:13:52,100 --> 01:13:54,970
I'd choose one of them
if I were the killer.

1747
01:13:54,970 --> 01:13:57,340
I was trying to hide in Room A or Room F,

1748
01:13:57,340 --> 01:13:59,410
where I thought the killer would rule out.

1749
01:13:59,410 --> 01:14:00,870
(Keun Woo)

1750
01:14:00,870 --> 01:14:02,140
You've chosen this card.

1751
01:14:02,340 --> 01:14:04,280
Ji Min, you've chosen this card.

1752
01:14:10,620 --> 01:14:12,320
Please point to two cards.

1753
01:14:19,090 --> 01:14:20,830
I'll pick these two.

1754
01:14:27,630 --> 01:14:29,340
Please choose one of the cards.

1755
01:14:32,110 --> 01:14:33,410
This is bad.

1756
01:14:40,750 --> 01:14:41,850
Room A.

1757
01:14:41,850 --> 01:14:42,850
(Beom chose Room A.)

1758
01:14:42,850 --> 01:14:45,350
Beom, you've chosen Room A.

1759
01:14:48,760 --> 01:14:54,560
(Xitsuh, the pickpocket,
enters the Voting Room.)

1760
01:14:54,630 --> 01:14:57,870
I'm in trouble.

1761
01:14:57,870 --> 01:15:00,370
- I'm in trouble.
- Xitsuh, please choose one of the cards.

1762
01:15:00,370 --> 01:15:01,470
I'm in trouble.

1763
01:15:01,470 --> 01:15:03,100
Steal a wallet or lose my life?

1764
01:15:06,710 --> 01:15:08,380
(Except for Room E,
which he chose in Round 1,)

1765
01:15:08,380 --> 01:15:11,350
(he can freely pick
from the rest of the rooms.)

1766
01:15:11,350 --> 01:15:14,980
The killer is likely
to enter Room D or Room E.

1767
01:15:14,980 --> 01:15:16,880
Ironically enough,

1768
01:15:16,880 --> 01:15:18,650
I also have to pick
between Rooms D and E...

1769
01:15:18,650 --> 01:15:19,750
to increase my chance.

1770
01:15:19,750 --> 01:15:21,390
I really can't go to Room B or Room C.

1771
01:15:21,390 --> 01:15:22,760
The chances of being alone with someone...

1772
01:15:22,760 --> 01:15:24,730
are practically zero.

1773
01:15:24,830 --> 01:15:26,160
On the other hand,

1774
01:15:26,330 --> 01:15:27,790
if I go to Room D or Room E,

1775
01:15:27,790 --> 01:15:30,960
I'm more likely to run into the killer.

1776
01:15:32,330 --> 01:15:33,530
This one. I'll choose to save my life.

1777
01:15:34,070 --> 01:15:37,100
Xitsuh, you've chosen Room C.

1778
01:15:37,100 --> 01:15:38,340
I wanted to save myself first.

1779
01:15:38,570 --> 01:15:40,510
So, I picked Room C.

1780
01:15:40,640 --> 01:15:43,410
I may fail in stealing here,

1781
01:15:43,540 --> 01:15:45,310
but I'll at least dodge the killer.

1782
01:15:45,310 --> 01:15:47,110
And I'm going to wait for my chance.

1783
01:15:47,780 --> 01:15:49,620
Please point to two cards.

1784
01:15:54,820 --> 01:15:57,930
(Outside the Voting Room in the meantime)

1785
01:15:59,360 --> 01:16:01,760
I can't tell when Ji Min is lying.

1786
01:16:02,260 --> 01:16:04,000
But there's that.

1787
01:16:04,230 --> 01:16:05,930
It's suspicious
if she can't answer a question...

1788
01:16:05,930 --> 01:16:06,930
which she's supposed to.

1789
01:16:06,930 --> 01:16:08,100
Like what? Give me an example.

1790
01:16:08,100 --> 01:16:09,900
For example, earlier...

1791
01:16:10,670 --> 01:16:13,070
I think Jin Ho is...

1792
01:16:13,810 --> 01:16:15,140
the follower.

1793
01:16:16,280 --> 01:16:18,580
Why? Whose guess is that?

1794
01:16:18,580 --> 01:16:20,110
- What?
- Whose guess is that?

1795
01:16:21,250 --> 01:16:22,950
I didn't ask them that.

1796
01:16:24,280 --> 01:16:25,820
It's just your intuition?

1797
01:16:28,660 --> 01:16:29,790
I feel scared to be dead.

1798
01:16:30,660 --> 01:16:33,760
If I were to say something like that
to someone,

1799
01:16:34,060 --> 01:16:36,530
I'd say, "He's not the pickpocket
for these reasons,"

1800
01:16:36,530 --> 01:16:37,530
- "so he must be the follower."
- Exactly.

1801
01:16:37,530 --> 01:16:38,800
Who said that to you?

1802
01:16:39,030 --> 01:16:40,470
- To me.
- Who did?

1803
01:16:40,470 --> 01:16:41,500
Ji Min did.

1804
01:16:41,800 --> 01:16:43,870
Ji Min kept saying to me...

1805
01:16:44,170 --> 01:16:46,270
that Jin Ho was the follower,
not the pickpocket.

1806
01:16:46,270 --> 01:16:48,940
So, I thought she might be the follower.

1807
01:16:48,940 --> 01:16:50,140
- Instead?
- Yes.

1808
01:16:50,740 --> 01:16:52,350
I thought she was framing him.

1809
01:16:53,210 --> 01:16:55,720
I'm not sure, though.
We can't be sure of anything yet.

1810
01:17:01,390 --> 01:17:03,420
(Ji Hoo's options are Rooms A and D.)

1811
01:17:03,420 --> 01:17:04,620
This one.

1812
01:17:04,620 --> 01:17:06,530
Ji Hoo, you've chosen this room.

1813
01:17:07,560 --> 01:17:08,900
(YunB,)

1814
01:17:08,900 --> 01:17:10,400
(Hye Seon,)

1815
01:17:10,400 --> 01:17:11,530
(and Seung Yong made their choices.)

1816
01:17:11,530 --> 01:17:12,630
I'll pick this one.

1817
01:17:12,630 --> 01:17:14,600
Seung Yong, you've chosen this room.

1818
01:17:21,040 --> 01:17:22,810
Please point to two cards.

1819
01:17:26,350 --> 01:17:27,780
Whatever. I'll pick these two.

1820
01:17:32,450 --> 01:17:33,920
(Seong Beom's options are Rooms A and F.)

1821
01:17:35,660 --> 01:17:37,490
Please choose one of the cards.

1822
01:17:37,490 --> 01:17:40,030
(Rooms A and F are the rooms they agreed
to leave out from Round 1.)

1823
01:17:40,030 --> 01:17:41,230
Are you serious?

1824
01:17:41,830 --> 01:17:44,400
There were six rooms
from Room A to Room F.

1825
01:17:44,400 --> 01:17:46,870
The likelihood
of picking Room A and Room F...

1826
01:17:47,130 --> 01:17:48,440
is less than ten percent.

1827
01:17:48,500 --> 01:17:50,600
It's a ridiculous possibility.

1828
01:17:51,100 --> 01:17:54,240
And I pulled that off.

1829
01:17:55,410 --> 01:17:58,950
I can't die.

1830
01:18:00,050 --> 01:18:02,350
But my role is too important to die.

1831
01:18:02,950 --> 01:18:04,180
I'm the psychic.

1832
01:18:04,750 --> 01:18:07,250
I knew my death would be terrible.

1833
01:18:07,390 --> 01:18:08,590
I'll pick Room A.

1834
01:18:08,990 --> 01:18:11,660
Seong Beom, you've chosen Room A.

1835
01:18:13,890 --> 01:18:16,630
Nighttime for Round Two has ended.

1836
01:18:23,400 --> 01:18:26,540
Please take off the blindfold
in your seat.

1837
01:18:28,980 --> 01:18:30,140
I'm so nervous.

1838
01:18:31,310 --> 01:18:33,680
Here's the result of last night.

1839
01:18:34,750 --> 01:18:35,850
Last night,

1840
01:18:43,090 --> 01:18:45,130
nothing happened.

1841
01:18:45,130 --> 01:18:46,330
(No one was murdered in Round 2.)

1842
01:18:46,330 --> 01:18:47,330
(Seong Beom exclaiming)

1843
01:18:47,330 --> 01:18:49,560
I narrowly escaped death.

1844
01:19:00,310 --> 01:19:01,340
Hello?

1845
01:19:02,080 --> 01:19:04,950
- Yes.
- Please tell me your name.

1846
01:19:04,980 --> 01:19:07,310
- Kwak Beom.
- Hyun Sung Joo.

1847
01:19:07,310 --> 01:19:08,320
Hong Jin Ho.

1848
01:19:08,550 --> 01:19:10,650
Jeong Keun Woo.

1849
01:19:10,720 --> 01:19:12,220
Choi Hye Seon.

1850
01:19:12,220 --> 01:19:14,990
You are the psychic.

1851
01:19:15,820 --> 01:19:18,090
You are the pickpocket.

1852
01:19:18,530 --> 01:19:21,230
Your burglary was...

1853
01:19:21,500 --> 01:19:22,760
successful last night.

1854
01:19:23,560 --> 01:19:24,830
Roger.

1855
01:19:24,830 --> 01:19:29,740
(Xitsuh pulled off his second burglary.)

1856
01:19:29,740 --> 01:19:31,100
That's insane. Okay.

1857
01:19:31,270 --> 01:19:32,310
At last,

1858
01:19:33,410 --> 01:19:35,410
I got lucky.

1859
01:19:35,580 --> 01:19:37,640
I pulled off two burglaries in a row...

1860
01:19:37,640 --> 01:19:40,010
even though I went to Room C.

1861
01:19:40,650 --> 01:19:42,280
But I thought
we were gathering in Rooms B and C.

1862
01:19:44,420 --> 01:19:46,990
Keun Woo, you've chosen Room C.

1863
01:19:47,290 --> 01:19:50,020
If I had been the killer,
I would have murdered two citizens.

1864
01:19:50,060 --> 01:19:51,990
The game would be practically over.

1865
01:19:52,290 --> 01:19:55,130
All I did was steal their wallets
because I was a pickpocket.

1866
01:19:55,430 --> 01:19:57,460
One more burglary,

1867
01:19:57,460 --> 01:19:59,470
and I accomplish my mission.

1868
01:19:59,630 --> 01:20:01,500
In that situation, I decided...

1869
01:20:01,500 --> 01:20:03,840
to find a way to finish the game
in Round Three.

1870
01:20:05,670 --> 01:20:09,640
(Round 3, Day Phase)

1871
01:20:09,640 --> 01:20:11,010
Where did you stay last night?

1872
01:20:13,210 --> 01:20:14,280
- What?
- Where did you stay?

1873
01:20:14,280 --> 01:20:15,950
I don't think I can tell you.

1874
01:20:15,950 --> 01:20:17,120
- Seriously?
- Yes.

1875
01:20:17,250 --> 01:20:19,450
- Ramada Hotel.
- Come on.

1876
01:20:19,450 --> 01:20:21,090
- What? Ramada Hotel.
- Which room?

1877
01:20:21,090 --> 01:20:22,090
Room 604.

1878
01:20:22,490 --> 01:20:25,190
- YunB, where did you stay?
- I think it was called Amanda Hotel.

1879
01:20:26,390 --> 01:20:28,630
- It turns out you're all villains.
- I...

1880
01:20:29,000 --> 01:20:31,670
There must be a psychopath
and a follower here.

1881
01:20:31,670 --> 01:20:32,770
I'm...

1882
01:20:33,470 --> 01:20:36,740
I feel like Beom is more like the killer.

1883
01:20:37,870 --> 01:20:39,810
You look like the psychopath.

1884
01:20:39,810 --> 01:20:41,440
Everyone says I'm the psychopath.

1885
01:20:42,610 --> 01:20:44,080
You don't want to share the information?

1886
01:20:44,080 --> 01:20:45,810
Should the three of us share? No?

1887
01:20:46,850 --> 01:20:47,980
Frankly speaking, I was in Room E.

1888
01:20:48,380 --> 01:20:49,450
I was in Room D.

1889
01:20:50,220 --> 01:20:51,720
- Room E? So was I.
- Yes.

1890
01:20:54,450 --> 01:20:56,090
My options were Rooms A and E.

1891
01:20:56,660 --> 01:20:59,060
We agreed not to pick Room A,
so I went to Room E.

1892
01:20:59,130 --> 01:21:01,390
- Which room were you in?
- What?

1893
01:21:02,000 --> 01:21:03,660
I'll tell you when everyone gathers.

1894
01:21:03,900 --> 01:21:05,270
But we shared our info.

1895
01:21:05,270 --> 01:21:06,300
- You did?
- Yes.

1896
01:21:06,300 --> 01:21:07,400
Room A.

1897
01:21:08,270 --> 01:21:10,340
- Room A? You went there?
- Yes.

1898
01:21:10,340 --> 01:21:11,340
What were your options?

1899
01:21:11,340 --> 01:21:12,340
Rooms A and F.

1900
01:21:12,340 --> 01:21:13,510
- Rooms A and F?
- Yes.

1901
01:21:15,440 --> 01:21:17,140
We'll talk when everyone gathers.

1902
01:21:20,080 --> 01:21:21,980
- Maybe I didn't pick one.
- I was actually in Room A.

1903
01:21:23,450 --> 01:21:24,520
What?

1904
01:21:25,690 --> 01:21:27,020
Why did you lie?

1905
01:21:27,620 --> 01:21:29,560
- Because he was there.
- What?

1906
01:21:29,560 --> 01:21:31,630
The one I'm most suspicious of was there.

1907
01:21:31,630 --> 01:21:32,890
Who's that?

1908
01:21:34,190 --> 01:21:36,030
- Sung Joo.
- Where were you?

1909
01:21:36,660 --> 01:21:37,800
Room E.

1910
01:21:37,800 --> 01:21:39,170
- You were in Room E?
- Yes.

1911
01:21:39,930 --> 01:21:42,240
What? Why would you lie about that?

1912
01:21:42,240 --> 01:21:44,670
What are you talking about? What lie?

1913
01:21:44,670 --> 01:21:46,540
- I just don't get it.
- You don't get what?

1914
01:21:47,210 --> 01:21:48,980
What did he lie about?

1915
01:21:48,980 --> 01:21:50,010
I'm in Room A.

1916
01:21:50,180 --> 01:21:51,440
- You were in Room A?
- Yes.

1917
01:21:51,710 --> 01:21:53,250
Which two cards did you pick?

1918
01:21:53,250 --> 01:21:54,310
A and E.

1919
01:21:54,310 --> 01:21:55,350
I was actually in Room A.

1920
01:21:55,680 --> 01:21:57,450
- Why would you do that?
- Why did you lie?

1921
01:21:58,320 --> 01:22:00,020
It happens, though.

1922
01:22:00,020 --> 01:22:03,120
That was all the information I had,

1923
01:22:03,120 --> 01:22:04,890
so I didn't want to reveal it...

1924
01:22:04,890 --> 01:22:06,230
when there were three people.

1925
01:22:06,430 --> 01:22:08,360
Why did you choose Room A between A and E?

1926
01:22:08,360 --> 01:22:10,900
I thought I could die in Room E.

1927
01:22:11,400 --> 01:22:12,500
So, I gave it a twist.

1928
01:22:14,630 --> 01:22:17,940
Were they supposed to meet somewhere?

1929
01:22:17,940 --> 01:22:18,940
You know,

1930
01:22:19,970 --> 01:22:21,780
I'm not sure if it means anything,

1931
01:22:21,780 --> 01:22:24,480
but I asked her what room she chose...

1932
01:22:24,480 --> 01:22:26,150
to sound her out.

1933
01:22:26,550 --> 01:22:28,180
And she hesitated for so long.

1934
01:22:30,420 --> 01:22:31,450
Which room were you in?

1935
01:22:32,420 --> 01:22:33,950
- Which room? My room?
- Yes.

1936
01:22:35,160 --> 01:22:37,060
- Oh, me?
- Yes, your room.

1937
01:22:40,930 --> 01:22:41,930
C?

1938
01:22:41,960 --> 01:22:44,760
No, I'll say it
in front of everyone downstairs.

1939
01:22:45,800 --> 01:22:48,500
- Okay. Hurry up.
- Everyone... Hey, Seong Beom.

1940
01:22:49,500 --> 01:22:50,670
- I won't tell.
- Don't tell anyone.

1941
01:22:50,670 --> 01:22:51,670
Okay.

1942
01:22:52,070 --> 01:22:53,810
"Room B? No, it was C."

1943
01:22:53,810 --> 01:22:56,580
She was trying to evade the question.

1944
01:22:56,580 --> 01:22:58,810
But it was a room that she picked.

1945
01:22:58,810 --> 01:22:59,910
And she told me,

1946
01:22:59,910 --> 01:23:03,080
"Don't tell anyone.
I'll say it in front of everyone."

1947
01:23:03,080 --> 01:23:04,720
"Wait until I go downstairs."

1948
01:23:04,720 --> 01:23:06,590
So, I was like,

1949
01:23:07,450 --> 01:23:08,520
"That's so suspicious."

1950
01:23:09,060 --> 01:23:11,690
Is there any reason
why she shouldn't talk about that?

1951
01:23:11,960 --> 01:23:14,460
There's no such reason.

1952
01:23:15,100 --> 01:23:17,130
But I also hesitated earlier.

1953
01:23:17,530 --> 01:23:19,470
I pointed to Rooms A and E,

1954
01:23:19,470 --> 01:23:21,130
and I thought the killer might come
to Room E.

1955
01:23:21,130 --> 01:23:23,200
That was why I went into Room A
for a switch.

1956
01:23:23,700 --> 01:23:25,870
I was with Sung Joo and YunB earlier.

1957
01:23:25,870 --> 01:23:27,240
We asked each other to reveal our cards,

1958
01:23:27,240 --> 01:23:29,140
but I couldn't do that.
That was why I lied.

1959
01:23:29,340 --> 01:23:31,080
Wasn't that why she did that?

1960
01:23:31,340 --> 01:23:33,450
That could be it. I'm not quite sure.

1961
01:23:34,010 --> 01:23:36,620
I'm not sure.
I'm starting to feel the sixth sense.

1962
01:23:36,620 --> 01:23:38,620
Isn't it because
Ji Min is being so suspicious?

1963
01:23:38,620 --> 01:23:39,620
- Right.
- Right.

1964
01:23:39,690 --> 01:23:42,520
I'm certain that it's not you.

1965
01:23:42,520 --> 01:23:44,660
- Right.
- You ran out first...

1966
01:23:44,660 --> 01:23:45,830
- to buy the get-out-of-jail card.
- Right.

1967
01:23:45,830 --> 01:23:48,030
So you're certainly not the killer...

1968
01:23:48,160 --> 01:23:50,030
- or the follower.
- Right.

1969
01:23:50,130 --> 01:23:51,330
Gosh, who is it over there?

1970
01:23:52,070 --> 01:23:53,630
Anyway, I didn't think
there was a reason...

1971
01:23:53,630 --> 01:23:55,340
for you to run out
if you were from the killer faction.

1972
01:23:55,500 --> 01:23:56,940
- I might be wrong.
- Right.

1973
01:23:56,940 --> 01:24:00,840
Anyway, Seong Beom thinks
you are meeting YunB quite often,

1974
01:24:00,840 --> 01:24:02,480
who he finds suspicious.

1975
01:24:02,480 --> 01:24:04,280
That is why he finds you
to be suspicious as well.

1976
01:24:04,280 --> 01:24:05,550
He thinks YunB is suspicious?

1977
01:24:05,680 --> 01:24:07,550
- I find him to be suspicious as well.
- Really?

1978
01:24:08,820 --> 01:24:11,950
I was told that I was spotted
having a secret conversation with YunB.

1979
01:24:12,150 --> 01:24:14,550
"Go to Room A. Go to Room F."

1980
01:24:14,690 --> 01:24:15,920
That was the only thing
we said to each other...

1981
01:24:15,920 --> 01:24:18,360
and that made me look suspicious.

1982
01:24:19,230 --> 01:24:20,290
Where must I go?

1983
01:24:22,600 --> 01:24:24,530
I think this is all based on luck.

1984
01:24:24,530 --> 01:24:26,170
I think Room B or Room C will be better.

1985
01:24:27,530 --> 01:24:30,670
I thought that there was some sort
of filter...

1986
01:24:31,040 --> 01:24:33,310
applied to these people's eyes.

1987
01:24:37,110 --> 01:24:38,780
- Where did Xitsuh go?
- Where's Xitsuh?

1988
01:24:38,880 --> 01:24:40,980
- I'm right here.
- No. I'm talking about your room.

1989
01:24:41,850 --> 01:24:43,880
I'm going to reveal it
in front of everyone.

1990
01:24:44,350 --> 01:24:46,220
I can't tell Jin Ho,
the one I can't trust.

1991
01:24:46,820 --> 01:24:48,290
I'm harmless.

1992
01:24:50,320 --> 01:24:51,990
What are you? Tell me even if it's a lie.

1993
01:24:52,890 --> 01:24:54,030
Are you from the killers?

1994
01:24:54,560 --> 01:24:56,430
What? No. I'm a pickpocket.

1995
01:24:58,300 --> 01:24:59,500
Are you a dirty cop?

1996
01:25:02,770 --> 01:25:04,470
I love it when people get together.

1997
01:25:05,070 --> 01:25:06,240
Stop lying.

1998
01:25:07,840 --> 01:25:09,140
I'm a pickpocket.

1999
01:25:10,510 --> 01:25:12,610
- You're a pickpocket?
- Speak quietly, will you?

2000
01:25:14,880 --> 01:25:17,880
I'll help you with anything
you need help with from now on.

2001
01:25:19,050 --> 01:25:20,450
If you're a dirty cop or follower,

2002
01:25:20,450 --> 01:25:21,890
don't arrest me.

2003
01:25:21,890 --> 01:25:23,090
I'm of no use anyway.

2004
01:25:24,020 --> 01:25:27,460
If I make another successful burglary,

2005
01:25:27,460 --> 01:25:28,600
I complete the winning condition.

2006
01:25:28,600 --> 01:25:29,830
The scariest thing for me is,

2007
01:25:30,660 --> 01:25:32,870
"What if a dirty cop arrests me?"

2008
01:25:33,030 --> 01:25:36,470
That was why I decided to approach Jin Ho.

2009
01:25:36,940 --> 01:25:39,640
I wanted him not to arrest me...

2010
01:25:40,210 --> 01:25:41,470
until I complete my mission.

2011
01:25:42,010 --> 01:25:43,210
I even got...

2012
01:25:44,440 --> 01:25:45,750
Rooms A and E.

2013
01:25:46,310 --> 01:25:47,580
According to our plan,

2014
01:25:47,580 --> 01:25:49,180
- I have to go to Room E.
- Right.

2015
01:25:49,180 --> 01:25:51,280
But I couldn't go as I was afraid
someone would kill me.

2016
01:25:52,090 --> 01:25:53,950
- But Xitsuh already sorted things out.
- Right.

2017
01:25:58,360 --> 01:26:01,860
There were three people
who were really suspicious.

2018
01:26:02,330 --> 01:26:05,300
YunB, who was against
Seung Yong's strategy.

2019
01:26:05,500 --> 01:26:07,970
Beom felt different
from how he was up until now.

2020
01:26:08,230 --> 01:26:12,210
I kept feeling bothered
about Ji Min as well.

2021
01:26:12,840 --> 01:26:14,510
She looked really unnatural.

2022
01:26:14,810 --> 01:26:16,380
"While avoiding these three people,"

2023
01:26:17,010 --> 01:26:18,710
"what must I do during this round..."

2024
01:26:19,480 --> 01:26:22,020
"to complete the third burglary?"

2025
01:26:22,120 --> 01:26:23,850
- There was a fear of that.
- Right.

2026
01:26:23,850 --> 01:26:25,220
The one from the devil's side
should move away for a while.

2027
01:26:25,290 --> 01:26:26,590
I'm sorry, but I'm not a devil.

2028
01:26:26,590 --> 01:26:27,790
- I'm neutral.
- Right.

2029
01:26:27,790 --> 01:26:29,890
Do you know who has
the get-out-of-jail card?

2030
01:26:30,290 --> 01:26:31,660
- Do you know them?
- Yes.

2031
01:26:31,820 --> 01:26:34,690
What I know is
that Jin Ho and Sung Joo have it.

2032
01:26:34,690 --> 01:26:36,230
I'm not so sure about the other one.

2033
01:26:36,460 --> 01:26:37,760
Sung Joo has a get-out-of-jail card?

2034
01:26:39,030 --> 01:26:40,830
I heard that
Sung Joo bought the get-out-of-jail card.

2035
01:26:41,530 --> 01:26:44,200
Hey, Sung Joo is right here.
Why would you ask him?

2036
01:26:45,100 --> 01:26:47,210
- You won't tell me.
- I won't.

2037
01:26:47,210 --> 01:26:48,940
- What's with you?
- Well,

2038
01:26:48,940 --> 01:26:50,180
there's no benefit to me in revealing it.

2039
01:26:50,280 --> 01:26:52,150
The ones with the get-out-of-jail card...

2040
01:26:52,210 --> 01:26:54,780
are Sung Joo, Ji Min, and Jin Ho?

2041
01:26:55,320 --> 01:26:56,320
- Then...
- No.

2042
01:26:56,320 --> 01:26:57,320
- No?
- It's me.

2043
01:26:57,320 --> 01:26:58,790
- Right. Seong Beom.
- Oh, really?

2044
01:26:58,790 --> 01:27:00,150
- Why do you ask?
- What about the room selection ticket?

2045
01:27:00,290 --> 01:27:01,450
- What?
- The room selection ticket.

2046
01:27:01,450 --> 01:27:03,320
Ji Min and I each have one.

2047
01:27:03,420 --> 01:27:04,820
I'm not sure who has the other one.

2048
01:27:04,820 --> 01:27:06,260
- Really?
- Right.

2049
01:27:07,090 --> 01:27:08,800
I asked around...

2050
01:27:08,800 --> 01:27:10,830
to find out
who had the room selection tickets.

2051
01:27:11,260 --> 01:27:12,630
I wanted to secretly meet the one...

2052
01:27:12,800 --> 01:27:15,130
with the room selection ticket.

2053
01:27:15,230 --> 01:27:16,370
Come out.

2054
01:27:20,710 --> 01:27:23,310
You and Ji Min bought
room selection tickets?

2055
01:27:24,010 --> 01:27:26,080
Ji Min bought both the selection ticket
and a get-out-of-jail card.

2056
01:27:26,710 --> 01:27:28,050
Ji Min is strange.

2057
01:27:28,310 --> 01:27:30,720
Wouldn't a killer not buy
the room selection ticket?

2058
01:27:30,850 --> 01:27:31,990
Well,

2059
01:27:31,990 --> 01:27:35,860
the one who I was certain about
from the start was Tae Gyun.

2060
01:27:35,990 --> 01:27:37,090
The next one was YunB.

2061
01:27:37,090 --> 01:27:39,630
It was because YunB wanted to stop
with the strategy...

2062
01:27:39,630 --> 01:27:42,130
of closing down Room A and Room F.

2063
01:27:42,130 --> 01:27:43,330
- Right.
- I asked why...

2064
01:27:43,330 --> 01:27:45,630
and he said it was a bad strategy
as Rooms C and D each had one person.

2065
01:27:45,870 --> 01:27:47,230
They were both suspicious...

2066
01:27:47,230 --> 01:27:50,300
and the one who met up with them the most
was Ji Min.

2067
01:27:52,240 --> 01:27:53,510
Look over there!

2068
01:27:53,510 --> 01:27:55,010
Tae Gyun and Ji Min are stuck together.

2069
01:27:55,580 --> 01:27:59,250
- There were some fingerprints found.
- Right.

2070
01:27:59,680 --> 01:28:02,880
There was a way to signal each other.

2071
01:28:04,620 --> 01:28:05,850
Ji Min felt like...

2072
01:28:07,020 --> 01:28:09,220
she was going to kill me in the same room.

2073
01:28:09,220 --> 01:28:11,560
"But why did she buy
the room selection ticket as a killer?"

2074
01:28:12,130 --> 01:28:14,730
I left her out
because I felt so suspicious about her.

2075
01:28:15,360 --> 01:28:19,330
I tried to talk things out
with Seong Beom who was my P3 teammate.

2076
01:28:19,970 --> 01:28:21,570
What do you want to talk about?

2077
01:28:22,200 --> 01:28:23,340
Your occupation?

2078
01:28:23,340 --> 01:28:24,500
I'm going to reveal my occupation.

2079
01:28:24,970 --> 01:28:26,940
- Just me or everyone?
- Just you.

2080
01:28:27,510 --> 01:28:28,980
- Let's reveal it at the same time.
- Right.

2081
01:28:29,180 --> 01:28:30,540
Say it at the count of three.

2082
01:28:30,540 --> 01:28:32,410
The one who doesn't speak will have
to give up 90,000 dollars.

2083
01:28:34,380 --> 01:28:35,480
- Pickpocket.
- Psychic.

2084
01:28:36,150 --> 01:28:38,550
- You're a pickpocket?
- That was why I was messing with Jin Ho.

2085
01:28:38,850 --> 01:28:40,020
I'm a psychic.

2086
01:28:40,650 --> 01:28:42,920
I'm completely neutral
as I'm a pickpocket.

2087
01:28:42,920 --> 01:28:43,960
Right.

2088
01:28:46,130 --> 01:28:47,990
- At most...
- My goal is to get into a room...

2089
01:28:47,990 --> 01:28:50,130
with someone I can trust
as soon as possible.

2090
01:28:50,130 --> 01:28:51,500
- So what you want is my help.
- If you help me...

2091
01:28:51,500 --> 01:28:53,400
Right. I'm asking if you can help me out
at least once.

2092
01:28:53,400 --> 01:28:55,400
To be honest,
that will be safe for you as well.

2093
01:28:55,400 --> 01:28:56,970
- Right.
- I'm putting my body on the line.

2094
01:28:57,270 --> 01:28:58,640
Then, what's Jin Ho?

2095
01:28:59,140 --> 01:29:00,870
- That's what I'm saying.
- What is he?

2096
01:29:01,640 --> 01:29:03,440
What got me confused was...

2097
01:29:03,440 --> 01:29:05,650
why Jin Ho made that play.

2098
01:29:05,750 --> 01:29:08,080
Did he really make that play
because he was a follower?

2099
01:29:08,210 --> 01:29:09,780
So this is what we'll do
when we go back inside.

2100
01:29:09,780 --> 01:29:11,880
We'll plan out a strategy
to leave out Room A and Room F.

2101
01:29:12,020 --> 01:29:13,550
Come into Room A or Room F
with me after that.

2102
01:29:13,690 --> 01:29:15,420
I'll do that if you won't kill me.

2103
01:29:15,420 --> 01:29:16,690
Whisper this to Hye Seon.

2104
01:29:17,020 --> 01:29:18,160
"If I die this round,"

2105
01:29:18,160 --> 01:29:19,330
- "Xitsuh is the killer."
- "Xitsuh is the killer?"

2106
01:29:19,330 --> 01:29:21,260
- That's what you can do.
- Okay.

2107
01:29:21,260 --> 01:29:23,330
- Let's choose a room now.
- Sure.

2108
01:29:23,460 --> 01:29:24,760
- Let's go to Room F.
- Let's choose now.

2109
01:29:24,760 --> 01:29:26,200
- Let's go to Room F.
- Will you be okay with Room F?

2110
01:29:26,530 --> 01:29:28,030
Let's go to Room F.
But we must go inside...

2111
01:29:28,030 --> 01:29:29,340
and shout together
that we should leave Room A and F out.

2112
01:29:29,340 --> 01:29:30,870
- That's right even for the citizens.
- Right.

2113
01:29:30,870 --> 01:29:31,870
- That's right.
- After that...

2114
01:29:31,870 --> 01:29:34,470
"If you help me,
I will be on the citizens' side."

2115
01:29:34,740 --> 01:29:36,380
I told Seong Beom
to use the room selection ticket...

2116
01:29:36,380 --> 01:29:37,410
and come to Room F.

2117
01:29:37,640 --> 01:29:39,850
Seong Beom definitely would've
felt cautious about it.

2118
01:29:39,850 --> 01:29:40,850
"What if you're a killer?"

2119
01:29:40,850 --> 01:29:43,720
That was when I thought that we should
set a witness for both of us.

2120
01:29:44,080 --> 01:29:46,850
Seong Beom will tell you this.
I'll also tell you this in advance.

2121
01:29:46,990 --> 01:29:49,020
If Seong Beom dies tonight, suspect me.

2122
01:29:49,120 --> 01:29:50,890
If Seong Beom dies tonight, suspect me.

2123
01:29:51,260 --> 01:29:52,730
I just told her. You tell her as well.

2124
01:29:53,660 --> 01:29:55,630
Are you two suspecting each other?

2125
01:29:56,200 --> 01:29:59,170
No. That's not it.
I just wanted to make things clear.

2126
01:29:59,170 --> 01:30:00,970
Otherwise, if I die,
he's the one you should suspect.

2127
01:30:01,530 --> 01:30:05,200
- Are you two going to the same room?
- The room selection will begin now.

2128
01:30:06,070 --> 01:30:08,880
Please enter the Voting Room
when your name is called.

2129
01:30:09,740 --> 01:30:11,680
We're sticking to the strategy
of leaving out Room A and Room F, right?

2130
01:30:11,680 --> 01:30:13,280
The previous round
was just a happening, right?

2131
01:30:13,650 --> 01:30:15,880
- We'll stick to it.
- We'll stick to leaving those two out.

2132
01:30:15,880 --> 01:30:17,380
- It's B, C, D, or E.
- Right.

2133
01:30:17,380 --> 01:30:18,580
- Just as we planned.
- Right.

2134
01:30:18,580 --> 01:30:19,950
- Just B, C, D, or E.
- Right.

2135
01:30:19,950 --> 01:30:21,790
Let's be certain about this.
Just B, C, D, or E.

2136
01:30:22,320 --> 01:30:24,060
- Pray to your ancestors before you go.
- Right.

2137
01:30:24,390 --> 01:30:26,060
Seong Beom said if he dies,

2138
01:30:26,060 --> 01:30:27,760
Xitsuh is the killer.

2139
01:30:27,960 --> 01:30:29,630
Xitsuh said the same thing.

2140
01:30:29,630 --> 01:30:31,630
If he dies, Seong Beom is the killer.

2141
01:30:31,630 --> 01:30:32,630
- Why is that?
- I don't know.

2142
01:30:32,630 --> 01:30:34,170
The two must be wanting
to enter the same room.

2143
01:30:34,170 --> 01:30:35,430
(The witness tells Tae Gyun everything.)

2144
01:30:35,430 --> 01:30:36,570
Just the two of them.

2145
01:30:37,700 --> 01:30:39,970
That's what I think.
I have no idea why, though.

2146
01:30:41,470 --> 01:30:43,680
- Where did that conversation come from?
- What conversation?

2147
01:30:44,210 --> 01:30:46,010
Are you two trying to enter the same room?

2148
01:30:46,010 --> 01:30:47,510
Don't tell anyone!

2149
01:30:47,510 --> 01:30:48,880
Don't tell anyone!

2150
01:30:48,880 --> 01:30:50,550
There's someone I really trust.

2151
01:30:51,120 --> 01:30:52,250
I'm certain about that person.

2152
01:30:52,250 --> 01:30:53,720
- Did you tell that person?
- Yes.

2153
01:30:53,950 --> 01:30:55,760
- Gosh!
- What's wrong?

2154
01:30:55,860 --> 01:30:58,490
You should tell me the reason then.

2155
01:30:59,090 --> 01:31:01,660
- I said not to tell anyone!
- We can tell you in the next round!

2156
01:31:01,660 --> 01:31:03,130
We can tell you in the next round!

2157
01:31:03,130 --> 01:31:04,630
- Gosh!
- There's always the next round.

2158
01:31:08,770 --> 01:31:10,070
- Earlier?
- What's going on?

2159
01:31:10,070 --> 01:31:11,270
My gosh.

2160
01:31:11,270 --> 01:31:12,570
I still don't get it. What's going on?

2161
01:31:17,780 --> 01:31:18,980
Is that Tae Gyun?

2162
01:31:20,210 --> 01:31:21,510
Tae Gyun is the one you're talking about.

2163
01:31:22,220 --> 01:31:23,320
Right.

2164
01:31:23,980 --> 01:31:25,480
Tae Gyun is the one you trust?

2165
01:31:28,550 --> 01:31:30,320
- Yes.
- Why?

2166
01:31:32,020 --> 01:31:33,330
When we answered the call,

2167
01:31:33,330 --> 01:31:35,660
there were the first two lines
from the call.

2168
01:31:35,660 --> 01:31:36,960
And he said the same thing.

2169
01:31:37,400 --> 01:31:39,330
- I also have an occupation.
- Right.

2170
01:31:39,330 --> 01:31:40,570
- But...
- I have one as well.

2171
01:31:40,970 --> 01:31:42,440
- Do you get calls?
- Yes.

2172
01:31:42,440 --> 01:31:43,540
What do they ask you?

2173
01:31:43,540 --> 01:31:45,140
- "Please tell me your name."
- What next?

2174
01:31:45,570 --> 01:31:47,910
"There's no information to be shared."
And the call ended.

2175
01:31:48,110 --> 01:31:50,640
Same here. I think I can trust you.

2176
01:31:50,640 --> 01:31:52,650
It was the same for me. I also get calls.

2177
01:31:52,780 --> 01:31:53,810
I also didn't have any information
that could be shared with me.

2178
01:31:53,810 --> 01:31:54,850
- That was why I asked.
- Right.

2179
01:31:54,850 --> 01:31:56,550
- We got the same call.
- Right.

2180
01:31:56,550 --> 01:31:57,780
- That was why I asked.
- Right.

2181
01:32:00,450 --> 01:32:03,790
The same things were said during the call.

2182
01:32:04,260 --> 01:32:07,330
That doesn't mean we can be certain
that he's a citizen.

2183
01:32:07,330 --> 01:32:10,260
Does it mean he's a killer
if he doesn't get the same call?

2184
01:32:10,800 --> 01:32:12,500
- Right.
- Why is that? Who said that?

2185
01:32:13,930 --> 01:32:15,030
Isn't it how it is?

2186
01:32:18,500 --> 01:32:19,610
Did you watch "The Chaser?"

2187
01:32:19,610 --> 01:32:21,110
There's a lady at the corner store.

2188
01:32:21,440 --> 01:32:23,140
"That lady is right here."

2189
01:32:24,140 --> 01:32:25,440
While I'm hiding in the room...

2190
01:32:25,580 --> 01:32:27,280
"Seong Beom is right here."

2191
01:32:27,280 --> 01:32:29,050
"Stay right here without leaving."

2192
01:32:29,950 --> 01:32:32,990
It just drove me crazy. Gosh.

2193
01:32:33,450 --> 01:32:35,890
The information was being delivered...

2194
01:32:35,890 --> 01:32:37,620
to the ones I was suspecting.

2195
01:32:39,790 --> 01:32:41,230
Has anyone talked with Ji Min?

2196
01:32:43,660 --> 01:32:44,730
No one?

2197
01:32:47,400 --> 01:32:48,830
She only talks with Tae Gyun.

2198
01:32:49,700 --> 01:32:50,800
Why is that?

2199
01:32:51,200 --> 01:32:53,310
She only talks with Tae Gyun and Keun Woo.

2200
01:32:53,310 --> 01:32:54,340
Why is that?

2201
01:32:54,340 --> 01:32:56,540
I talk with them as well.
They also let me join in.

2202
01:32:56,540 --> 01:32:58,140
What are you doing over there?

2203
01:32:58,380 --> 01:32:59,450
Gosh!

2204
01:33:02,050 --> 01:33:04,080
Xitsuh, please head to the Voting Room.

2205
01:33:11,090 --> 01:33:14,330
Xitsuh, you have chosen Room F.

2206
01:33:14,890 --> 01:33:17,060
I chose Room F without hesitation...

2207
01:33:17,760 --> 01:33:19,170
while waiting for Seong Beom.

2208
01:33:21,930 --> 01:33:25,770
(Seong Beom decided to choose Room F
with his room selection ticket.)

2209
01:33:26,910 --> 01:33:28,540
Please point to two cards.

2210
01:33:34,210 --> 01:33:36,150
I suddenly got this thought.

2211
01:33:37,280 --> 01:33:39,390
"Why must I use
the room selection ticket?"

2212
01:33:39,850 --> 01:33:42,220
I picked A and F in the previous round.

2213
01:33:42,390 --> 01:33:44,960
I looked at the patterns
on the back of the cards under the lights.

2214
01:33:45,190 --> 01:33:46,330
"I wonder what these two are."

2215
01:33:46,330 --> 01:33:48,530
I picked the ones
with specific patterns...

2216
01:33:48,790 --> 01:33:50,530
and they were A and F.

2217
01:33:50,760 --> 01:33:53,300
"If I pick A and F again,"

2218
01:33:53,470 --> 01:33:55,070
"can't I save my room selection ticket..."

2219
01:33:55,070 --> 01:33:56,570
"and enter Room F?"

2220
01:33:58,670 --> 01:33:59,740
This is it.

2221
01:34:00,640 --> 01:34:01,970
Please flip these two cards.

2222
01:34:08,480 --> 01:34:09,550
I'm doomed.

2223
01:34:11,450 --> 01:34:12,520
"Gosh!"

2224
01:34:12,690 --> 01:34:14,690
The cards turned out to be A and B.

2225
01:34:15,450 --> 01:34:17,090
"What happened?"

2226
01:34:18,960 --> 01:34:20,630
The worst-case-scenario at this point...

2227
01:34:21,060 --> 01:34:23,400
is for me to get killed
in Room A or Room B.

2228
01:34:23,530 --> 01:34:26,200
Or if Xitsuh gets killed
by the killer in Room F,

2229
01:34:26,800 --> 01:34:29,770
I would do something terrible against him.

2230
01:34:30,100 --> 01:34:31,800
(Xitsuh is kept separated
without knowing anything.)

2231
01:34:31,800 --> 01:34:32,940
Please!

2232
01:34:33,840 --> 01:34:34,870
Please!

2233
01:34:38,480 --> 01:34:39,480
Please!

2234
01:34:40,350 --> 01:34:42,480
It wasn't this? Why?

2235
01:34:43,520 --> 01:34:44,850
Why?

2236
01:34:46,690 --> 01:34:49,320
Heo Seong Beom,
Please choose one of the cards.

2237
01:34:49,320 --> 01:34:51,160
- I'll choose Room B.
- Heo Seong Beom,

2238
01:34:51,720 --> 01:34:53,630
- you have chosen Room B.
- Right.

2239
01:34:57,000 --> 01:34:58,160
Hello.

2240
01:35:00,700 --> 01:35:03,740
Hong Jin Ho, please point to two cards.

2241
01:35:07,140 --> 01:35:09,740
The room selection
for Round Three has ended.

2242
01:35:10,410 --> 01:35:13,380
Please take off the blindfold
in your seat.

2243
01:35:15,850 --> 01:35:17,280
Please.

2244
01:35:19,050 --> 01:35:20,750
I don't care if anyone else dies.
I just have to survive.

2245
01:35:22,660 --> 01:35:24,920
Here's the result of last night.

2246
01:35:25,930 --> 01:35:26,990
Last night,

2247
01:35:26,990 --> 01:35:29,160
(Last night)

2248
01:35:29,160 --> 01:35:31,030
nothing happened.

2249
01:35:32,770 --> 01:35:34,970
(Round 3: No murders)

2250
01:35:34,970 --> 01:35:36,940
Nothing happened.

2251
01:35:37,270 --> 01:35:38,340
Okay.

2252
01:35:41,510 --> 01:35:42,580
Hello?

2253
01:35:43,210 --> 01:35:45,210
Please tell me your name.

2254
01:35:45,210 --> 01:35:46,480
I'm Xitsuh.

2255
01:35:47,850 --> 01:35:51,420
Your burglary was successful last night.

2256
01:35:51,650 --> 01:35:53,890
- Have you confirmed it?
- Yes. I have.

2257
01:35:53,890 --> 01:35:55,120
(He manages to reach
the pickpocket win condition...)

2258
01:35:55,120 --> 01:35:56,120
(with 3 successful burglaries.)

2259
01:35:58,260 --> 01:35:59,830
It's over. Okay.

2260
01:36:01,790 --> 01:36:03,700
"Your burglary was successful last night."

2261
01:36:03,700 --> 01:36:05,760
As soon as I heard that,
I almost screamed.

2262
01:36:07,270 --> 01:36:08,730
For three rounds,

2263
01:36:09,370 --> 01:36:13,010
I was with 1 other person
for 3 consecutive times.

2264
01:36:13,540 --> 01:36:14,970
It's really hard for this to happen.

2265
01:36:15,270 --> 01:36:17,840
The game would be over
if I were the killer.

2266
01:36:18,210 --> 01:36:22,050
The game would've ended
after three "kills."

2267
01:36:23,350 --> 01:36:24,950
Seong Beom is the best.

2268
01:36:25,720 --> 01:36:26,990
I want to give him a hug.

2269
01:36:28,820 --> 01:36:32,320
Now is the time for me to find a way
to quickly end the game.

2270
01:36:33,730 --> 01:36:36,830
Last night, Room B was occupied
by four people.

2271
01:36:37,330 --> 01:36:39,530
- Have you confirmed it?
- Yes. I have.

2272
01:36:42,540 --> 01:36:44,570
Did you make it with the burglary?

2273
01:36:44,570 --> 01:36:45,970
- Yes.
- What?

2274
01:36:46,670 --> 01:36:48,040
- You must know if you're a psychic.
- What?

2275
01:36:48,040 --> 01:36:49,610
You must know
that there was one other than you.

2276
01:36:51,440 --> 01:36:54,650
This was what was hilarious.
I had to use the item,

2277
01:36:55,050 --> 01:36:57,320
but I was told that I couldn't use it
after flipping the cards.

2278
01:36:57,480 --> 01:36:59,850
I flipped the cards, and F didn't appear.

2279
01:37:00,150 --> 01:37:03,420
I said I was doomed and chose B.

2280
01:37:03,420 --> 01:37:05,260
You made it because I didn't go.

2281
01:37:05,260 --> 01:37:06,290
Really?

2282
01:37:06,490 --> 01:37:10,500
Seong Beom suddenly said
he failed to use the item.

2283
01:37:11,060 --> 01:37:15,130
"What? How can a smart guy like him
fail to use the item?"

2284
01:37:15,330 --> 01:37:16,570
It didn't make sense.

2285
01:37:17,870 --> 01:37:20,340
- Stop lying. Are you serious?
- Shush. Let's talk later.

2286
01:37:21,110 --> 01:37:22,880
- Shall we share what we've got first?
- But...

2287
01:37:23,240 --> 01:37:24,280
Yes.

2288
01:37:24,580 --> 01:37:25,950
- A, 0.
- A, 0.

2289
01:37:25,950 --> 01:37:29,650
B, 4. C, 5. D, 2.

2290
01:37:29,950 --> 01:37:31,850
E, 0. F, 1.

2291
01:37:33,250 --> 01:37:34,790
That was when I felt goosebumps.

2292
01:37:35,420 --> 01:37:36,960
"Who was I with, then?"

2293
01:37:37,520 --> 01:37:39,390
Let's share the information that we have.

2294
01:37:39,560 --> 01:37:40,960
What are you talking about
with Seong Beom?

2295
01:37:40,960 --> 01:37:43,060
You must know which side
he is on right now.

2296
01:37:43,060 --> 01:37:44,930
Seong Beom had a room selection ticket,

2297
01:37:44,930 --> 01:37:46,670
so we were planning
to go into the same room.

2298
01:37:46,670 --> 01:37:47,870
But Seong Beom said...

2299
01:37:48,470 --> 01:37:50,340
he failed to use the item.

2300
01:37:50,340 --> 01:37:51,870
- Why is that?
- Because he flipped the cards first.

2301
01:37:51,870 --> 01:37:52,940
I see.

2302
01:37:52,940 --> 01:37:55,570
But what's funny is
that my burglary was successful.

2303
01:37:56,280 --> 01:37:57,780
They said I was the only one in Room F.

2304
01:37:58,610 --> 01:38:00,180
- It was successful?
- Someone is lying right now.

2305
01:38:00,180 --> 01:38:01,380
It's certain that someone is lying.

2306
01:38:01,380 --> 01:38:03,020
- It doesn't make sense.
- Then...

2307
01:38:03,020 --> 01:38:04,320
- I didn't die.
- Right.

2308
01:38:04,550 --> 01:38:06,590
The one who came to Room F was a citizen.

2309
01:38:07,150 --> 01:38:09,760
No. It could've been a follower
or dirty cop.

2310
01:38:09,920 --> 01:38:11,160
- Right.
- Right.

2311
01:38:11,960 --> 01:38:13,430
It was quite funny.

2312
01:38:13,530 --> 01:38:15,430
He didn't know who I was
even though I lied.

2313
01:38:16,360 --> 01:38:19,500
(Round 3 room selection)

2314
01:38:20,400 --> 01:38:22,840
I'll go to Room F.

2315
01:38:23,140 --> 01:38:24,200
Hong Jin Ho,

2316
01:38:24,400 --> 01:38:26,410
- you have chosen Room F.
- Right.

2317
01:38:26,840 --> 01:38:28,570
- Room F.
- Room F?

2318
01:38:29,810 --> 01:38:31,010
- Jin Ho.
- Room C.

2319
01:38:31,010 --> 01:38:32,140
(He lied that he was in Room C.)

2320
01:38:32,340 --> 01:38:34,080
Xitsuh was lucky...

2321
01:38:34,410 --> 01:38:37,150
to make three successful burglaries
right from the start.

2322
01:38:37,280 --> 01:38:40,320
So you don't know which side
Seong Beom is on yet?

2323
01:38:40,590 --> 01:38:42,120
This is what I find suspicious.

2324
01:38:42,120 --> 01:38:43,460
A smart guy like him
said he failed to use...

2325
01:38:43,460 --> 01:38:45,390
- the room selection ticket.
- Right.

2326
01:38:45,390 --> 01:38:47,090
- As a result, my burglary was successful.
- Right.

2327
01:38:47,230 --> 01:38:48,630
He said he couldn't make it to Room F.

2328
01:38:49,030 --> 01:38:50,960
- So...
- Why did you two try to be...

2329
01:38:50,960 --> 01:38:52,100
in the same room
after using the room selection ticket?

2330
01:38:52,430 --> 01:38:53,870
That way, my burglary becomes successful.

2331
01:38:53,870 --> 01:38:55,500
- That was the reason.
- Did you reveal your occupation to him?

2332
01:38:55,730 --> 01:38:57,000
- I did.
- You did?

2333
01:38:57,200 --> 01:38:58,870
I said that it didn't matter...

2334
01:38:58,870 --> 01:39:00,240
- as the pickpocket was neutral.
- Right.

2335
01:39:02,780 --> 01:39:04,680
- If this round ends, you'll...
- What?

2336
01:39:05,310 --> 01:39:07,410
A special ability has been used.

2337
01:39:07,410 --> 01:39:08,450
- What?
- What?

2338
01:39:08,450 --> 01:39:10,350
Please gather in the main hall.

2339
01:39:10,850 --> 01:39:12,520
This must be an arrest.

2340
01:39:12,520 --> 01:39:13,650
Was it the dirty cop?

2341
01:39:14,720 --> 01:39:16,660
- It must be the dirty cop.
- What about the cop?

2342
01:39:17,720 --> 01:39:18,960
Didn't I get arrested?

2343
01:39:18,960 --> 01:39:20,630
The dirty cop should be on the move.

2344
01:39:20,990 --> 01:39:23,600
Someone should just die.
Gosh, what is this?

2345
01:39:23,730 --> 01:39:25,160
There's a big possibility that it's you.

2346
01:39:25,500 --> 01:39:26,870
Your voice is too loud.

2347
01:39:29,130 --> 01:39:30,270
YunB...

2348
01:39:30,270 --> 01:39:34,340
(YunB)

2349
01:39:34,340 --> 01:39:37,540
used the arrest ability
against Heo Seong Beom.

2350
01:39:40,210 --> 01:39:41,350
The arrest of the killer...

2351
01:39:42,280 --> 01:39:43,550
has been...

2352
01:39:43,550 --> 01:39:46,350
(The arrest of the killer...)

2353
01:39:46,350 --> 01:39:47,420
unsuccessful.

2354
01:39:48,490 --> 01:39:51,720
YunB and Heo Seong Beom will be removed
from the game.

2355
01:39:52,390 --> 01:39:54,890
He's so scary. He looks like a real cop.

2356
01:39:54,890 --> 01:39:58,600
(YunB and Heo Seong Beom get separated.)

2357
01:39:58,600 --> 01:39:59,900
Seong Beom...

2358
01:40:01,030 --> 01:40:02,300
was acting out too much.

2359
01:40:02,500 --> 01:40:03,500
It made me feel uncomfortable.

2360
01:40:03,500 --> 01:40:05,940
I thought that I had
to get rid of him as soon as possible.

2361
01:40:06,470 --> 01:40:09,910
If he's a cop,

2362
01:40:10,410 --> 01:40:12,680
the game ends the moment
the killer gets arrested.

2363
01:40:14,310 --> 01:40:16,080
- The cop made the arrest, right?
- What?

2364
01:40:16,080 --> 01:40:18,120
- It was the cop, right?
- Yes.

2365
01:40:18,120 --> 01:40:19,620
Well, we don't know
if it's a cop or a dirty cop.

2366
01:40:19,750 --> 01:40:21,090
- We don't know?
- Right.

2367
01:40:24,290 --> 01:40:25,560
Can we have a talk?

2368
01:40:27,290 --> 01:40:28,390
Well played.

2369
01:40:28,390 --> 01:40:29,460
Gosh.

2370
01:40:30,900 --> 01:40:32,300
Did Seong Beom give you some information?

2371
01:40:33,070 --> 01:40:36,070
He didn't have a lot of information,

2372
01:40:36,070 --> 01:40:37,400
but he did give me some before he left.

2373
01:40:37,870 --> 01:40:39,300
But if you are to share that...

2374
01:40:40,470 --> 01:40:42,410
Is it hard for you
to share that information?

2375
01:40:43,840 --> 01:40:45,540
What kind of help do you need?

2376
01:40:46,080 --> 01:40:48,080
If you're a killer,

2377
01:40:48,080 --> 01:40:50,250
you won't be that curious
about Seong Beom.

2378
01:40:50,780 --> 01:40:52,350
Have you revealed your occupation
to anyone?

2379
01:40:52,350 --> 01:40:53,690
No. It's my first time sharing.

2380
01:40:54,090 --> 01:40:55,790
What's your occupation?

2381
01:40:56,390 --> 01:40:57,690
I'm clean.

2382
01:40:57,960 --> 01:41:00,390
Stop lying. You're a regular citizen?

2383
01:41:00,390 --> 01:41:01,430
No.

2384
01:41:01,960 --> 01:41:04,000
- You're clean? What does that mean?
- That one was the dirty cop.

2385
01:41:04,530 --> 01:41:06,060
- You're a cop?
- Yes.

2386
01:41:06,470 --> 01:41:07,570
- Really?
- Yes.

2387
01:41:08,030 --> 01:41:09,100
- Really?
- Yes.

2388
01:41:10,040 --> 01:41:14,270
(The role selection before Round 1)

2389
01:41:14,270 --> 01:41:15,310
Let's survive.

2390
01:41:16,580 --> 01:41:17,680
Kwak Beom,

2391
01:41:17,980 --> 01:41:20,110
please point to one Role Card.

2392
01:41:22,410 --> 01:41:23,480
Right.

2393
01:41:24,250 --> 01:41:25,750
- You have chosen this card.
- Yes.

2394
01:41:26,290 --> 01:41:29,190
(Cop)

2395
01:41:32,190 --> 01:41:33,330
It's a big role.

2396
01:41:34,660 --> 01:41:37,730
I knew that the cop was a really big role.

2397
01:41:38,260 --> 01:41:40,070
There are two ways to end the game.

2398
01:41:40,600 --> 01:41:42,100
The cop arrests the killer...

2399
01:41:42,600 --> 01:41:45,500
or three die by the killer.

2400
01:41:46,840 --> 01:41:48,310
"I have such a big role."

2401
01:41:49,240 --> 01:41:50,310
"What do I do?"

2402
01:41:50,310 --> 01:41:51,910
(Cop)

2403
01:41:55,550 --> 01:41:57,980
- Yes?
- Cop Kwak Beom,

2404
01:41:58,820 --> 01:42:02,220
you have not been attacked
by the killer last night.

2405
01:42:02,820 --> 01:42:04,090
Have you confirmed it?

2406
01:42:04,520 --> 01:42:05,590
Yes.

2407
01:42:06,190 --> 01:42:09,730
There's nothing the cop can do right now.

2408
01:42:10,060 --> 01:42:11,830
I thought that I had to hurry up
with gathering evidence...

2409
01:42:11,830 --> 01:42:15,570
and carry on with the investigation
on my own like an actual cop.

2410
01:42:16,340 --> 01:42:18,970
(Out of Room A and Room E in Round 2...)

2411
01:42:19,270 --> 01:42:20,410
I will choose Room A.

2412
01:42:21,110 --> 01:42:23,580
Kwak Beom, you have chosen Room A.

2413
01:42:23,640 --> 01:42:25,280
- Room E.
- Room E? So was I.

2414
01:42:25,980 --> 01:42:29,980
(He checked the reactions
of the suspects with his lies.)

2415
01:42:29,980 --> 01:42:31,420
- What?
- It happens, though.

2416
01:42:31,580 --> 01:42:34,390
And a decisive incident occurs.

2417
01:42:34,690 --> 01:42:36,820
The dirty cop appears.

2418
01:42:37,190 --> 01:42:38,360
If that's the case...

2419
01:42:38,960 --> 01:42:43,400
(Dirty cop YunB arrests Heo Seong Beom.)

2420
01:42:43,760 --> 01:42:45,060
At the last moment,

2421
01:42:45,060 --> 01:42:48,270
I saw Seong Beom say something
in Xitsuh's ear.

2422
01:42:49,300 --> 01:42:52,270
I confirmed that there was...

2423
01:42:52,270 --> 01:42:54,570
no one else with the ability
to arrest the citizens.

2424
01:42:54,810 --> 01:42:56,540
So I decided to reveal my cards to Xitsuh.

2425
01:42:56,680 --> 01:42:58,540
That way, Xitsuh will reveal his cards
to me as well.

2426
01:42:59,210 --> 01:43:02,280
That was why I kept moving around
different rooms.

2427
01:43:02,880 --> 01:43:04,080
I wanted the killer to follow me.

2428
01:43:04,950 --> 01:43:06,690
When Seong Beom got dragged out,

2429
01:43:06,850 --> 01:43:08,720
you were the one
who got his information from him.

2430
01:43:08,720 --> 01:43:10,060
That is why I'm trusting you
and telling you everything right now.

2431
01:43:10,060 --> 01:43:11,860
- After confirming that he was a citizen?
- Yes.

2432
01:43:12,020 --> 01:43:13,030
Okay.

2433
01:43:13,590 --> 01:43:15,890
I'll give you all the information I have.

2434
01:43:16,030 --> 01:43:18,400
I'm a pickpocket.

2435
01:43:19,770 --> 01:43:20,900
That's sexy.

2436
01:43:21,530 --> 01:43:22,770
I finished all three burglaries.

2437
01:43:23,100 --> 01:43:24,540
- Really?
- Within three rounds.

2438
01:43:24,870 --> 01:43:27,570
The one I was with at the start...

2439
01:43:28,110 --> 01:43:30,110
- was Jin Ho.
- Right.

2440
01:43:30,110 --> 01:43:32,010
- The second one was Keun Woo.
- Right.

2441
01:43:32,010 --> 01:43:33,710
- Both burglaries were successful.
- Gosh.

2442
01:43:33,850 --> 01:43:36,010
- Keun Woo isn't a killer.
- Right.

2443
01:43:36,950 --> 01:43:38,720
Jin Ho isn't a killer.

2444
01:43:39,850 --> 01:43:42,990
As a result, I was able to confirm
that the ones who were with me...

2445
01:43:43,260 --> 01:43:45,160
weren't the killers.

2446
01:43:46,160 --> 01:43:49,190
(Xitsuh went into Room E in Round 1.)

2447
01:43:49,190 --> 01:43:52,460
(Jin Ho was excluded
from being a killer candidate.)

2448
01:43:52,460 --> 01:43:55,800
(Xitsuh went into Room C in Round 2.)

2449
01:43:55,800 --> 01:43:58,570
(Only Keun Woo claimed
to have gone into Room C in Round 2.)

2450
01:43:58,570 --> 01:44:02,040
So Keun Woo and I aren't killers.

2451
01:44:02,240 --> 01:44:05,780
The two that Seong Beom felt
suspicious about were Ji Min and...

2452
01:44:06,550 --> 01:44:07,850
- What?
- Sung Joo?

2453
01:44:08,650 --> 01:44:09,680
It wasn't him.

2454
01:44:09,680 --> 01:44:10,980
- I'll try to remember the name.
- Wasn't it Sung Joo?

2455
01:44:11,980 --> 01:44:13,520
The three kept meeting each other.

2456
01:44:14,420 --> 01:44:15,850
It was Tae Gyun.

2457
01:44:16,150 --> 01:44:18,460
He kept suspecting Ji Min and Tae Gyun
before he left.

2458
01:44:18,990 --> 01:44:23,630
Sung Joo is the one I have my eyes on.

2459
01:44:24,330 --> 01:44:28,230
Tae Gyun and Ji Min were called out
to be strange.

2460
01:44:28,330 --> 01:44:31,200
I started to focus on those two
after hearing that.

2461
01:44:32,470 --> 01:44:35,310
I also think Ji Min is a bit suspicious.

2462
01:44:35,310 --> 01:44:38,080
Same here. I think it'll be great
to wait one more round.

2463
01:44:38,180 --> 01:44:41,180
I said we should wait
as no one was killed yet.

2464
01:44:41,550 --> 01:44:42,810
We shouldn't be too hasty.

2465
01:44:43,350 --> 01:44:45,250
The room selection has ended.

2466
01:44:45,250 --> 01:44:46,590
(The room selection for Round 4 ends.)

2467
01:44:46,790 --> 01:44:47,850
Last night,

2468
01:44:48,290 --> 01:44:50,020
nothing happened.

2469
01:44:58,560 --> 01:44:59,630
Yes?

2470
01:44:59,630 --> 01:45:01,170
Cop Kwak Beom,

2471
01:45:01,570 --> 01:45:02,670
you have not been attacked...

2472
01:45:02,670 --> 01:45:04,940
- by the killer last night.
- Gosh.

2473
01:45:05,570 --> 01:45:06,610
Okay.

2474
01:45:16,550 --> 01:45:19,920
The most suspicious ones,
Park Ji Min and Lee Tae Gyun.

2475
01:45:19,920 --> 01:45:22,620
I saw the two of them talk
in the main hall...

2476
01:45:22,850 --> 01:45:24,690
after running down quickly.

2477
01:45:24,960 --> 01:45:27,290
(After the night of the previous round...)

2478
01:45:27,290 --> 01:45:28,730
(Peeking)

2479
01:45:30,330 --> 01:45:32,960
(Tae Gyun and Ji Min had
a secret conversation in the main hall.)

2480
01:45:32,960 --> 01:45:36,330
So, as soon as the call ended,

2481
01:45:36,330 --> 01:45:38,240
I decided to run down
and hide behind the table.

2482
01:45:43,980 --> 01:45:45,980
(Sprinting)

2483
01:45:49,580 --> 01:45:51,880
(Kwak Beom hides behind the counter.)

2484
01:45:53,790 --> 01:45:56,460
"I'm sure they'll talk. Let's eavesdrop."

2485
01:45:57,260 --> 01:45:59,860
I was planning to make an arrest
right after eavesdropping.

2486
01:46:05,160 --> 01:46:10,640
(Kwak Beom starts his stakeout.)

2487
01:46:11,340 --> 01:46:14,870
(However, no one comes down
to the main hall.)

2488
01:46:19,680 --> 01:46:21,410
No one came down at that moment.

2489
01:46:23,950 --> 01:46:25,220
I just became a mole.

2490
01:46:30,220 --> 01:46:33,360
After checking the movement
of the citizens until Round Four,

2491
01:46:33,790 --> 01:46:35,190
I thought an arrest had to be made...

2492
01:46:35,660 --> 01:46:36,760
for the game to end quickly.

2493
01:46:37,100 --> 01:46:40,000
That was why I started coming up
with a plan for the citizens.

2494
01:46:42,530 --> 01:46:44,740
- Are you checking for the rooms already?
- Not yet.

2495
01:46:44,740 --> 01:46:45,940
No one has said anything yet?

2496
01:46:46,200 --> 01:46:48,870
To make things clear,

2497
01:46:49,140 --> 01:46:51,980
we must make no one say anything,
go inside,

2498
01:46:52,380 --> 01:46:54,180
write it out, and place it
on our foreheads like Indian Poker.

2499
01:46:54,710 --> 01:46:56,280
- I think that's the best method.
- Right.

2500
01:46:56,520 --> 01:46:59,080
When we share about our rooms,

2501
01:46:59,520 --> 01:47:01,150
we shouldn't just take turns
to call out the rooms.

2502
01:47:01,150 --> 01:47:02,220
We should do it like Indian Poker.

2503
01:47:02,220 --> 01:47:04,890
We should write out the words
and place them on our foreheads.

2504
01:47:05,060 --> 01:47:06,190
One, two, three.

2505
01:47:06,190 --> 01:47:07,830
(That was how the game
of Indian Poker began.)

2506
01:47:07,830 --> 01:47:09,330
- Why were there so many in Room C?
- It's Room C for me.

2507
01:47:09,960 --> 01:47:11,430
I'll write it down.

2508
01:47:11,430 --> 01:47:12,500
- Jin Ho, C.
- Ji Min?

2509
01:47:12,500 --> 01:47:14,330
Keun Woo, C. Sung Joo, C.

2510
01:47:14,330 --> 01:47:16,330
- Ji Min, C.
- Ji Min, C?

2511
01:47:16,670 --> 01:47:18,800
Tae Gyun, E. Kwak Beom, A.

2512
01:47:18,940 --> 01:47:21,940
Xitsuh, C. Ji Hoo, A.

2513
01:47:21,940 --> 01:47:23,340
- What about Seung Yong?
- I was in Room C.

2514
01:47:23,610 --> 01:47:24,740
Where were you? A?

2515
01:47:25,180 --> 01:47:26,780
Were you alone, Tae Gyun?

2516
01:47:26,780 --> 01:47:28,110
- I was alone.
- Right.

2517
01:47:28,110 --> 01:47:29,280
I almost got killed.

2518
01:47:29,850 --> 01:47:31,020
- Is that right?
- Yes.

2519
01:47:31,180 --> 01:47:34,220
There were 3 in Room A,
6 in Room C, and 1 in Room E.

2520
01:47:34,450 --> 01:47:35,620
Why were there so many in Room A?

2521
01:47:36,250 --> 01:47:37,490
How does this sound?

2522
01:47:37,490 --> 01:47:40,260
Shall we all take turns to talk about...

2523
01:47:40,260 --> 01:47:42,260
who feels the most suspicious
and share any evidence that was found?

2524
01:47:42,260 --> 01:47:44,200
Should we take some time to talk about
what we want to do?

2525
01:47:44,200 --> 01:47:45,430
- With everyone gathered?
- Right.

2526
01:47:45,430 --> 01:47:46,530
- Sounds good.
- Let's do that.

2527
01:47:46,730 --> 01:47:49,300
As you already know, I'm a citizen.

2528
01:47:49,630 --> 01:47:52,600
The ones I suspect the most are Ji Min...

2529
01:47:52,600 --> 01:47:54,840
(Ji Min)

2530
01:47:54,840 --> 01:47:55,870
and Tae Gyun.

2531
01:47:56,340 --> 01:47:57,480
After those two,

2532
01:47:58,580 --> 01:47:59,610
it's Keun Woo.

2533
01:47:59,780 --> 01:48:03,750
These three are the ones
I suspect the most as the killer faction.

2534
01:48:04,080 --> 01:48:06,820
Aren't you just hating the members
of Team P1?

2535
01:48:06,820 --> 01:48:08,320
- That's not true.
- Right.

2536
01:48:08,320 --> 01:48:09,350
The evidence that I have...

2537
01:48:09,350 --> 01:48:10,890
He's talking nonsense.

2538
01:48:10,890 --> 01:48:14,190
The fact that he chose just the 3 members
of Team P1...

2539
01:48:14,390 --> 01:48:16,460
felt too personal.

2540
01:48:16,460 --> 01:48:19,160
Ji Min, Tae Gyun, and Keun Woo.
There was an idea...

2541
01:48:19,160 --> 01:48:22,700
that it was strange for them
to be together.

2542
01:48:22,870 --> 01:48:25,600
I simply thought
they were members of Team P1...

2543
01:48:25,640 --> 01:48:29,010
and it was possible for them
to have chats with each other.

2544
01:48:30,010 --> 01:48:31,440
This is the first piece of evidence.

2545
01:48:31,440 --> 01:48:34,150
YunB has left the game.
The dirty cop has left.

2546
01:48:34,150 --> 01:48:36,480
These three were the ones
who YunB met up with the most.

2547
01:48:36,550 --> 01:48:38,250
The second piece of evidence is that...

2548
01:48:38,250 --> 01:48:39,990
Seong Beom was the one
who suspected these four people.

2549
01:48:40,250 --> 01:48:42,620
After seeing Seong Beom get eliminated,

2550
01:48:42,620 --> 01:48:45,220
I thought that the ones
he strongly suspected...

2551
01:48:45,620 --> 01:48:49,090
decided to remove him from the game.

2552
01:48:49,090 --> 01:48:50,530
That's my reasoning.

2553
01:48:50,760 --> 01:48:54,570
If I am to add to that,
there were things I witnessed as well.

2554
01:48:54,570 --> 01:48:55,570
What did you witness?

2555
01:48:55,570 --> 01:48:57,240
As soon as the round ended,

2556
01:48:57,240 --> 01:48:59,640
I hid behind the table
after being the first one to run down.

2557
01:48:59,940 --> 01:49:03,340
It was because of the previous round.

2558
01:49:03,340 --> 01:49:06,810
Tae Gyun ran down in a hurry
in the previous round.

2559
01:49:07,110 --> 01:49:10,520
He ran down as if he had someone
to meet here.

2560
01:49:10,820 --> 01:49:13,120
The one I saw after that was Ji Min.

2561
01:49:13,750 --> 01:49:14,790
- What?
- And...

2562
01:49:14,790 --> 01:49:16,390
the one who mumbled something...

2563
01:49:16,390 --> 01:49:18,690
while keeping me in check...

2564
01:49:19,720 --> 01:49:20,860
was Sung Joo.

2565
01:49:21,860 --> 01:49:24,700
Tae Gyun was the one
I had in mind from the start.

2566
01:49:24,960 --> 01:49:27,100
It was Tae Gyun straight from Round One.

2567
01:49:27,270 --> 01:49:30,500
I think the killer made an order
to move quietly.

2568
01:49:30,770 --> 01:49:32,370
I was a bit confused with Sung Joo.

2569
01:49:35,340 --> 01:49:38,580
So in terms of what we are to do,

2570
01:49:38,780 --> 01:49:40,880
I believe keeping things is a good method.

2571
01:49:40,880 --> 01:49:43,580
I'm not sure if you'll agree on this.

2572
01:49:43,780 --> 01:49:46,380
We have a prison guard and a cop, right?

2573
01:49:46,380 --> 01:49:48,450
I'm certain that there's a killer...

2574
01:49:48,450 --> 01:49:50,390
between these two.

2575
01:49:50,520 --> 01:49:52,460
One of the two should be imprisoned.

2576
01:49:52,460 --> 01:49:54,930
If the one who gets imprisoned
gets killed,

2577
01:49:54,930 --> 01:49:57,160
the other one can get arrested by the cop.

2578
01:49:57,330 --> 01:50:01,000
I think it will be a good method
to go in this direction.

2579
01:50:01,130 --> 01:50:03,840
If we all come to an agreement like this,

2580
01:50:03,840 --> 01:50:05,440
I believe it's a good method...

2581
01:50:05,440 --> 01:50:07,810
for the prison guard to take action.

2582
01:50:07,810 --> 01:50:09,640
- So, one of us will...
- Then...

2583
01:50:09,640 --> 01:50:11,510
get imprisoned, and we might get killed.

2584
01:50:11,680 --> 01:50:13,750
Are we trying to see
if we get killed or not?

2585
01:50:13,750 --> 01:50:15,010
Right. But...

2586
01:50:15,110 --> 01:50:17,180
- This was just my opinion.
- Right.

2587
01:50:17,180 --> 01:50:19,650
- My suspicion might not be true.
- Right.

2588
01:50:20,020 --> 01:50:22,420
- What does everyone else think?
- We'll imprison one of them?

2589
01:50:22,750 --> 01:50:25,460
The moment the prison guard
imprisons someone,

2590
01:50:25,460 --> 01:50:27,630
that person might become a target
and get killed.

2591
01:50:27,630 --> 01:50:29,530
- Right. We must all agree.
- That will bring up the kill count...

2592
01:50:29,730 --> 01:50:31,560
for the killer faction.

2593
01:50:31,730 --> 01:50:34,800
You must be certain about this
for this to follow through.

2594
01:50:34,930 --> 01:50:36,400
If there's no certainty,

2595
01:50:36,840 --> 01:50:38,840
this is a terrible strategy
for the citizens.

2596
01:50:39,200 --> 01:50:41,010
I think the prison guard must stay still.

2597
01:50:42,040 --> 01:50:44,240
We can't let the killers get one kill.

2598
01:50:45,510 --> 01:50:49,050
The prison guard's ability
is a very dangerous one.

2599
01:50:49,580 --> 01:50:51,080
Anyone would want to...

2600
01:50:51,520 --> 01:50:54,220
use an ability when given one.

2601
01:50:54,520 --> 01:50:55,950
I wanted to use my ability,

2602
01:50:56,050 --> 01:50:59,160
but the prison guard's ability
was too risky to use.

2603
01:50:59,420 --> 01:51:01,460
Kang Ji Hoo,
your role is the prison guard.

2604
01:51:01,460 --> 01:51:02,490
Right.

2605
01:51:04,700 --> 01:51:07,100
I wasn't really curious about
who the killer was.

2606
01:51:08,830 --> 01:51:11,400
I was curious about the other citizens.

2607
01:51:13,070 --> 01:51:14,940
It was because my plan was...

2608
01:51:15,810 --> 01:51:17,110
to reach Round 9 and Round 10...

2609
01:51:17,110 --> 01:51:20,050
and get the citizens killed
after imprisoning them.

2610
01:51:20,910 --> 01:51:22,110
My targets were definitely...

2611
01:51:23,050 --> 01:51:25,120
Heo Seong Beom, Xitsuh, Hong Jin Ho,
and Choi Hye Seon.

2612
01:51:25,250 --> 01:51:26,480
These four were my targets.

2613
01:51:26,990 --> 01:51:30,060
My role as a prison guard
must never get revealed.

2614
01:51:30,190 --> 01:51:33,730
For me to make the perfect plays
in Round 9 and Round 10,

2615
01:51:34,160 --> 01:51:35,960
my role as a prison guard
must never get revealed.

2616
01:51:36,560 --> 01:51:38,530
- It was Room A.
- A?

2617
01:51:38,960 --> 01:51:40,670
It's right for us not to do anything.

2618
01:51:42,330 --> 01:51:44,370
- Don't you think so?
- It was a really weird opinion.

2619
01:51:44,370 --> 01:51:45,370
Right.

2620
01:51:45,370 --> 01:51:46,370
- Why?
- What?

2621
01:51:46,370 --> 01:51:47,410
Why?

2622
01:51:47,740 --> 01:51:51,310
"Let's imprison someone. Let's do this."

2623
01:51:51,310 --> 01:51:53,450
- I don't think this is the time for that.
- Right.

2624
01:51:53,450 --> 01:51:55,910
Based on the randomizing process,

2625
01:51:56,410 --> 01:51:58,750
- we survived for four rounds.
- Right.

2626
01:51:59,050 --> 01:52:00,690
- Then,
- There's no need for that?

2627
01:52:00,850 --> 01:52:03,620
there's no reason
to change the current strategy.

2628
01:52:04,620 --> 01:52:08,330
"Since no one got killed until now,
let's carry on."

2629
01:52:08,530 --> 01:52:12,000
That opinion felt so frustrating
and it drove me crazy.

2630
01:52:12,260 --> 01:52:13,900
What if you are the one to end up dying?

2631
01:52:14,200 --> 01:52:17,770
Safety complacency is the only way
to describe this.

2632
01:52:17,770 --> 01:52:19,400
- The prison guard must be alive.
- Actually,

2633
01:52:19,400 --> 01:52:21,270
I think it's a good idea
to go with the arrest.

2634
01:52:21,670 --> 01:52:23,140
- Why make an arrest right now?
- Why make an arrest?

2635
01:52:23,140 --> 01:52:24,140
Well...

2636
01:52:24,140 --> 01:52:25,940
- Xitsuh and I...
- I might get killed!

2637
01:52:26,880 --> 01:52:28,050
It's because I might get killed.

2638
01:52:28,050 --> 01:52:29,310
That makes sense as well.

2639
01:52:29,310 --> 01:52:30,520
- I might get killed.
- Well...

2640
01:52:30,520 --> 01:52:32,220
Things are fine right now.

2641
01:52:32,220 --> 01:52:33,750
- Just because things are fine...
- You want to...

2642
01:52:33,750 --> 01:52:35,320
use the cop in case you get killed.

2643
01:52:35,320 --> 01:52:36,920
Two people will be lost
if it's the wrong person.

2644
01:52:36,920 --> 01:52:38,890
- That's what you want to do?
- Taking one suspicious person...

2645
01:52:39,160 --> 01:52:42,490
When a few rounds go by
without any murders,

2646
01:52:42,490 --> 01:52:45,400
that by itself is good for the citizens.

2647
01:52:45,500 --> 01:52:47,800
I believe it won't be late
to take action...

2648
01:52:47,800 --> 01:52:51,040
when things feel tight or dangerous.

2649
01:52:51,270 --> 01:52:53,370
So, up until now,

2650
01:52:53,370 --> 01:52:55,910
- we were all lucky.
- Right.

2651
01:52:55,910 --> 01:52:58,980
There's still a possibility
for the killer to get lucky...

2652
01:52:58,980 --> 01:53:00,650
- and choose a room with one person in it.
- Right.

2653
01:53:00,650 --> 01:53:01,710
Let's say we lose one like that.

2654
01:53:01,710 --> 01:53:03,620
We'll hurriedly arrest someone after that.

2655
01:53:03,620 --> 01:53:05,750
Then, the killer will kill
the person who gets arrested...

2656
01:53:05,750 --> 01:53:07,620
if it isn't someone on his or her side.

2657
01:53:07,620 --> 01:53:10,560
Even if it is someone on his or her side,
a lot of people have been removed.

2658
01:53:10,560 --> 01:53:12,860
There's a greater chance for one person...

2659
01:53:12,860 --> 01:53:14,930
- to be in A, B, C, D, and E.
- Right.

2660
01:53:15,460 --> 01:53:17,530
That is why I believe...

2661
01:53:18,000 --> 01:53:20,100
nothing is safe now.

2662
01:53:20,100 --> 01:53:22,600
As there were people...

2663
01:53:22,600 --> 01:53:24,800
who showed clear signs
of being suspicious,

2664
01:53:24,800 --> 01:53:27,710
I believe it's right to make a move
out of certainty.

2665
01:53:27,710 --> 01:53:29,010
It's because I might become the one
to get killed.

2666
01:53:29,740 --> 01:53:31,840
Waiting for a citizen to get killed...

2667
01:53:32,340 --> 01:53:35,350
is the same thing as praying
that it isn't me.

2668
01:54:00,670 --> 01:54:01,970
- Do you have something in mind?
- Sorry?

2669
01:54:01,970 --> 01:54:03,070
Do you have something in mind?

2670
01:54:03,070 --> 01:54:05,110
Well,

2671
01:54:05,110 --> 01:54:06,610
the moment I mention this,

2672
01:54:06,610 --> 01:54:09,680
everyone will find out about it.

2673
01:54:09,680 --> 01:54:11,480
- This is what I think.
- Right.

2674
01:54:12,950 --> 01:54:14,320
- I think we're doomed.
- Right.

2675
01:54:14,720 --> 01:54:16,020
- This is what I am.
- Right.

2676
01:54:16,020 --> 01:54:18,460
So I should kill someone.
But why aren't you showing off your power?

2677
01:54:19,990 --> 01:54:22,730
Jin Ho came and told me
that he was the psychopath.

2678
01:54:23,060 --> 01:54:25,500
(Role selection)

2679
01:54:25,500 --> 01:54:26,560
This one.

2680
01:54:26,560 --> 01:54:28,330
- You have chosen this card.
- Right.

2681
01:54:28,600 --> 01:54:31,200
Hong Jin Ho, your role is the psychopath.

2682
01:54:32,140 --> 01:54:34,070
(Sighing)

2683
01:54:34,610 --> 01:54:35,710
It wasn't all that great.

2684
01:54:35,710 --> 01:54:37,610
It was a role that I didn't like...

2685
01:54:37,610 --> 01:54:40,980
as it didn't have
a specific characteristic.

2686
01:54:41,650 --> 01:54:43,720
It was disappointing as it was a role...

2687
01:54:43,720 --> 01:54:46,320
with just a certain win condition.

2688
01:54:47,050 --> 01:54:48,820
I gave it some thought during the night...

2689
01:54:48,820 --> 01:54:50,860
about what to do as the psychopath.

2690
01:54:52,320 --> 01:54:54,890
While thinking about
which role I should pretend to be,

2691
01:54:55,290 --> 01:54:56,390
I decided to go with the pickpocket.

2692
01:54:56,390 --> 01:54:59,830
Even if I yell out
that I'm the pickpocket,

2693
01:55:00,330 --> 01:55:02,070
there will be another pickpocket.

2694
01:55:02,070 --> 01:55:05,370
There's no reason for the pickpocket
to come out as it's a neutral role.

2695
01:55:05,540 --> 01:55:09,840
(Jin Ho boldly acted like a pickpocket.)

2696
01:55:09,840 --> 01:55:13,910
(Jin Ho boldly acted like a pickpocket.)

2697
01:55:14,050 --> 01:55:15,850
- The pickpocket is neutral.
- Right.

2698
01:55:16,050 --> 01:55:17,620
- So?
- I need to share the information.

2699
01:55:17,620 --> 01:55:18,720
- Is that so?
- Yes.

2700
01:55:18,780 --> 01:55:22,120
After Round Two, Xitsuh came up to me.

2701
01:55:22,890 --> 01:55:24,320
I'm a pickpocket.

2702
01:55:25,560 --> 01:55:27,660
- You're a pickpocket?
- Speak quietly, will you?

2703
01:55:28,230 --> 01:55:29,290
Gosh.

2704
01:55:29,860 --> 01:55:31,560
Xitsuh happened to be the pickpocket.

2705
01:55:32,400 --> 01:55:36,300
In the midst of that, there was
another reason I couldn't really act.

2706
01:55:36,770 --> 01:55:40,540
Xitsuh was talking a lot with Seong Beom.

2707
01:55:40,870 --> 01:55:43,810
I figured that their stance was
to be on the citizens' side...

2708
01:55:44,680 --> 01:55:47,210
to find the killer.

2709
01:55:47,210 --> 01:55:48,750
I couldn't really act...

2710
01:55:48,750 --> 01:55:50,320
and all I could do...

2711
01:55:50,320 --> 01:55:52,880
was to foolishly pray
for the killer faction to do well.

2712
01:55:53,580 --> 01:55:57,220
Seung Yong strongly led the others
to go in this direction.

2713
01:55:57,790 --> 01:56:00,860
A few survived by luck
in the early rounds.

2714
01:56:00,860 --> 01:56:02,190
- At least one should've gotten killed.
- Right.

2715
01:56:02,190 --> 01:56:03,560
No one got killed.

2716
01:56:03,830 --> 01:56:08,230
Luck was a part of this game.

2717
01:56:08,570 --> 01:56:12,500
We need some luck to be able
to win this game.

2718
01:56:12,500 --> 01:56:14,670
Things became really hard at that point.

2719
01:56:15,070 --> 01:56:16,810
- Right.
- I'm not sure.

2720
01:56:16,810 --> 01:56:17,810
Tae Gyun.

2721
01:56:17,810 --> 01:56:20,450
(Xitsuh called for Tae Gyun.)

2722
01:56:20,450 --> 01:56:22,450
It's just you and Ji Min's occupation
that are left.

2723
01:56:23,720 --> 01:56:25,650
If you call out an occupation
that no one else has called out,

2724
01:56:25,920 --> 01:56:27,250
you can be free.

2725
01:56:27,750 --> 01:56:28,820
Xitsuh.

2726
01:56:30,250 --> 01:56:32,090
- Do you want to make a deal with me?
- Let's go.

2727
01:56:33,830 --> 01:56:35,630
I know what your occupation is.

2728
01:56:35,630 --> 01:56:37,230
- What?
- I know what your occupation is.

2729
01:56:37,530 --> 01:56:38,800
- I'm the pickpocket.
- Sorry?

2730
01:56:38,800 --> 01:56:40,300
- I'm the pickpocket.
- Right.

2731
01:56:40,300 --> 01:56:43,070
- Are you willing to help me?
- Things have begun.

2732
01:56:43,400 --> 01:56:44,570
- The killers?
- Yes.

2733
01:56:45,600 --> 01:56:46,870
Tae Gyun...

2734
01:56:47,000 --> 01:56:50,410
openly revealed
that he was from the killer faction.

2735
01:56:50,810 --> 01:56:53,710
I thought that he was really
in need of help.

2736
01:56:54,580 --> 01:56:55,950
He was in a crisis.

2737
01:56:56,310 --> 01:57:00,150
It doesn't matter to the pickpocket
whichever side wins.

2738
01:57:00,620 --> 01:57:01,920
To find a way out,

2739
01:57:02,490 --> 01:57:05,160
I had to get Xitsuh on my side.

2740
01:57:06,060 --> 01:57:07,130
How should I help you?

2741
01:57:07,130 --> 01:57:08,690
Should I wait until three murders occur?

2742
01:57:09,330 --> 01:57:10,730
Right. Anyway...

2743
01:57:10,730 --> 01:57:13,630
During that time,

2744
01:57:13,630 --> 01:57:15,830
I must avoid getting killed.

2745
01:57:15,830 --> 01:57:18,140
There's no guarantee that
the killer won't come to where I'm hiding.

2746
01:57:18,140 --> 01:57:20,740
I can tell you where the killer will go
for each round.

2747
01:57:21,110 --> 01:57:23,410
He said he can tell me
where the killer will go for each round.

2748
01:57:23,640 --> 01:57:25,110
That was a tempting deal.

2749
01:57:25,440 --> 01:57:26,710
- But...
- Well,

2750
01:57:26,980 --> 01:57:28,750
- it doesn't matter to me which side wins.
- Exactly.

2751
01:57:28,750 --> 01:57:30,750
- It's obvious.
- Right.

2752
01:57:30,880 --> 01:57:32,520
So for me,

2753
01:57:33,250 --> 01:57:34,890
- I wish for things to end quickly.
- Right.

2754
01:57:34,890 --> 01:57:36,150
- If someone gets killed...
- Lee Tae Gyun,

2755
01:57:36,150 --> 01:57:37,920
- please head to the Voting Room.
- Let's carry on with our conversation.

2756
01:57:37,920 --> 01:57:38,990
Right.

2757
01:57:39,620 --> 01:57:40,860
- Lee Tae Gyun,
- Right.

2758
01:57:40,860 --> 01:57:41,890
please head to the Voting Room.

2759
01:57:46,700 --> 01:57:47,870
He's a follower, isn't he?

2760
01:57:48,770 --> 01:57:50,400
- I wasn't able to hear that much.
- Right.

2761
01:57:51,800 --> 01:57:54,310
- There's something off about him.
- He's from the killer faction.

2762
01:57:55,010 --> 01:57:57,210
- He tried to make a deal with me.
- He keeps doing that.

2763
01:57:57,210 --> 01:57:59,310
He tried to make a deal with me.
He's from the killer faction.

2764
01:57:59,580 --> 01:58:03,310
I don't think I'll be making a deal
with the killer.

2765
01:58:03,310 --> 01:58:05,750
The game must end the next day.

2766
01:58:06,180 --> 01:58:08,990
I'll share the occupations
I found out about...

2767
01:58:09,120 --> 01:58:11,920
and make an arrest happen after
finding out the rest of the occupations.

2768
01:58:13,260 --> 01:58:15,330
Do you know the probability
of you getting killed inside?

2769
01:58:15,730 --> 01:58:17,760
- I don't know. I'm not interested.
- It's only eight percent.

2770
01:58:17,760 --> 01:58:19,160
- What?
- It's only eight percent.

2771
01:58:19,160 --> 01:58:20,330
- Why?
- You won't get killed.

2772
01:58:20,400 --> 01:58:22,600
You have an eight percent
of getting killed in B, C, or D.

2773
01:58:23,070 --> 01:58:24,770
- You won't get killed.
- What?

2774
01:58:25,070 --> 01:58:27,340
After going in B, C, or D...

2775
01:58:27,910 --> 01:58:30,110
and after the killer chooses one
out of B, C, or D,

2776
01:58:30,110 --> 01:58:31,410
there's only an eight percent chance
of getting killed.

2777
01:58:31,410 --> 01:58:32,780
There's a very low chance
of getting killed.

2778
01:58:32,780 --> 01:58:34,210
- B, C, or D?
- "Xitsuh,"

2779
01:58:34,410 --> 01:58:36,450
"do you know what the probability is
of getting killed..."

2780
01:58:36,450 --> 01:58:38,080
"in B, C, or D?"

2781
01:58:39,050 --> 01:58:40,050
I didn't know.

2782
01:58:40,050 --> 01:58:42,320
Could the probability be calculated?

2783
01:58:42,320 --> 01:58:43,960
I didn't even try
to find the probability anyway.

2784
01:58:44,520 --> 01:58:45,690
Why did you mention that?

2785
01:58:46,320 --> 01:58:47,830
It was to keep him relieved.

2786
01:58:48,660 --> 01:58:52,130
Things might get ruined
while trying to be hasty.

2787
01:58:52,930 --> 01:58:55,970
I was with 1 other person 3 times!

2788
01:58:55,970 --> 01:58:58,800
I've pulled off a burglary even in Room C!

2789
01:58:59,270 --> 01:59:02,070
Things will end if I die
by that 8.8 percent chance!

2790
01:59:03,170 --> 01:59:04,340
Where are you going to go this time?

2791
01:59:05,010 --> 01:59:06,180
I don't know. I was told to go
in B, C, or D,

2792
01:59:06,180 --> 01:59:07,350
as it's an eight percent chance.

2793
01:59:07,480 --> 01:59:09,880
Xitsuh, please head to the Voting Room.

2794
01:59:09,880 --> 01:59:12,180
(Xitsuh enters for his room selection.)

2795
01:59:16,020 --> 01:59:17,150
Xitsuh,

2796
01:59:18,320 --> 01:59:19,890
please choose one of the cards.

2797
01:59:21,090 --> 01:59:23,030
When Round Five started,

2798
01:59:23,630 --> 01:59:25,460
we all shared about the rooms we were in.

2799
01:59:25,630 --> 01:59:27,530
Room B was empty.

2800
01:59:28,030 --> 01:59:33,000
(Many were in Room A and Room C
during Round 4.)

2801
01:59:33,340 --> 01:59:35,240
It's never certain for there...

2802
01:59:35,240 --> 01:59:37,410
to be many people in Rooms B, C, or D.

2803
01:59:37,780 --> 01:59:39,410
After giving it some thought,

2804
01:59:39,780 --> 01:59:41,680
I tried to think
from the killer's perspective.

2805
01:59:42,210 --> 01:59:43,510
From the killer's perspective,

2806
01:59:44,250 --> 01:59:47,220
I thought that the killer would try
to pray...

2807
01:59:47,590 --> 01:59:49,650
to find a room with one other...

2808
01:59:49,850 --> 01:59:52,420
out of Rooms B, C, D, and E.

2809
01:59:55,230 --> 01:59:58,260
Xitsuh, you have chosen Room F.

2810
01:59:59,030 --> 02:00:02,030
It was the room
where I made a successful burglary.

2811
02:00:02,400 --> 02:00:05,770
I decided to enter Room F again.

2812
02:00:06,770 --> 02:00:09,340
The room selection has ended
for all players.

2813
02:00:10,440 --> 02:00:16,480
(Round 5, Night Phase)

2814
02:00:16,480 --> 02:00:22,190
(Round 5, Night Phase)

2815
02:00:27,090 --> 02:00:28,730
Nighttime has ended.

2816
02:00:30,630 --> 02:00:32,100
Please take off the blindfold.

2817
02:00:42,670 --> 02:00:44,980
Here's the result of last night.

2818
02:00:45,680 --> 02:00:46,740
Last night,

2819
02:00:47,950 --> 02:00:50,450
Xitsuh got killed.

2820
02:00:50,680 --> 02:00:53,080
(First victim, Xitsuh)

2821
02:00:53,080 --> 02:00:54,750
Darn it, I knew it.

2822
02:00:56,390 --> 02:00:57,760
What bad luck I have.

2823
02:00:58,960 --> 02:01:02,790
Why does this bad feeling
always become true?

2824
02:01:03,760 --> 02:01:06,700
I thought I was really unlucky
when I picked the pickpocket card.

2825
02:01:07,700 --> 02:01:09,300
After making 3 burglaries in a row
in Rounds 1, 2, and 3,

2826
02:01:09,300 --> 02:01:11,200
I considered myself to be a lucky guy.

2827
02:01:12,470 --> 02:01:15,610
But the 1st one to get killed
after 6 rounds is me.

2828
02:01:18,580 --> 02:01:19,840
I shouldn't have gone to Room F.

2829
02:01:22,250 --> 02:01:23,310
This...

2830
02:01:23,980 --> 02:01:25,150
doesn't make sense.

2831
02:01:26,450 --> 02:01:28,550
I made the impossible possible.

2832
02:01:28,550 --> 02:01:29,950
(Xitsuh died
after making 3 burglaries in a row.)

2833
02:01:32,620 --> 02:01:33,890
Where must I go?

2834
02:01:36,130 --> 02:01:39,230
Someone should've been arrested
in the previous round.

2835
02:01:39,630 --> 02:01:42,170
"Let's take it slow
since no one got killed."

2836
02:01:42,400 --> 02:01:45,700
"Gosh! Then will you speed things up now?"

2837
02:01:46,200 --> 02:01:48,070
It was so upsetting that it felt like
the game was going to end quickly...

2838
02:01:48,070 --> 02:01:49,310
right after my death.

2839
02:01:53,740 --> 02:01:55,550
(Sighing)

2840
02:01:55,550 --> 02:01:57,050
Gosh.

2841
02:01:57,050 --> 02:01:58,920
There's a need to act boldly now.

2842
02:02:00,020 --> 02:02:01,550
Xitsuh got killed.

2843
02:02:01,950 --> 02:02:03,290
The pickpocket died...

2844
02:02:03,290 --> 02:02:05,860
and that got me pressed for time.

2845
02:02:06,160 --> 02:02:08,890
The pickpocket and the killer
follow the same structure.

2846
02:02:09,190 --> 02:02:11,230
A burglary is made
when there is one other person.

2847
02:02:11,430 --> 02:02:13,060
One can get killed
when there is one other person.

2848
02:02:13,060 --> 02:02:15,670
Xitsuh managed to do it
three times in a row.

2849
02:02:15,670 --> 02:02:18,340
He managed to make three burglaries
in a row.

2850
02:02:18,640 --> 02:02:20,840
This meant the killer could make
three murders in a row...

2851
02:02:20,840 --> 02:02:22,440
even though it was still Round Six.

2852
02:02:22,770 --> 02:02:24,410
There's a need to be bold.

2853
02:02:24,740 --> 02:02:25,810
Bold?

2854
02:02:25,810 --> 02:02:27,910
Ji Hoo, how many people are left now?

2855
02:02:28,010 --> 02:02:29,110
- There are 9 left.
- There are 9 left.

2856
02:02:29,110 --> 02:02:31,150
- There are 9 left with 6 rooms.
- Right.

2857
02:02:31,350 --> 02:02:32,650
It's 2 against 7.

2858
02:02:32,950 --> 02:02:36,890
There's a hint that can be found
once a murder has been committed.

2859
02:02:36,990 --> 02:02:39,160
Getting someone killed
was a bit disappointing,

2860
02:02:39,160 --> 02:02:43,530
but I thought it was an opportunity
to narrow down on someone.

2861
02:02:43,830 --> 02:02:46,200
Let's gather for a game of Indian Poker.

2862
02:02:46,460 --> 02:02:48,530
Whose hands are bloody right now?

2863
02:02:49,230 --> 02:02:51,800
Hold on. Let's share about our rooms first
before we talk, Hye Seon.

2864
02:02:51,800 --> 02:02:53,070
We can write down our rooms.

2865
02:02:53,070 --> 02:02:54,670
- Right.
- Right. We'll gather for Indian Poker.

2866
02:02:56,610 --> 02:02:59,680
The hidden item will now be revealed.

2867
02:03:00,180 --> 02:03:01,180
Gosh!

2868
02:03:01,180 --> 02:03:02,910
The hidden item for the Killer Game...

2869
02:03:02,910 --> 02:03:05,520
(They get in line first.)

2870
02:03:05,720 --> 02:03:07,080
(Extra killer vote ticket)

2871
02:03:07,080 --> 02:03:08,890
is the extra killer vote ticket.

2872
02:03:08,890 --> 02:03:10,290
(An additional vote is made
in the final killer vote.)

2873
02:03:10,290 --> 02:03:11,720
In the final killer vote,

2874
02:03:12,320 --> 02:03:14,730
this item can be used as an extra vote.

2875
02:03:16,330 --> 02:03:18,600
It's nothing special. It's a vote ticket.

2876
02:03:18,860 --> 02:03:21,800
It can be purchased in the Voting Room
starting from now.

2877
02:03:22,830 --> 02:03:25,570
There's one ticket for sale.

2878
02:03:26,200 --> 02:03:28,840
(Sung Joo rushes into the Voting Room.)

2879
02:03:30,470 --> 02:03:32,940
He went right in
when I pretended to go in.

2880
02:03:33,310 --> 02:03:35,650
- I think he got tricked.
- I was just faking it.

2881
02:03:35,980 --> 02:03:38,450
I'll purchase the voting ticket.

2882
02:03:39,750 --> 02:03:41,550
- Will you purchase the item?
- Yes.

2883
02:03:41,550 --> 02:03:43,250
(Is Sung Joo purchasing the item?)

2884
02:03:43,590 --> 02:03:45,460
- Right.
- Didn't he just turn himself in?

2885
02:03:45,560 --> 02:03:46,690
- What?
- I don't have any money.

2886
02:03:46,690 --> 02:03:48,990
- Doing that...
- He turned himself in.

2887
02:03:48,990 --> 02:03:50,230
Isn't he going to make an extra vote...

2888
02:03:50,230 --> 02:03:51,760
when voting for the killer?

2889
02:03:52,160 --> 02:03:56,100
To prevent others
from using the voting ticket,

2890
02:03:56,100 --> 02:03:57,300
the killer can purchase it on purpose.

2891
02:03:58,770 --> 02:04:01,140
- It will be used to vote someone else.
- There are nine of us left.

2892
02:04:02,140 --> 02:04:03,670
One, two, three.

2893
02:04:04,280 --> 02:04:05,310
D.

2894
02:04:05,310 --> 02:04:06,410
(The game of Indian Poker begins.)

2895
02:04:06,410 --> 02:04:08,080
I'll write it down. I'm sorry.

2896
02:04:09,180 --> 02:04:10,850
Ji Hoo, A.

2897
02:04:11,520 --> 02:04:12,750
Jin Ho, C.

2898
02:04:13,680 --> 02:04:16,320
Sung Joo, A. Hye Seon, E.

2899
02:04:16,720 --> 02:04:18,090
(Room selection result of Round 5)

2900
02:04:18,090 --> 02:04:19,860
(A: Hyun Sung Joo, Kang Ji Hoo,
Kwak Beom, B: Lee Tae Gyun,)

2901
02:04:19,860 --> 02:04:20,860
(C: Hong Jin Ho, D: Jeong Keun Woo,
Shin Seung Yong, Park Ji Min,)

2902
02:04:20,860 --> 02:04:21,890
(E: Choi Hye Seon)

2903
02:04:22,060 --> 02:04:23,760
But starting from now,

2904
02:04:23,760 --> 02:04:25,930
if someone gets unlucky and gets killed,

2905
02:04:26,430 --> 02:04:28,530
things will get a lot tougher.

2906
02:04:28,900 --> 02:04:30,100
- Right.
- Right.

2907
02:04:30,230 --> 02:04:32,970
We're in that situation.
I don't really understand...

2908
02:04:33,470 --> 02:04:35,670
why the citizens are being so slow
about this.

2909
02:04:35,870 --> 02:04:36,870
Right.

2910
02:04:36,870 --> 02:04:39,710
There's a need
for the forensic doctor to make a check.

2911
02:04:39,710 --> 02:04:40,780
(The investigative ability earned
after a murder can be used to check...)

2912
02:04:40,780 --> 02:04:41,850
(if someone is the killer.)

2913
02:04:41,850 --> 02:04:42,850
We had to move quickly.

2914
02:04:42,850 --> 02:04:45,150
I asked
for the forensic doctor to show up,

2915
02:04:45,620 --> 02:04:47,280
but no one said anything.

2916
02:04:48,890 --> 02:04:49,950
"What are we doing?"

2917
02:04:49,950 --> 02:04:51,920
"Why are we struggling
to finish off the game?"

2918
02:04:52,220 --> 02:04:55,090
I felt so frustrated
that I even raised my voice.

2919
02:04:56,690 --> 02:04:59,200
I'm really frustrated right now.

2920
02:04:59,430 --> 02:05:02,670
We're almost winning, so why...

2921
02:05:03,800 --> 02:05:05,140
A murder took place,

2922
02:05:05,140 --> 02:05:07,710
so we should act quickly
and catch the killer.

2923
02:05:07,710 --> 02:05:09,640
Did they get brainwashed or something?

2924
02:05:09,640 --> 02:05:11,410
Did the forensic doctor die?

2925
02:05:13,340 --> 02:05:14,950
I suddenly became suspicious.

2926
02:05:15,880 --> 02:05:17,950
"Did the forensic doctor decide
to team up with the killer?"

2927
02:05:19,280 --> 02:05:22,350
Did they strike a deal about something
that'd come after the game ended?

2928
02:05:22,490 --> 02:05:24,760
If the forensic doctor
revealed themselves...

2929
02:05:24,760 --> 02:05:28,160
and shared their plans with us,

2930
02:05:28,160 --> 02:05:29,260
the game could've gone...

2931
02:05:29,260 --> 02:05:30,730
a lot smoother.

2932
02:05:30,730 --> 02:05:32,660
- Why...
- I'd like the forensic doctor...

2933
02:05:33,160 --> 02:05:36,230
to check Tae Gyun or someone else.

2934
02:05:36,530 --> 02:05:38,740
That would be a good move.

2935
02:05:38,740 --> 02:05:40,370
Exactly. Why are they...

2936
02:05:40,370 --> 02:05:43,640
Anyway, we got one case of murder.

2937
02:05:43,640 --> 02:05:47,080
In this case,
the citizens will get impatient...

2938
02:05:47,080 --> 02:05:49,350
because none of them
have revealed their identities yet.

2939
02:05:49,350 --> 02:05:50,450
They're all nuts.

2940
02:05:50,450 --> 02:05:51,550
And in the midst of it,

2941
02:05:52,080 --> 02:05:55,050
Tae Gyun made a stupid mistake.

2942
02:05:55,050 --> 02:05:56,890
- No.
- Do you know my occupation?

2943
02:05:57,120 --> 02:05:58,690
No. What is it?

2944
02:05:58,890 --> 02:05:59,890
I'm a forensic doctor.

2945
02:06:00,390 --> 02:06:01,490
I see.

2946
02:06:02,560 --> 02:06:03,830
Then can you use...

2947
02:06:03,830 --> 02:06:05,400
the investigative ability and let me know?

2948
02:06:06,330 --> 02:06:08,170
You can't go in during the day...

2949
02:06:08,170 --> 02:06:10,730
and ask her.

2950
02:06:11,400 --> 02:06:13,970
I talk to her via a phone call
when the day starts.

2951
02:06:15,740 --> 02:06:18,340
It says to investigate by talking
with the butler in the Voting Room.

2952
02:06:20,440 --> 02:06:21,710
I mean, the other...

2953
02:06:21,710 --> 02:06:23,350
(Flustered)

2954
02:06:23,350 --> 02:06:25,450
That was a big mistake I made.

2955
02:06:25,780 --> 02:06:27,150
The forensic doctor...

2956
02:06:27,580 --> 02:06:31,760
has to go to the Voting Room
to exercise one's investigative ability.

2957
02:06:32,160 --> 02:06:33,290
I missed that part.

2958
02:06:33,760 --> 02:06:37,260
I just had a talk with Tae Gyun.

2959
02:06:37,530 --> 02:06:39,960
Tae Gyun said he was a forensic doctor,

2960
02:06:39,960 --> 02:06:41,700
and since one person had died,

2961
02:06:42,000 --> 02:06:44,400
he used his investigative ability on me.

2962
02:06:44,400 --> 02:06:45,900
But he said he did it over a phone call.

2963
02:06:45,900 --> 02:06:47,470
But from what I can read here,

2964
02:06:47,470 --> 02:06:49,910
it says to talk to the butler
in the Voting Room to investigate.

2965
02:06:49,910 --> 02:06:51,280
And I just confirmed that.

2966
02:06:51,280 --> 02:06:53,780
He is on the killer's side.

2967
02:06:53,780 --> 02:06:54,780
This is...

2968
02:06:54,910 --> 02:06:56,710
You shot yourself in the foot.

2969
02:06:57,450 --> 02:07:00,620
Tae Gyun shot himself in the foot
and got caught there.

2970
02:07:00,620 --> 02:07:03,220
The game could've gone smoothly.

2971
02:07:03,220 --> 02:07:05,690
This is the worst.

2972
02:07:05,690 --> 02:07:08,590
Do we still not know
who the forensic doctor is?

2973
02:07:09,090 --> 02:07:10,230
No.

2974
02:07:10,790 --> 02:07:15,100
I think it's fine for the citizens
to disclose our occupations now.

2975
02:07:15,100 --> 02:07:16,930
You should share it now...

2976
02:07:16,930 --> 02:07:18,440
if you want the citizens to win.

2977
02:07:19,240 --> 02:07:20,240
Now.

2978
02:07:20,770 --> 02:07:22,770
I don't know
what kind of deal you've made, but...

2979
02:07:24,310 --> 02:07:27,310
Seung Yong,
if you think about it carefully,

2980
02:07:27,540 --> 02:07:30,080
it's all about luck.
If another person dies next round,

2981
02:07:30,080 --> 02:07:31,620
that'll make it two people.

2982
02:07:31,620 --> 02:07:32,620
We're taking things way too slow.

2983
02:07:32,620 --> 02:07:34,420
The forensic doctor needs to make a move.

2984
02:07:34,420 --> 02:07:36,450
It's over if one more person dies.

2985
02:07:36,450 --> 02:07:38,320
- The killer will win.
- Exactly. This...

2986
02:07:42,330 --> 02:07:43,330
Yes.

2987
02:07:44,160 --> 02:07:45,730
The forensic doctor...

2988
02:07:45,730 --> 02:07:47,460
- needs to make a move.
- Do you know why?

2989
02:07:47,730 --> 02:07:50,070
Because they're on the killer's team.

2990
02:07:50,070 --> 02:07:51,970
That's why they can't tell us.

2991
02:07:51,970 --> 02:07:54,410
Come on, that's impossible.

2992
02:07:54,410 --> 02:07:56,110
Then why aren't they doing anything?

2993
02:07:57,110 --> 02:07:59,410
That's the only logical reason.

2994
02:08:00,180 --> 02:08:02,310
They won't share any information with us.

2995
02:08:02,580 --> 02:08:03,780
Nobody stood up.

2996
02:08:03,780 --> 02:08:05,380
In this case,

2997
02:08:05,380 --> 02:08:08,590
things will get really tough
if another citizen dies.

2998
02:08:11,790 --> 02:08:13,190
I have no choice.

2999
02:08:14,890 --> 02:08:15,890
Salute!

3000
02:08:16,330 --> 02:08:17,390
I'll get going!

3001
02:08:18,030 --> 02:08:19,100
- Are you serious?
- What?

3002
02:08:23,230 --> 02:08:24,300
There's no other way.

3003
02:08:24,700 --> 02:08:26,970
If the forensic doctor is so unwilling
to help,

3004
02:08:27,370 --> 02:08:29,210
I must trust my intuition.

3005
02:08:29,740 --> 02:08:31,480
I can't help it.

3006
02:08:33,410 --> 02:08:36,080
Kwak Beom. How may I help you?

3007
02:08:36,650 --> 02:08:37,750
I will arrest.

3008
02:08:38,520 --> 02:08:40,180
Who will you arrest?

3009
02:08:40,180 --> 02:08:45,820
(Round 6, Day Phase)

3010
02:08:45,820 --> 02:08:51,500
(Round 6, Day Phase)

3011
02:08:51,500 --> 02:08:52,660
Park Ji Min.

3012
02:08:52,660 --> 02:08:53,730
(He arrests Park Ji Min.)

3013
02:08:53,730 --> 02:08:55,830
I'll arrest her for murder.

3014
02:08:55,830 --> 02:08:58,170
(He arrests Park Ji Min.)

3015
02:08:58,170 --> 02:08:59,640
Ji Min came to me...

3016
02:08:59,940 --> 02:09:02,470
and asked, "What will you do?"

3017
02:09:02,470 --> 02:09:06,340
"I'm a gambler."

3018
02:09:06,340 --> 02:09:07,340
So I said, "Really?"

3019
02:09:07,480 --> 02:09:09,050
I'm a gambler.

3020
02:09:09,050 --> 02:09:10,680
- What?
- I'm a gambler.

3021
02:09:11,580 --> 02:09:15,320
I revealed myself to Hye Seon
since Round One.

3022
02:09:15,520 --> 02:09:16,920
- You revealed your occupations?
- Yes.

3023
02:09:17,550 --> 02:09:18,620
What is Hye Seon?

3024
02:09:18,990 --> 02:09:20,420
Hye Seon didn't share hers with me.

3025
02:09:20,420 --> 02:09:21,730
Why did you reveal yours to her then?

3026
02:09:21,730 --> 02:09:22,830
For what?

3027
02:09:23,290 --> 02:09:25,900
- Why did you tell her?
- Because Seong Beom was suspicious of me.

3028
02:09:25,900 --> 02:09:28,030
- What?
- Seong Beom was suspicious of me.

3029
02:09:28,030 --> 02:09:29,130
- But even if he does,
- If I die...

3030
02:09:29,130 --> 02:09:30,500
you don't get any information in return,

3031
02:09:30,500 --> 02:09:32,470
so why did you tell her
you were a gambler?

3032
02:09:32,470 --> 02:09:33,770
She revealed her occupation...

3033
02:09:33,770 --> 02:09:36,670
without finding out about theirs
in return?

3034
02:09:37,310 --> 02:09:39,440
She must be lying.

3035
02:09:40,240 --> 02:09:41,250
Park Ji Min...

3036
02:09:41,550 --> 02:09:42,710
is the killer.

3037
02:09:43,550 --> 02:09:45,780
The arrest result will be revealed soon.

3038
02:09:45,780 --> 02:09:47,350
Please head to the main hall.

3039
02:09:54,420 --> 02:09:56,390
Turns out I'm not the cop.

3040
02:09:56,890 --> 02:09:58,600
You're so annoying.

3041
02:09:58,600 --> 02:10:00,260
- I'm not.
- But...

3042
02:10:00,260 --> 02:10:01,930
you looked so real until the last moment.

3043
02:10:03,000 --> 02:10:05,000
Turns out I'm not the cop.

3044
02:10:05,740 --> 02:10:07,800
A special ability has been used.

3045
02:10:08,740 --> 02:10:11,780
Kwak Beom used his arrest ability...

3046
02:10:12,010 --> 02:10:14,080
on Park Ji Min.

3047
02:10:14,310 --> 02:10:15,350
If I fail to arrest the killer,

3048
02:10:15,350 --> 02:10:16,650
I'll leave it to the citizens.

3049
02:10:16,650 --> 02:10:18,350
This is all the forensic doctor's fault.

3050
02:10:18,820 --> 02:10:22,050
Beom went into the Voting Room
without discussing...

3051
02:10:22,050 --> 02:10:24,120
and rushed to end the game quickly.

3052
02:10:24,560 --> 02:10:25,620
The arrest...

3053
02:10:26,160 --> 02:10:27,420
of the killer...

3054
02:10:31,330 --> 02:10:32,430
has been successful.

3055
02:10:33,600 --> 02:10:38,470
(He successfully arrests
Park Ji Min, the killer.)

3056
02:10:38,470 --> 02:10:40,700
This is why people play Bloody Game.

3057
02:10:41,100 --> 02:10:43,910
People keep coming back
for the rush of dopamine.

3058
02:10:44,270 --> 02:10:47,310
I even felt as elated as the time...

3059
02:10:47,310 --> 02:10:48,950
I passed the comedian audition.

3060
02:10:49,050 --> 02:10:50,050
Gosh, Beom.

3061
02:10:50,650 --> 02:10:52,350
Beom, we would've found out
in the next round.

3062
02:10:52,350 --> 02:10:54,380
The forensic doctor was supposed to
announce it on the day of the next round.

3063
02:10:54,950 --> 02:10:56,620
And I even chose Ji Min.

3064
02:10:56,820 --> 02:11:00,020
(30 minutes ago)

3065
02:11:00,820 --> 02:11:02,890
Can I use my investigative ability now?

3066
02:11:03,690 --> 02:11:04,930
Yes, you can.

3067
02:11:06,600 --> 02:11:07,760
Park Ji Min.

3068
02:11:07,760 --> 02:11:08,770
(He used his investigative ability
on Ji Min.)

3069
02:11:09,070 --> 02:11:10,770
YunB and Ji Min are very close.

3070
02:11:10,770 --> 02:11:12,400
YunB and Tae Gyun aren't.

3071
02:11:12,570 --> 02:11:14,770
But YunB would only talk with Tae Gyun.

3072
02:11:14,770 --> 02:11:15,810
Logically,

3073
02:11:15,810 --> 02:11:18,140
why would he talk with that guy
when he's closer with her?

3074
02:11:18,140 --> 02:11:21,310
Because he has a reason
to stay away from her.

3075
02:11:21,580 --> 02:11:23,580
The reason is, she is the killer.

3076
02:11:23,580 --> 02:11:25,180
That's how my thought process went.

3077
02:11:25,420 --> 02:11:28,350
If 1 of the 3 is the killer,
it has to be Ji Min.

3078
02:11:28,350 --> 02:11:29,790
That was what I thought.

3079
02:11:29,790 --> 02:11:34,160
So the game turned out easy for us,

3080
02:11:34,160 --> 02:11:36,730
and for Ji Min,
it was the end of a tough battle.

3081
02:11:37,330 --> 02:11:38,400
Has been successful.

3082
02:11:43,430 --> 02:11:45,940
Gosh, Beom. Beom, we would've found out...

3083
02:11:46,570 --> 02:11:48,040
I felt so bad.

3084
02:11:49,270 --> 02:11:50,670
First of all,

3085
02:11:52,210 --> 02:11:54,180
I felt so bad for Keun Woo.

3086
02:11:57,710 --> 02:12:00,120
Jeong Keun Woo, your role is a gambler.

3087
02:12:00,120 --> 02:12:01,120
(Keun Woo drew the gambler card.)

3088
02:12:06,220 --> 02:12:07,220
I'm a gambler.

3089
02:12:07,220 --> 02:12:09,430
(Early in the game, he shared his role
with Tae Gyun, the follower.)

3090
02:12:10,590 --> 02:12:16,030
(Round 4, when it was already likely
that the killer faction would lose)

3091
02:12:21,840 --> 02:12:24,270
Jeong Keun Woo, would you like to bet?

3092
02:12:24,270 --> 02:12:25,540
I'd like to bet.

3093
02:12:25,710 --> 02:12:28,280
Jeong Keun Woo,
which faction will you bet on?

3094
02:12:30,250 --> 02:12:31,850
If I wanted to survive,

3095
02:12:31,850 --> 02:12:34,280
I would bet on the citizens.

3096
02:12:34,580 --> 02:12:37,220
I estimated a 90 to 100 percent chance...

3097
02:12:37,220 --> 02:12:39,460
of survival.

3098
02:12:40,920 --> 02:12:44,190
But the time I spent with my teammates.

3099
02:12:45,600 --> 02:12:49,370
And even if I lost,
I wanted to lose with them.

3100
02:12:51,640 --> 02:12:53,740
I'll bet on the killer faction.

3101
02:12:54,810 --> 02:12:57,740
Jeong Keun Woo,
you've bet on the killer faction.

3102
02:12:58,640 --> 02:13:00,840
He would've survived
if he'd bet on the citizens.

3103
02:13:00,840 --> 02:13:02,350
I felt so bad about it.

3104
02:13:03,210 --> 02:13:04,410
I played so poorly.

3105
02:13:04,410 --> 02:13:05,420
- No, it can't be helped.
- No.

3106
02:13:05,420 --> 02:13:06,980
The game itself is very tough
for the killer.

3107
02:13:06,980 --> 02:13:08,890
Yes, it's tough to win.

3108
02:13:08,890 --> 02:13:10,150
Goodness.

3109
02:13:10,150 --> 02:13:12,460
- Don't be like this, Tae Gyun.
- If it's like...

3110
02:13:14,660 --> 02:13:17,060
What's there for him to be guilty about?

3111
02:13:17,060 --> 02:13:19,660
Tae Gyun did make a mistake,

3112
02:13:20,160 --> 02:13:22,500
but it's definitely not his fault.

3113
02:13:22,500 --> 02:13:25,240
As his teammate...

3114
02:13:25,240 --> 02:13:27,770
and as an older member,
I was really sad to see him like that.

3115
02:13:28,170 --> 02:13:30,610
I regretted each and every moment.

3116
02:13:30,610 --> 02:13:33,180
"I should've done this instead of that."

3117
02:13:33,180 --> 02:13:35,850
If I'd survived...

3118
02:13:35,850 --> 02:13:38,120
and continued to kill people,

3119
02:13:38,120 --> 02:13:41,490
Tae Gyun might not have cried.

3120
02:13:41,490 --> 02:13:45,760
I regretted my every action.

3121
02:13:47,490 --> 02:13:49,630
The Money Challenge has ended.

3122
02:13:49,630 --> 02:13:51,530
Please gather in the main hall.

3123
02:13:54,300 --> 02:13:56,400
The winners
of today's Money Challenge are...

3124
02:13:56,870 --> 02:13:57,870
Kwak Beom,

3125
02:13:58,370 --> 02:13:59,370
Kang Ji Hoo,

3126
02:13:59,970 --> 02:14:00,970
Hyun Sung Joo,

3127
02:14:01,570 --> 02:14:02,570
Heo Seong Beom,

3128
02:14:03,040 --> 02:14:04,040
Choi Hye Seon,

3129
02:14:04,440 --> 02:14:06,280
and Shin Seung Yong.

3130
02:14:11,750 --> 02:14:15,650
The winners,
please enter the Voting Room...

3131
02:14:16,120 --> 02:14:18,760
and collect 20,000 dollars
of personal funds.

3132
02:14:18,760 --> 02:14:19,790
It's 20,000 dollars.

3133
02:14:19,790 --> 02:14:22,430
Here is 20,000 dollars
for winning the Money Challenge.

3134
02:14:24,830 --> 02:14:25,830
Is this mine?

3135
02:14:26,230 --> 02:14:27,460
Please deposit it.

3136
02:14:28,130 --> 02:14:29,670
I'm always dreaming of that day.

3137
02:14:29,670 --> 02:14:31,270
The day when I win, withdraw all the cash,

3138
02:14:31,270 --> 02:14:33,040
and throw them on Yanghwa Bridge...

3139
02:14:33,040 --> 02:14:34,240
like a movie scene.

3140
02:14:34,240 --> 02:14:35,410
I'm dreaming of that day.

3141
02:14:38,210 --> 02:14:40,710
My personal funds grew to 30,000 dollars.

3142
02:14:40,710 --> 02:14:42,310
It's not a small amount of money.

3143
02:14:42,310 --> 02:14:45,050
Now, I can buy any item.

3144
02:14:46,250 --> 02:14:47,250
My gosh.

3145
02:14:47,550 --> 02:14:48,950
Thank you.

3146
02:14:49,890 --> 02:14:51,520
I'm glad I won.

3147
02:14:51,520 --> 02:14:53,690
In the end, the citizens won.

3148
02:14:53,690 --> 02:14:54,990
I'm so happy.

3149
02:14:55,230 --> 02:14:59,000
Next, I will announce
the elimination candidates.

3150
02:14:59,330 --> 02:15:02,130
The losers
of today's Money Challenge are...

3151
02:15:02,570 --> 02:15:03,630
Park Ji Min,

3152
02:15:04,230 --> 02:15:05,240
Lee Tae Gyun,

3153
02:15:05,770 --> 02:15:06,770
YunB,

3154
02:15:07,300 --> 02:15:08,310
Hong Jin Ho,

3155
02:15:08,970 --> 02:15:09,970
Jeong Keun Woo,

3156
02:15:10,240 --> 02:15:12,140
and Xitsuh.

3157
02:15:12,540 --> 02:15:17,550
The number of players
to join the Deathmatch is four.

3158
02:15:19,750 --> 02:15:23,120
Since there are six losers,

3159
02:15:23,390 --> 02:15:25,290
the winners will vote to decide...

3160
02:15:25,490 --> 02:15:29,330
two players for the Deathmatch.

3161
02:15:29,930 --> 02:15:33,860
And the two players chosen by the votes...

3162
02:15:33,860 --> 02:15:36,100
will each select their opponent.

3163
02:15:36,100 --> 02:15:39,640
Thus, four players in total
will participate in the Deathmatch.

3164
02:15:41,070 --> 02:15:44,170
First, the six winners will vote...

3165
02:15:44,170 --> 02:15:47,640
for the two players for the Deathmatch.

3166
02:15:47,980 --> 02:15:48,980
My gosh.

3167
02:15:50,510 --> 02:15:52,220
Shall we have a discussion, then?

3168
02:15:52,220 --> 02:15:55,220
I was very glad
that the citizens have won,

3169
02:15:55,390 --> 02:15:56,550
but when I looked around,

3170
02:15:56,720 --> 02:15:58,590
the citizens, who've won alongside me,

3171
02:15:58,660 --> 02:16:01,420
were those who've been going against me.

3172
02:16:01,420 --> 02:16:03,290
Rather, those who've become
the elimination candidates...

3173
02:16:03,290 --> 02:16:04,830
have been playing the games with me.

3174
02:16:04,830 --> 02:16:07,730
Xitsuh, Jin Ho, Ji Min,
Keun Woo, and Tae Gyun.

3175
02:16:07,730 --> 02:16:09,000
That was the situation.

3176
02:16:10,030 --> 02:16:11,870
Please save me.

3177
02:16:11,870 --> 02:16:13,470
Please save me.

3178
02:16:13,470 --> 02:16:15,410
- Please save me.
- My gosh.

3179
02:16:15,410 --> 02:16:17,840
- Please save me.
- No, I...

3180
02:16:17,840 --> 02:16:19,240
- Xitsuh.
- I...

3181
02:16:19,240 --> 02:16:21,110
Until just now, you were saying,
"I'll kill everyone."

3182
02:16:21,110 --> 02:16:22,910
- Please save me.
- My gosh.

3183
02:16:22,910 --> 02:16:25,350
I can't believe a player from Team P3
is kneeling in front of me.

3184
02:16:25,880 --> 02:16:28,350
I did my best until the end, Beom.

3185
02:16:28,350 --> 02:16:29,750
I know. He...

3186
02:16:29,750 --> 02:16:32,190
- Shall we all discuss in the pantry?
- Yes.

3187
02:16:32,190 --> 02:16:34,320
- I did my best until the end.
- I know.

3188
02:16:34,320 --> 02:16:35,560
- You're right.
- I told you everything.

3189
02:16:35,560 --> 02:16:37,590
We do owe a big part of the victory
to Xitsuh.

3190
02:16:37,590 --> 02:16:38,760
Please save me.

3191
02:16:38,760 --> 02:16:41,360
We can't kill off so many of them
if we don't make use of this chance.

3192
02:16:41,530 --> 02:16:43,700
They'd beat us in all the games.

3193
02:16:43,970 --> 02:16:45,900
They'd definitely pick me, then.

3194
02:16:46,540 --> 02:16:48,970
They would vote
for two formidable players.

3195
02:16:49,240 --> 02:16:51,210
I think they'd pick two...

3196
02:16:51,210 --> 02:16:52,980
out of me, Xitsuh, and Jin Ho.

3197
02:16:52,980 --> 02:16:54,140
- That's possible.
- Yes.

3198
02:16:55,050 --> 02:16:57,080
First of all, congratulations on winning.

3199
02:16:57,080 --> 02:16:59,450
- I can't believe...
- I'm scared of them coming back alive.

3200
02:16:59,450 --> 02:17:01,550
I can't believe we're having this moment.

3201
02:17:01,550 --> 02:17:03,590
- But...
- Let's savor this moment for a bit.

3202
02:17:04,750 --> 02:17:07,860
I'd like to talk about those
whom we'd exclude from the voting.

3203
02:17:08,260 --> 02:17:10,760
Out of everyone,

3204
02:17:11,390 --> 02:17:15,870
Xitsuh sided with us citizens
throughout the game...

3205
02:17:15,870 --> 02:17:17,730
until he was killed off by the killer.

3206
02:17:17,730 --> 02:17:20,070
So I'm willing to save him.

3207
02:17:20,070 --> 02:17:23,640
In my opinion,
he said he sided with the citizens,

3208
02:17:23,970 --> 02:17:26,080
but he just did
what benefited him the most.

3209
02:17:26,080 --> 02:17:27,310
He did what benefited him, yes,

3210
02:17:27,310 --> 02:17:29,910
but in the end,
we could catch the killer...

3211
02:17:29,910 --> 02:17:31,380
because he played the bridge.

3212
02:17:31,380 --> 02:17:32,520
- It was Xitsuh.
- Seong Beom...

3213
02:17:32,680 --> 02:17:33,950
Actually,

3214
02:17:33,950 --> 02:17:37,020
Xitsuh played a very big role
in today's victory.

3215
02:17:37,420 --> 02:17:40,160
To keep his promise with me,

3216
02:17:40,160 --> 02:17:42,960
he helped us citizens with the deductions
as much as he could.

3217
02:17:43,290 --> 02:17:46,830
I thought we should not send Xitsuh
to play the Deathmatch.

3218
02:17:46,930 --> 02:17:49,270
I told Xitsuh that I was suspicious of...

3219
02:17:49,270 --> 02:17:50,970
Ji Min and Tae Gyun.

3220
02:17:50,970 --> 02:17:54,240
I can't be sure
because I wasn't there to see,

3221
02:17:54,240 --> 02:17:57,010
and he might've been fierce and intense
in how he expressed himself,

3222
02:17:57,010 --> 02:17:58,940
but I think he did his utmost best...

3223
02:17:58,940 --> 02:18:01,280
to help the citizens
and end the game fast.

3224
02:18:01,280 --> 02:18:03,510
Right. And I went into the room...

3225
02:18:04,180 --> 02:18:06,150
to try and arrest the killer quickly...

3226
02:18:06,150 --> 02:18:07,250
thanks to Xitsuh.

3227
02:18:10,850 --> 02:18:12,590
We can't allow that. We must kill Xitsuh.

3228
02:18:13,620 --> 02:18:15,990
Okay, let's exclude Xitsuh, then.

3229
02:18:15,990 --> 02:18:18,230
No, let us think about this for a moment.

3230
02:18:18,230 --> 02:18:19,900
Normally, for votes like this,

3231
02:18:20,130 --> 02:18:23,600
we vote for those who played a big part
in the loss of the game.

3232
02:18:23,600 --> 02:18:26,040
But the bigger justification would be...

3233
02:18:26,040 --> 02:18:28,370
for us to get closer to winning the show
as much as possible.

3234
02:18:28,370 --> 02:18:30,710
- That's right. We should think about it.
- That's the fundamental justification.

3235
02:18:30,710 --> 02:18:32,040
- Yes.
- Just because...

3236
02:18:32,040 --> 02:18:34,140
he played as our ally
in the previous game,

3237
02:18:34,140 --> 02:18:37,810
it doesn't give us enough reason
not to vote for him.

3238
02:18:37,810 --> 02:18:40,780
So I think everyone can agree...

3239
02:18:40,780 --> 02:18:43,150
that we should vote for 2 out of these 3.

3240
02:18:43,150 --> 02:18:45,020
What do you think? Any objection?

3241
02:18:49,790 --> 02:18:51,960
Still, we need to vote for those
we can justify voting for.

3242
02:18:51,960 --> 02:18:53,700
It may be our choice, but still.

3243
02:18:53,700 --> 02:18:55,270
I think we should vote for Tae Gyun.

3244
02:18:55,270 --> 02:18:57,270
- We agree on that.
- But...

3245
02:18:57,270 --> 02:18:58,400
You don't agree?

3246
02:18:58,400 --> 02:18:59,470
Because he was on your team?

3247
02:18:59,470 --> 02:19:01,100
My team or not,

3248
02:19:01,100 --> 02:19:04,810
I don't know what goals you had in mind
when you came here,

3249
02:19:04,810 --> 02:19:06,610
and winning the show is important,
of course.

3250
02:19:06,610 --> 02:19:08,580
But the process...

3251
02:19:08,580 --> 02:19:10,210
- You want it to look good?
- I want it to look good.

3252
02:19:10,210 --> 02:19:12,380
That way, we can be more proud
of ourselves.

3253
02:19:12,380 --> 02:19:13,380
Exactly.

3254
02:19:13,380 --> 02:19:15,350
You're looking for the justification
within the game itself.

3255
02:19:15,350 --> 02:19:17,450
Yes. So I think...

3256
02:19:18,050 --> 02:19:20,890
Well, that's how Seong Beom is.

3257
02:19:20,890 --> 02:19:22,030
We're just very different.

3258
02:19:22,290 --> 02:19:24,330
What he said did sound reasonable.

3259
02:19:24,330 --> 02:19:27,100
But it doesn't mean
I have to agree with him.

3260
02:19:27,430 --> 02:19:30,900
And I don't know how long
the strong bond of Team P3...

3261
02:19:30,900 --> 02:19:32,540
will last.

3262
02:19:32,540 --> 02:19:34,000
Anyway,

3263
02:19:34,000 --> 02:19:35,710
- I...
- Let's all share our thoughts.

3264
02:19:35,710 --> 02:19:37,970
I think everyone has sensible reasons.

3265
02:19:37,970 --> 02:19:40,880
I'll vote according to what I think.

3266
02:19:40,880 --> 02:19:42,310
Whatever others say,

3267
02:19:42,310 --> 02:19:43,810
I respect that,

3268
02:19:43,810 --> 02:19:44,850
and I'm not going to force...

3269
02:19:44,850 --> 02:19:46,480
- my principles on you.
- What are your principles?

3270
02:19:47,180 --> 02:19:49,320
I just think it'd be nice
to vote for the two who would...

3271
02:19:49,320 --> 02:19:51,650
- put up a good fight against each other.
- Yes, you can think that.

3272
02:19:51,650 --> 02:19:53,090
- So who are those people?
- That's sexy.

3273
02:19:53,420 --> 02:19:55,760
Tae Gyun and Jin Ho...

3274
02:19:55,760 --> 02:19:57,260
or Tae Gyun and Xitsuh.

3275
02:19:57,260 --> 02:19:59,860
So is everyone okay with Tae Gyun?

3276
02:19:59,860 --> 02:20:02,370
You don't exactly prefer
one over the other, right?

3277
02:20:02,800 --> 02:20:04,930
- Who?
- Jin Ho and Xitsuh.

3278
02:20:05,740 --> 02:20:09,240
If we're discussing
just based on this game,

3279
02:20:09,610 --> 02:20:11,110
I'm okay with it.

3280
02:20:11,110 --> 02:20:13,680
Everyone agreed on Tae Gyun.

3281
02:20:14,010 --> 02:20:17,680
As for these two,
we can just choose who we want.

3282
02:20:17,680 --> 02:20:20,780
If I must choose
between Xitsuh and Jin Ho...

3283
02:20:20,780 --> 02:20:23,390
Xitsuh still did something.

3284
02:20:23,590 --> 02:20:25,320
Whether it was for himself or for us.

3285
02:20:25,320 --> 02:20:27,660
- On the other hand,
- That's right.

3286
02:20:27,660 --> 02:20:30,530
- Jin Ho didn't do much as a psychopath.
- Yes.

3287
02:20:30,530 --> 02:20:33,000
So who do you each want to vote for?

3288
02:20:33,660 --> 02:20:35,470
You're asking because you're curious.

3289
02:20:35,470 --> 02:20:36,970
I'm not asking solely out of curiosity.

3290
02:20:36,970 --> 02:20:39,700
We can't have the votes split among us.

3291
02:20:40,170 --> 02:20:42,770
I'll vote for Tae Gyun, then.

3292
02:20:43,510 --> 02:20:46,140
I think I'll vote for Tae Gyun too.

3293
02:20:46,140 --> 02:20:47,280
You'll vote for Tae Gyun?

3294
02:20:47,280 --> 02:20:49,350
Okay. Sung Joo will vote for Tae Gyun.

3295
02:20:49,910 --> 02:20:51,650
I'll vote for him too.

3296
02:20:52,220 --> 02:20:53,220
What?

3297
02:20:53,220 --> 02:20:55,150
- I'll vote for Jin Ho.
- Jin Ho.

3298
02:20:56,050 --> 02:20:57,890
I'll vote for Keun Woo.

3299
02:20:57,890 --> 02:20:58,890
Keun Woo?

3300
02:20:59,590 --> 02:21:01,520
In that case,

3301
02:21:02,190 --> 02:21:04,490
I'll vote for Jin Ho.

3302
02:21:05,060 --> 02:21:06,160
Then it's decided.

3303
02:21:06,930 --> 02:21:08,530
- I'll go first.
- Over there...

3304
02:21:08,530 --> 02:21:10,230
Four of us should talk about it again.

3305
02:21:11,130 --> 02:21:14,400
I don't think my opinion matters anyway.

3306
02:21:15,470 --> 02:21:17,610
We don't need to discuss.
It's funny talking about it anyway.

3307
02:21:17,940 --> 02:21:19,580
She left, saying she'd vote for Keun Woo.

3308
02:21:20,040 --> 02:21:22,480
That's how she shirks responsibility.

3309
02:21:22,480 --> 02:21:24,580
Voting for Keun Woo is
practically making her vote void.

3310
02:21:24,780 --> 02:21:28,990
I played with both Jin Ho and Xitsuh,

3311
02:21:28,990 --> 02:21:30,320
so I didn't want to vote for them.

3312
02:21:30,320 --> 02:21:33,860
Tae Gyun played very well yesterday too.

3313
02:21:33,860 --> 02:21:36,430
If I had to find fault among them,

3314
02:21:36,430 --> 02:21:40,900
Tae Gyun and Ji Min failed
to play well as the killer faction.

3315
02:21:46,700 --> 02:21:48,610
But I think...

3316
02:21:48,610 --> 02:21:51,910
if Keun Woo was involved a bit more today,

3317
02:21:52,180 --> 02:21:56,350
the killer faction wouldn't have lost
so helplessly.

3318
02:21:57,050 --> 02:22:01,180
So I wanted to hold Keun Woo
a bit more accountable than the others.

3319
02:22:02,420 --> 02:22:05,920
(Choi Hye Seon votes for Jeong Keun Woo.)

3320
02:22:05,990 --> 02:22:09,460
I think we should vote for Jin Ho too.

3321
02:22:09,460 --> 02:22:12,600
- He'd want to showcase his skills by now.
- Yes.

3322
02:22:12,600 --> 02:22:14,430
We can respect that.

3323
02:22:18,870 --> 02:22:20,700
He wouldn't want this.

3324
02:22:23,040 --> 02:22:26,080
Hye Seon made her vote void.

3325
02:22:26,340 --> 02:22:27,580
- Let's discuss among ourselves.
- What?

3326
02:22:27,580 --> 02:22:29,510
- Let's discuss among ourselves.
- Hye Seon made her vote void.

3327
02:22:29,510 --> 02:22:31,950
Aren't we going to vote as discussed?

3328
02:22:31,950 --> 02:22:33,320
Are you going to change your vote, Ji Hoo?

3329
02:22:33,320 --> 02:22:34,550
To whom?

3330
02:22:34,550 --> 02:22:37,290
Wouldn't it be for the best
to send Jin Ho and Xitsuh?

3331
02:22:37,720 --> 02:22:38,760
- What?
- What?

3332
02:22:53,300 --> 02:22:55,440
- Is there more to discuss?
- No.

3333
02:22:55,440 --> 02:22:57,270
I think Ji Hoo has an opinion to raise.

3334
02:22:58,410 --> 02:22:59,610
You want to talk?

3335
02:23:03,080 --> 02:23:04,350
- But...
- Yes.

3336
02:23:04,650 --> 02:23:07,320
will it change the result of the voting?

3337
02:23:07,550 --> 02:23:10,690
If yes, you should've said it
before Hye Seon went to vote.

3338
02:23:10,820 --> 02:23:11,990
Oh...

3339
02:23:14,720 --> 02:23:15,790
We can do as you say,

3340
02:23:15,790 --> 02:23:16,860
- but anyway,
- Yes.

3341
02:23:16,860 --> 02:23:18,630
Hye Seon went to vote first
because we've decided.

3342
02:23:20,330 --> 02:23:22,530
Well, that's up to Ji Hoo.

3343
02:23:22,530 --> 02:23:23,530
Yes.

3344
02:23:23,830 --> 02:23:25,870
It's my freedom to speak my mind.

3345
02:23:25,870 --> 02:23:28,070
Can I listen to it,
or would you like me to leave?

3346
02:23:28,070 --> 02:23:30,240
- I don't want you to listen.
- Is that so? Okay.

3347
02:23:30,240 --> 02:23:31,840
The KAIST battle is scary.

3348
02:23:32,780 --> 02:23:33,780
What do you want to do?

3349
02:23:33,780 --> 02:23:34,780
Isn't that for the best?

3350
02:23:41,680 --> 02:23:43,490
They're freaking idiots.

3351
02:23:43,650 --> 02:23:45,660
This sucks. They're all wimps.

3352
02:23:45,660 --> 02:23:47,620
- What?
- I want to kill all of them.

3353
02:23:47,620 --> 02:23:49,390
They want to vote for strong players, no?

3354
02:23:49,390 --> 02:23:50,790
That's one thing,

3355
02:23:50,790 --> 02:23:51,860
and they don't have a justification.

3356
02:23:51,860 --> 02:23:54,130
We discussed and decided who to vote for,
so Hye Seon went and voted.

3357
02:23:54,130 --> 02:23:56,470
Suddenly, Ji Hoo says he has another idea,

3358
02:23:56,470 --> 02:23:58,770
and they're going to change
who to vote for.

3359
02:24:00,070 --> 02:24:01,700
You must be pissed.

3360
02:24:02,040 --> 02:24:03,940
When I was about to go and vote,

3361
02:24:03,940 --> 02:24:06,040
Ji Hoo suddenly held the people back.

3362
02:24:06,040 --> 02:24:07,710
"Wait."

3363
02:24:08,140 --> 02:24:10,450
Seeing that...

3364
02:24:11,180 --> 02:24:13,980
triggered my pent-up frustration
from earlier,

3365
02:24:13,980 --> 02:24:15,390
and I was this close to exploding.

3366
02:24:15,390 --> 02:24:17,550
"What's wrong with these guys?"

3367
02:24:18,250 --> 02:24:19,360
They're such wimps.

3368
02:24:19,360 --> 02:24:21,260
"I just need to survive today."

3369
02:24:21,260 --> 02:24:22,390
"I don't care how the game went today."

3370
02:24:22,390 --> 02:24:23,890
"It doesn't matter who helped me."

3371
02:24:23,890 --> 02:24:25,660
"I just need to survive today."

3372
02:24:25,660 --> 02:24:26,960
"Let's send off the strong guys."

3373
02:24:27,660 --> 02:24:30,270
And Team P3...

3374
02:24:30,570 --> 02:24:31,570
What?

3375
02:24:31,570 --> 02:24:33,500
- Can we talk among ourselves?
- We're talking.

3376
02:24:34,540 --> 02:24:35,540
Why?

3377
02:24:37,010 --> 02:24:39,580
- Ji Hoo wants to talk among ourselves.
- We are talking about something.

3378
02:24:40,110 --> 02:24:41,880
Well, okay, but this is...

3379
02:24:42,550 --> 02:24:43,780
I'll tell you the filtered version later.

3380
02:24:43,780 --> 02:24:45,110
- Okay.
- Filtered version?

3381
02:24:46,620 --> 02:24:48,720
- They're too much.
- What is it?

3382
02:24:48,720 --> 02:24:51,550
They're too attached
to their own inner circle.

3383
02:24:51,790 --> 02:24:53,390
- What do you mean?
- We're all on the winning side,

3384
02:24:53,390 --> 02:24:55,260
- but they won't even let us join them.
- Really?

3385
02:24:55,260 --> 02:24:56,260
The moment I went there,
Seung Yong was like,

3386
02:24:56,260 --> 02:24:57,490
"We'll talk among ourselves."

3387
02:24:57,490 --> 02:24:58,830
- He told me to leave.
- Who?

3388
02:24:58,830 --> 02:25:00,660
- Seung Yong.
- They're such eyesores.

3389
02:25:00,660 --> 02:25:02,400
They're the public enemy.

3390
02:25:02,400 --> 02:25:03,400
At this point...

3391
02:25:03,400 --> 02:25:06,040
- I hate them so much.
- There's no reason to do that.

3392
02:25:06,040 --> 02:25:08,940
I think they've been holding a grudge
since yesterday's Equation Combo.

3393
02:25:09,070 --> 02:25:12,010
And Ji Hoo is being
way too confrontational with me.

3394
02:25:13,010 --> 02:25:15,140
Guess he wants to beat me
in one way or another.

3395
02:25:15,140 --> 02:25:19,450
Ji Hoo got triggered by you...

3396
02:25:19,450 --> 02:25:21,180
yesterday.
From playing the Equation Combo.

3397
02:25:21,180 --> 02:25:22,690
- To go that far...
- He lost because...

3398
02:25:22,690 --> 02:25:23,750
- he was bad at it.
- Exactly.

3399
02:25:23,750 --> 02:25:24,950
- What's there to be triggered?
- Exactly.

3400
02:25:24,950 --> 02:25:27,020
He's getting back at you
in such petty way.

3401
02:25:27,020 --> 02:25:28,320
He's getting back at me
by changing the voting results...

3402
02:25:28,320 --> 02:25:29,630
which we've already decided on?

3403
02:25:29,860 --> 02:25:31,730
Exactly. He's a wimp. A loser.

3404
02:25:32,130 --> 02:25:34,130
He was angry at Seong Beom yesterday.

3405
02:25:34,560 --> 02:25:37,470
They do say revenge is a best dish
served cold, but this...

3406
02:25:38,530 --> 02:25:40,200
I even thought if he was possessed
by an evil spirit...

3407
02:25:40,200 --> 02:25:42,740
because he couldn't get over the defeat
of Equation Combo.

3408
02:25:42,740 --> 02:25:44,840
I don't think I acted that way
when I was his age.

3409
02:25:45,170 --> 02:25:49,910
Actually, I still had residual emotions
from the heist.

3410
02:25:49,910 --> 02:25:53,250
So the fact
that the elimination candidates...

3411
02:25:53,250 --> 02:25:57,550
had the people
from Team Outdoor Alliance...

3412
02:25:57,550 --> 02:25:59,390
was upsetting for me.

3413
02:26:00,190 --> 02:26:02,890
I'm sorry, but whoever ends up
in the Deathmatch...

3414
02:26:03,190 --> 02:26:05,230
must do your utmost best to come back...

3415
02:26:05,230 --> 02:26:06,300
- to everyone here.
- That's a given.

3416
02:26:14,540 --> 02:26:16,340
Prove yourself.

3417
02:26:18,110 --> 02:26:20,510
Tae Gyun is very good
at all the other games,

3418
02:26:20,510 --> 02:26:23,280
but he was lacking in today's game,

3419
02:26:23,280 --> 02:26:25,520
and that led to his defeat.

3420
02:26:25,520 --> 02:26:27,380
It wouldn't be bad
for him to prove himself...

3421
02:26:27,380 --> 02:26:29,550
in the Deathmatch.

3422
02:26:29,790 --> 02:26:32,690
(Heo Seong Beom votes for Lee Tae Gyun.)

3423
02:26:33,660 --> 02:26:35,320
Isn't it better to send Jin Ho and Xitsuh?

3424
02:26:36,160 --> 02:26:38,030
Can I ask why?

3425
02:26:38,900 --> 02:26:41,600
I don't know what their reason is,

3426
02:26:41,600 --> 02:26:44,100
but they think it's better to save Xitsuh
and send Jin Ho.

3427
02:26:44,100 --> 02:26:46,100
- Yes, Tae Gyun and Jin Ho.
- Yes.

3428
02:26:46,100 --> 02:26:49,110
They need to send 1 of the 2,

3429
02:26:49,110 --> 02:26:50,410
and although they're reluctant
to let both go,

3430
02:26:50,410 --> 02:26:52,280
Team P3...

3431
02:26:52,780 --> 02:26:54,340
- chose Xitsuh.
- Yes.

3432
02:26:54,340 --> 02:26:57,210
So it's better to turn the tables.
Is it not?

3433
02:26:57,210 --> 02:27:00,250
So you just want
to go against what they say?

3434
02:27:00,250 --> 02:27:04,420
Those two simply notified us
of their decisions.

3435
02:27:04,420 --> 02:27:06,720
- And I don't like that.
- I understand.

3436
02:27:06,720 --> 02:27:09,060
I wanted to vote for Jin Ho and Xitsuh.

3437
02:27:09,060 --> 02:27:12,630
I wanted to eliminate
as many Team P3 players as possible.

3438
02:27:12,930 --> 02:27:17,000
"We must find the justification
for the voting within the game."

3439
02:27:17,000 --> 02:27:18,270
That was his argument.

3440
02:27:18,270 --> 02:27:20,340
I don't understand.

3441
02:27:20,870 --> 02:27:22,910
Even if we form an alliance in the future,

3442
02:27:22,910 --> 02:27:25,340
Tae Gyun has a higher chance
of helping us.

3443
02:27:25,840 --> 02:27:28,180
Even if we voted for Tae Gyun,

3444
02:27:28,180 --> 02:27:29,650
he would make it back alive.

3445
02:27:29,650 --> 02:27:31,780
- Yes.
- That's right.

3446
02:27:31,780 --> 02:27:33,620
I think he'll make it back
even if we vote for him.

3447
02:27:33,620 --> 02:27:36,490
But Xitsuh and Jin Ho
could make a mistake and lose.

3448
02:27:36,820 --> 02:27:38,420
- It doesn't really matter to me.
- Me too.

3449
02:27:38,420 --> 02:27:41,290
If that's what you want, Ji Hoo,
I'm willing to follow.

3450
02:27:41,290 --> 02:27:42,790
- Anyway, they...
- This...

3451
02:27:42,790 --> 02:27:44,190
One by one...

3452
02:27:45,330 --> 02:27:47,230
- You want to send them off?
- Let's try it.

3453
02:27:47,230 --> 02:27:48,360
Let's do it.

3454
02:27:48,760 --> 02:27:51,400
We'll continue to be at odds with Team P3,

3455
02:27:51,670 --> 02:27:53,170
and they're way too strong.

3456
02:27:53,170 --> 02:27:55,340
This was a perfect chance to weaken them.

3457
02:27:59,440 --> 02:28:01,580
I talked with the guys from Team Rookie,

3458
02:28:01,580 --> 02:28:03,710
and they were thinking the same thing.

3459
02:28:03,710 --> 02:28:06,180
How can we eliminate him
when he's so good?

3460
02:28:06,180 --> 02:28:07,650
This is the only kind of game
we can eliminate him.

3461
02:28:07,650 --> 02:28:09,020
We must grab the chance while we can.

3462
02:28:22,370 --> 02:28:24,330
The voting has ended.

3463
02:28:24,330 --> 02:28:26,300
(The voting has ended.)

3464
02:28:26,640 --> 02:28:29,010
I will announce the voting results.

3465
02:28:29,740 --> 02:28:32,170
The first player
to play the Deathmatch is...

3466
02:28:37,180 --> 02:28:39,420
Hong Jin Ho.

3467
02:28:40,280 --> 02:28:41,280
Okay.

3468
02:28:41,280 --> 02:28:42,950
I'm pretty unfazed.

3469
02:28:42,950 --> 02:28:46,660
There was almost a 90 percent chance
I'd be chosen this time.

3470
02:28:46,660 --> 02:28:50,960
I felt that they were trying
to eliminate the strong players.

3471
02:28:51,760 --> 02:28:52,760
And...

3472
02:28:56,470 --> 02:28:59,800
Lee Tae Gyun.

3473
02:28:59,970 --> 02:29:00,970
Thank you.

3474
02:29:02,570 --> 02:29:03,870
As I thought, they voted for me.

3475
02:29:04,210 --> 02:29:05,270
Rather,

3476
02:29:05,410 --> 02:29:08,480
thank you for allowing me
to take responsibility.

3477
02:29:08,480 --> 02:29:10,250
Those two are scary.

3478
02:29:14,920 --> 02:29:16,890
But think about it.

3479
02:29:16,890 --> 02:29:19,020
If we vote for Tae Gyun,
who would he vote for?

3480
02:29:19,020 --> 02:29:20,890
He wouldn't vote for Keun Woo or Ji Min.

3481
02:29:20,890 --> 02:29:21,890
He wouldn't.

3482
02:29:22,190 --> 02:29:23,560
And Xitsuh...

3483
02:29:23,560 --> 02:29:24,560
I think he'll vote for YunB.

3484
02:29:24,560 --> 02:29:25,660
- Yes.
- Out of them...

3485
02:29:25,660 --> 02:29:26,900
He'll vote for YunB.

3486
02:29:27,460 --> 02:29:30,900
But I think Tae Gyun will vote for Xitsuh.

3487
02:29:31,100 --> 02:29:33,900
Because he'll want to save
Ji Min and Keun Woo.

3488
02:29:34,200 --> 02:29:36,970
Then wouldn't Jin Ho pick YunB?

3489
02:29:36,970 --> 02:29:38,510
I think that's the best-case scenario.

3490
02:29:38,510 --> 02:29:40,110
Then we should vote for Tae Gyun.

3491
02:29:40,310 --> 02:29:42,210
That's true too.

3492
02:29:42,210 --> 02:29:44,010
Voting for Tae Gyun and Jin Ho
sounds good to me.

3493
02:29:44,010 --> 02:29:45,410
One from each team.

3494
02:29:45,820 --> 02:29:47,680
- So what we discussed initially?
- I think that's for the best.

3495
02:29:47,680 --> 02:29:48,880
We've talked enough about it,

3496
02:29:48,880 --> 02:29:50,590
and I understand your point.

3497
02:29:50,990 --> 02:29:55,860
Tae Gyun, Jin Ho, and Xitsuh
are too strong.

3498
02:29:55,860 --> 02:29:57,560
So we were thinking who to vote for.

3499
02:29:57,560 --> 02:30:00,630
We wanted to vote for Jin Ho...

3500
02:30:00,630 --> 02:30:02,900
so that there's a chance of Tae Gyun...

3501
02:30:02,900 --> 02:30:04,600
picking Xitsuh as his opponent.

3502
02:30:04,600 --> 02:30:07,400
So I insisted on voting
for Tae Gyun and Jin Ho.

3503
02:30:07,870 --> 02:30:09,340
I'm voting for you
because I know you'll win.

3504
02:30:10,270 --> 02:30:13,510
(Hyun Sung Joo votes for Lee Tae Gyun.)

3505
02:30:14,980 --> 02:30:18,410
(Kang Ji Hoo votes for Lee Tae Gyun.)

3506
02:30:18,810 --> 02:30:21,880
Jin Ho is one of the most formidable
winning candidates,

3507
02:30:22,250 --> 02:30:25,650
so I thought I should vote for him.

3508
02:30:25,920 --> 02:30:27,020
Jin Ho, you're the best.

3509
02:30:28,290 --> 02:30:30,860
(Shin Seung Yong votes for Hong Jin Ho.)

3510
02:30:35,630 --> 02:30:38,930
(Kwak Beom votes for Hong Jin Ho.)

3511
02:30:39,440 --> 02:30:43,210
Lee Tae Gyun and Hong Jin Ho,
please enter the Voting Room separately...

3512
02:30:43,640 --> 02:30:47,510
and select your Deathmatch opponent.

3513
02:30:49,580 --> 02:30:51,710
This is so hard.

3514
02:30:52,350 --> 02:30:55,750
I need to select the Deathmatch opponent
among them.

3515
02:30:56,490 --> 02:30:57,550
This is so hard.

3516
02:30:58,050 --> 02:31:02,220
I wasn't in the place
to give it a lot of thought.

3517
02:31:02,220 --> 02:31:05,530
The candidates were Ji Min,

3518
02:31:05,760 --> 02:31:08,930
YunB, and Keun Woo. One of the three.

3519
02:31:12,440 --> 02:31:14,140
Hello.

3520
02:31:18,770 --> 02:31:22,380
Please select a player for the Deathmatch.

3521
02:31:28,450 --> 02:31:30,050
Seriously...

3522
02:31:30,050 --> 02:31:33,720
Please select a player for the Deathmatch.

3523
02:31:38,860 --> 02:31:41,300
