3533
02:32:04,820 --> 02:32:07,620
The biggest reason is,

3534
02:32:07,620 --> 02:32:09,390
he looked like the easiest opponent.

3535
02:32:09,390 --> 02:32:11,660
I was 100 percent sure
Jin Ho would choose me.

3536
02:32:13,030 --> 02:32:15,360
The next Deathmatch player is...

3537
02:32:18,730 --> 02:32:20,240
(Xitsuh)

3538
02:32:20,240 --> 02:32:22,910
Xitsuh.

3539
02:32:24,240 --> 02:32:25,670
Goodness.

3540
02:32:25,670 --> 02:32:28,210
My gosh.

3541
02:32:28,810 --> 02:32:31,010
Since I'm playing the Deathmatch anyway,

3542
02:32:31,950 --> 02:32:33,920
I'll play against the strongest player.

3543
02:32:35,280 --> 02:32:37,550
You have chosen Xitsuh.

3544
02:32:38,320 --> 02:32:41,220
How did it end up like this today?

3545
02:32:41,720 --> 02:32:43,590
Why am I on the list
of the Deathmatch players?

3546
02:32:44,190 --> 02:32:47,930
The only people I could choose
were Xitsuh and YunB.

3547
02:32:47,930 --> 02:32:51,730
And most importantly, when I was...

3548
02:32:51,730 --> 02:32:54,240
thinking about who to choose,

3549
02:32:54,640 --> 02:32:56,270
YunB spoke to me quietly.

3550
02:32:56,270 --> 02:32:57,470
I've just made it back alive.

3551
02:32:57,470 --> 02:32:58,540
- You?
- Yes.

3552
02:32:59,480 --> 02:33:00,840
Give me some time to breathe.

3553
02:33:02,080 --> 02:33:03,080
Please.

3554
02:33:04,780 --> 02:33:06,620
This...

3555
02:33:06,620 --> 02:33:09,950
He asked me
to give him some time to breathe.

3556
02:33:10,220 --> 02:33:13,590
He's not the type to swallow his pride
and show his weakness.

3557
02:33:13,590 --> 02:33:16,890
He really must be very exhausted. Okay.

3558
02:33:16,890 --> 02:33:20,030
Since I'm going to do it,
I might as well go against the strongest.

3559
02:33:20,330 --> 02:33:21,800
Goodness.

3560
02:33:24,500 --> 02:33:26,340
Regardless, thank you, guys.

3561
02:33:26,340 --> 02:33:27,340
Win and come back.

3562
02:33:27,340 --> 02:33:28,700
I was on the citizens' side.

3563
02:33:28,700 --> 02:33:30,070
Win and come back.

3564
02:33:31,170 --> 02:33:32,340
Come back proud.

3565
02:33:32,340 --> 02:33:33,340
Good luck.

3566
02:33:35,610 --> 02:33:39,150
I want Jin Ho and Xitsuh
to get eliminated.

3567
02:33:39,150 --> 02:33:42,050
The alliance of Team P3 is way too strong.

3568
02:33:42,220 --> 02:33:44,350
I want them to fall apart.

3569
02:33:44,350 --> 02:33:45,420
They have way too much money too.

3570
02:33:46,020 --> 02:33:49,260
I hope one of them except Keun Woo
would go home.

3571
02:33:49,260 --> 02:33:51,990
This is so hard.
They've raised the bar so high.

3572
02:33:52,330 --> 02:33:53,500
Please keep it balanced.

3573
02:33:54,800 --> 02:33:58,330
The Deathmatch players,
please gather in the main hall.

3574
02:34:01,040 --> 02:34:02,770
Goodness.

3575
02:34:02,770 --> 02:34:05,110
It feels like it's been ages
since I've played the Deathmatch.

3576
02:34:05,110 --> 02:34:06,580
- This...
- Do we just stand anywhere?

3577
02:34:06,910 --> 02:34:07,910
Yes.

3578
02:34:08,880 --> 02:34:13,550
Whenever I play a game, any kind of game,

3579
02:34:13,750 --> 02:34:17,420
I play with the mindset
that I can beat any opponent.

3580
02:34:17,750 --> 02:34:20,660
I believe my chances at victory go up
that way.

3581
02:34:20,760 --> 02:34:25,160
I will survive and go back to the mansion.

3582
02:34:26,830 --> 02:34:28,630
- Goodness.
- You're here.

3583
02:34:31,500 --> 02:34:33,470
I can't believe I'm joining you guys.

3584
02:34:33,470 --> 02:34:35,440
- I'm sorry.
- It's an honor.

3585
02:34:35,440 --> 02:34:37,340
You don't know how the game will turn out.

3586
02:34:37,340 --> 02:34:38,340
It's an honor.

3587
02:34:39,040 --> 02:34:41,310
I'll write history today.

3588
02:34:41,310 --> 02:34:42,650
I'll write history.

3589
02:34:43,050 --> 02:34:44,410
Who would ever have the chance...

3590
02:34:44,610 --> 02:34:47,880
to play the Deathmatch against...

3591
02:34:47,880 --> 02:34:52,150
Lee Tae Gyun, Xitsuh, and Hong Jin Ho
on a survival show?

3592
02:34:52,620 --> 02:34:53,620
But...

3593
02:34:54,520 --> 02:34:56,090
in the face of death,

3594
02:34:56,490 --> 02:34:58,090
I can never yield.

3595
02:34:59,300 --> 02:35:02,800
I've gone through thick and thin...

3596
02:35:03,200 --> 02:35:06,170
playing baseball and made it here.

3597
02:35:07,000 --> 02:35:08,800
I'm not a pushover.

3598
02:35:11,340 --> 02:35:13,910
Since I'm playing the Deathmatch
for the first time in a while,

3599
02:35:14,040 --> 02:35:15,440
I want to win.

3600
02:35:15,640 --> 02:35:16,650
Nowadays,

3601
02:35:17,210 --> 02:35:19,780
the younger players pull ahead,

3602
02:35:19,780 --> 02:35:23,350
and my position and stance have been...

3603
02:35:23,550 --> 02:35:26,460
to watch and support them.

3604
02:35:26,890 --> 02:35:28,490
I wanted to break away from it...

3605
02:35:28,490 --> 02:35:30,460
by winning today.

3606
02:35:32,630 --> 02:35:36,730
I'm grateful that Tae Gyun thought
I was a strong opponent,

3607
02:35:36,730 --> 02:35:40,470
but I also think he chose me regardless
because he still thought he could beat me.

3608
02:35:41,440 --> 02:35:43,740
Okay. You're in for trouble, Tae Gyun.

3609
02:35:43,740 --> 02:35:46,340
I'll balance it out for you.

3610
02:35:46,780 --> 02:35:47,780
Let's do this.

3611
02:35:49,850 --> 02:35:50,850
Hong Jin Ho,

3612
02:35:51,610 --> 02:35:52,610
Lee Tae Gyun,

3613
02:35:53,420 --> 02:35:55,480
Jeong Keun Woo, and Xitsuh.

3614
02:35:56,750 --> 02:36:00,690
The four players must play...

3615
02:36:00,690 --> 02:36:02,460
the 1-on-1-on-1-on-1 Deathmatch.

3616
02:36:03,430 --> 02:36:04,760
I will reveal...

3617
02:36:05,460 --> 02:36:08,000
today's Deathmatch.

3618
02:36:09,230 --> 02:36:10,670
Today's Deathmatch is...

3619
02:36:11,500 --> 02:36:12,630
(High and Low)

3620
02:36:12,630 --> 02:36:15,040
High and Low.

3621
02:36:16,370 --> 02:36:19,480
Through card management and mind games,

3622
02:36:19,680 --> 02:36:22,140
you must make the highest number
to win High and Low.

3623
02:36:23,410 --> 02:36:25,250
There will be a total of nine rounds.

3624
02:36:25,250 --> 02:36:28,150
Out of 10 point cards,
9 cards, excluding 1 random card,

3625
02:36:28,150 --> 02:36:31,150
will be shown each round.

3626
02:36:32,450 --> 02:36:35,920
Each player will be given
1 to 10 number cards,

3627
02:36:35,920 --> 02:36:37,990
a reverse card, which is a special card,

3628
02:36:37,990 --> 02:36:39,630
and a normal card.

3629
02:36:39,900 --> 02:36:42,030
The back of the number cards 1 to 5...

3630
02:36:42,030 --> 02:36:44,000
is blue.

3631
02:36:44,000 --> 02:36:47,040
The back of the number cards 6 to 10
are yellow.

3632
02:36:47,600 --> 02:36:50,170
After the point card is revealed,

3633
02:36:50,170 --> 02:36:51,670
you will put one number card...

3634
02:36:51,670 --> 02:36:54,140
upon one special card and submit them.

3635
02:36:55,910 --> 02:36:57,310
Once the cards have been submitted,

3636
02:36:57,310 --> 02:36:59,310
the special cards will be revealed first,

3637
02:36:59,310 --> 02:37:01,820
which will decide the number advantage
of the particular round.

3638
02:37:02,120 --> 02:37:04,750
If an odd number of reverse cards
is submitted,

3639
02:37:04,750 --> 02:37:06,160
the advantage of the numbers
will be reversed,

3640
02:37:06,160 --> 02:37:07,890
and the lowest number wins.

3641
02:37:08,290 --> 02:37:10,290
If an even number of reverse cards
is submitted,

3642
02:37:10,290 --> 02:37:11,760
they will cancel out each other,

3643
02:37:11,760 --> 02:37:13,860
and higher numbers
will remain advantageous.

3644
02:37:14,900 --> 02:37:19,670
However, players can use the reverse card
only once throughout the game.

3645
02:37:20,740 --> 02:37:24,170
The starting player will reveal
the front of their number card,

3646
02:37:24,170 --> 02:37:26,580
and the player who submitted
the most advantageous card...

3647
02:37:26,580 --> 02:37:29,110
wins the point card
of the particular round.

3648
02:37:29,780 --> 02:37:32,580
If you do not wish to reveal
the front of the card,

3649
02:37:32,580 --> 02:37:34,280
you can pass.

3650
02:37:34,680 --> 02:37:38,250
However, the starting player
and the player who has passed...

3651
02:37:38,250 --> 02:37:40,960
in the previous round
must reveal the front of the number card.

3652
02:37:41,560 --> 02:37:44,860
If the number cards
submitted by the players overlap,

3653
02:37:44,860 --> 02:37:47,430
the player
with the next most advantageous card...

3654
02:37:47,430 --> 02:37:49,160
wins the point card.

3655
02:37:49,930 --> 02:37:52,600
In the round with a negative point card,

3656
02:37:52,600 --> 02:37:55,340
the rules to win the point card
change slightly.

3657
02:37:56,040 --> 02:37:58,810
If a player passes the round,

3658
02:37:58,810 --> 02:38:01,440
that player will get the point card.

3659
02:38:01,940 --> 02:38:04,350
If there are two or more players
who've submitted the same number cards,

3660
02:38:04,350 --> 02:38:06,050
the player
who've acquired the point card...

3661
02:38:06,050 --> 02:38:08,420
can choose one of the players...

3662
02:38:08,420 --> 02:38:10,250
to hand over the point card.

3663
02:38:11,150 --> 02:38:14,290
Nine rounds will be played
following the rules,

3664
02:38:14,290 --> 02:38:18,390
and two players
with the highest total scores win.

3665
02:38:18,760 --> 02:38:20,060
If there's a draw,

3666
02:38:20,060 --> 02:38:23,430
the player with a higher point card wins.

3667
02:38:23,930 --> 02:38:27,140
We shall commence High and Low
in a minute.

3668
02:38:29,000 --> 02:38:30,910
You need to read your opponents' minds...

3669
02:38:30,910 --> 02:38:33,810
and make good combinations
with your own cards.

3670
02:38:33,810 --> 02:38:35,880
The rules themselves aren't complicated.

3671
02:38:35,880 --> 02:38:37,150
But...

3672
02:38:37,750 --> 02:38:40,250
anyone can win this game in a way.

3673
02:38:40,580 --> 02:38:42,620
This is the easiest game so far.

3674
02:38:44,390 --> 02:38:47,290
The game is advantageous to me.

3675
02:38:47,290 --> 02:38:50,590
You couldn't form an alliance
to play this game.

3676
02:38:50,590 --> 02:38:52,730
As long as I play my mind games right,

3677
02:38:52,730 --> 02:38:54,500
I can win this.

3678
02:38:54,500 --> 02:38:56,730
When there are four players,

3679
02:38:56,730 --> 02:38:58,700
the mind games become really complicated.

3680
02:38:58,700 --> 02:39:00,040
I should not get swayed...

3681
02:39:00,040 --> 02:39:03,670
and stick to my own playing style.

3682
02:39:04,140 --> 02:39:06,980
I'm more or less confident
in mind games too.

3683
02:39:06,980 --> 02:39:10,050
I could optimize the card management too.

3684
02:39:10,450 --> 02:39:13,920
We will begin today's Deathmatch.

3685
02:39:14,420 --> 02:39:16,790
The order will be decided
by drawing cards.

3686
02:39:16,790 --> 02:39:18,720
Please select one card each.

3687
02:39:18,720 --> 02:39:20,090
Give me the one closest to me.

3688
02:39:24,660 --> 02:39:26,530
Number one, Xitsuh.

3689
02:39:26,760 --> 02:39:28,460
Number two, Lee Tae Gyun.

3690
02:39:28,730 --> 02:39:30,500
Number three, Jeong Keun Woo.

3691
02:39:30,700 --> 02:39:33,170
Number four, Hong Jin Ho.

3692
02:39:34,170 --> 02:39:35,240
(Round 1 Playing Order)

3693
02:39:35,240 --> 02:39:37,910
(1: Xitsuh, 2: Lee Tae Gyun,
3: Jeong Keun Woo, 4: Hong Jin Ho)

3694
02:39:38,470 --> 02:39:42,110
Before the round starts,
I will remove a point card from the deck.

3695
02:39:42,880 --> 02:39:46,050
(A point card has been removed.)

3696
02:39:46,050 --> 02:39:48,320
Which point card will the dealer draw?

3697
02:39:48,320 --> 02:39:50,890
A good card or a minus card?
Depending on that,

3698
02:39:50,890 --> 02:39:52,320
I'll either go for it...

3699
02:39:52,320 --> 02:39:53,860
or avoid it.

3700
02:39:53,860 --> 02:39:55,420
I need to calculate it carefully...

3701
02:39:55,420 --> 02:39:57,090
and win the right cards
and avoid the wrong cards.

3702
02:39:57,090 --> 02:39:59,490
When you add up all the numbers,
you get plus five.

3703
02:39:59,490 --> 02:40:02,000
Split it among the 4 of us,
and it's plus 1 each.

3704
02:40:02,000 --> 02:40:05,270
Plus two is already a pretty decent point.

3705
02:40:05,270 --> 02:40:07,140
Let's make the number positive.

3706
02:40:07,140 --> 02:40:08,840
We will begin Round One.

3707
02:40:10,040 --> 02:40:13,310
The point card of this round
is minus five.

3708
02:40:13,980 --> 02:40:17,550
All players, please submit
your number card and special card.

3709
02:40:17,550 --> 02:40:21,650
(The Round 1 point card: Minus 5)

3710
02:40:21,650 --> 02:40:24,690
They can't read my mind.

3711
02:40:24,690 --> 02:40:26,960
During my days as a baseball player,

3712
02:40:26,960 --> 02:40:31,090
I've played many mind games
with countless ace pitchers.

3713
02:40:31,090 --> 02:40:32,760
Let's not get carried away.

3714
02:40:32,760 --> 02:40:33,760
But...

3715
02:40:33,900 --> 02:40:36,930
let's not try to make it perfect either.

3716
02:40:36,930 --> 02:40:38,730
Within reasons,

3717
02:40:38,730 --> 02:40:41,800
let's win not-so-good
but not-so-bad cards.

3718
02:40:42,100 --> 02:40:43,670
That was my strategy.

3719
02:40:43,670 --> 02:40:48,940
(The Round 1 point card: Minus 5)

3720
02:40:48,940 --> 02:40:50,680
Minus five point card...

3721
02:40:50,680 --> 02:40:53,080
isn't exactly a bad card.

3722
02:40:53,080 --> 02:40:54,750
There are cards
of number minus 7 and minus 9 too.

3723
02:40:54,750 --> 02:40:56,180
But I don't want to take it.

3724
02:40:56,180 --> 02:40:59,920
(The Round 1 point card: Minus 5)

3725
02:40:59,920 --> 02:41:00,920
Here.

3726
02:41:03,130 --> 02:41:04,130
Here.

3727
02:41:04,130 --> 02:41:06,290
(Xitsuh has submitted his cards.)

3728
02:41:06,290 --> 02:41:12,530
(The Round 1 point card: Minus 5)

3729
02:41:12,530 --> 02:41:14,300
(Lee Tae Gyun has submitted his cards.)

3730
02:41:14,300 --> 02:41:15,300
This is hard.

3731
02:41:17,040 --> 02:41:19,570
(Jeong Keun Woo has submitted his cards.)

3732
02:41:20,140 --> 02:41:21,410
Goodness.

3733
02:41:21,910 --> 02:41:24,510
That was quick.

3734
02:41:24,510 --> 02:41:31,150
(The Round 1 point card: Minus 5)

3735
02:41:31,150 --> 02:41:32,150
Why?

3736
02:41:33,120 --> 02:41:34,520
Hong Jin Ho, are you scared?

3737
02:41:35,020 --> 02:41:36,890
I don't know.

3738
02:41:36,890 --> 02:41:38,330
I can't guess at all.

3739
02:41:39,260 --> 02:41:41,560
First, please reveal your special cards.

3740
02:41:48,640 --> 02:41:50,670
Because everyone submitted normal cards,

3741
02:41:50,670 --> 02:41:52,910
the reverse effect does not apply.

3742
02:41:53,140 --> 02:41:55,680
Please reveal the backs
of your number cards.

3743
02:42:01,020 --> 02:42:03,950
(Everyone has submitted low number cards.)

3744
02:42:04,590 --> 02:42:06,890
Nice, let's go!

3745
02:42:06,890 --> 02:42:09,190
- We'll overlap.
- I'm screwed. We'll definitely overlap.

3746
02:42:09,190 --> 02:42:10,730
We'll definitely overlap.

3747
02:42:10,960 --> 02:42:13,160
The range I can use on that...

3748
02:42:13,160 --> 02:42:16,000
is between 3 and 6.

3749
02:42:16,200 --> 02:42:18,830
If I were Xitsuh or Tae Gyun...

3750
02:42:19,330 --> 02:42:21,500
They would use...

3751
02:42:21,500 --> 02:42:25,210
either 4 or 5.

3752
02:42:25,210 --> 02:42:28,140
Xitsuh,
please flip over your number cards.

3753
02:42:28,540 --> 02:42:29,880
I think you all would've
submitted this number card.

3754
02:42:30,610 --> 02:42:31,610
Welcome.

3755
02:42:32,510 --> 02:42:33,520
Welcome.

3756
02:42:33,850 --> 02:42:34,980
It's this number, right?

3757
02:42:35,680 --> 02:42:38,590
Lee Tae Gyun,
please flip over your number cards.

3758
02:42:38,590 --> 02:42:41,260
(Xitsuh, 4)

3759
02:42:41,260 --> 02:42:44,230
Lee Tae Gyun submitted card number five.

3760
02:42:44,590 --> 02:42:46,660
(The Round 1 point card: Minus 5)

3761
02:42:49,430 --> 02:42:51,170
I think they'll submit 4 or 5.

3762
02:42:51,170 --> 02:42:53,140
I can't predict Keun Woo at all.

3763
02:42:53,140 --> 02:42:55,940
I'll keep an eye on him for Round One.

3764
02:42:55,940 --> 02:42:58,210
Since they'll submit 4 or 5,

3765
02:42:58,210 --> 02:43:00,240
I submitted a three to avoid them.

3766
02:43:05,310 --> 02:43:07,080
(Hong Jin Ho submitted card number 3.)

3767
02:43:07,520 --> 02:43:08,520
Xitsuh is the first to go.

3768
02:43:08,520 --> 02:43:10,350
It's four. I got it right.

3769
02:43:10,750 --> 02:43:12,650
Tae Gyun flipped over his card,
and it's five.

3770
02:43:12,890 --> 02:43:13,890
I got it right.

3771
02:43:14,120 --> 02:43:16,320
Just as I predicted.

3772
02:43:16,320 --> 02:43:20,030
All there's left is for Keun Woo
to submit 4 or 5.

3773
02:43:20,030 --> 02:43:22,860
Jeong Keun Woo,
please flip over your number cards.

3774
02:43:23,470 --> 02:43:26,670
(Xitsuh: 4, Lee Tae Gyun: 5,
Hong Jin Ho: 3)

3775
02:43:26,670 --> 02:43:29,540
Jeong Keun Woo submitted
card number three.

3776
02:43:29,540 --> 02:43:31,570
(Xitsuh: 4, Lee Tae Gyun: 5,
Hong Jin Ho: 3, Jeong Keun Woo: 3)

3777
02:43:31,570 --> 02:43:32,570
Darn it.

3778
02:43:32,640 --> 02:43:34,380
He submitted the same card as me.

3779
02:43:34,380 --> 02:43:35,740
I screwed up from the first round.

3780
02:43:35,740 --> 02:43:38,350
Hong Jin Ho,
please flip over your number cards.

3781
02:43:38,350 --> 02:43:40,820
(The Round 1 point card: Minus 5)

3782
02:43:40,820 --> 02:43:42,080
- No.
- No.

3783
02:43:42,080 --> 02:43:44,950
Hong Jin Ho submitted card number three.

3784
02:43:44,950 --> 02:43:47,590
(The Round 1 point card: Minus 5)

3785
02:43:47,590 --> 02:43:50,590
I thought Jin Ho wouldn't push himself
on Round One,

3786
02:43:50,590 --> 02:43:51,590
and as I thought,

3787
02:43:51,590 --> 02:43:54,430
he tested the waters
by submitting card number three.

3788
02:43:54,930 --> 02:43:57,130
The same number cards have been submitted.

3789
02:43:57,730 --> 02:44:00,100
(The Round 1 point card: Minus 5)

3790
02:44:00,100 --> 02:44:03,340
For the minus card,
the winner can hand the card over...

3791
02:44:03,340 --> 02:44:05,710
to one of the players
who have submitted the same cards.

3792
02:44:05,710 --> 02:44:06,710
They can attack, basically.

3793
02:44:06,710 --> 02:44:09,480
(Tae Gyun has the right to attack.)

3794
02:44:09,580 --> 02:44:13,220
Out of the low blue cards,
I thought the card numbers of 3 or 4...

3795
02:44:13,220 --> 02:44:15,550
were the safe median.

3796
02:44:15,550 --> 02:44:19,150
I should keep them to prepare myself...

3797
02:44:19,150 --> 02:44:20,460
for card numbers minus 7 and minus 9
just in case.

3798
02:44:20,720 --> 02:44:22,890
I'll submit card number five...

3799
02:44:22,890 --> 02:44:24,190
and avoid this card.

3800
02:44:24,830 --> 02:44:27,900
Lee Tae Gyun, to which player
will you give the number card?

3801
02:44:27,900 --> 02:44:29,030
Right from the start?

3802
02:44:29,430 --> 02:44:30,670
Is there anything
you can strike a deal with?

3803
02:44:31,900 --> 02:44:34,100
If you don't pass me
minus five point card,

3804
02:44:34,740 --> 02:44:36,470
and if we survive together,

3805
02:44:37,310 --> 02:44:39,340
I'll give you 50,000 dollars
of my personal funds.

3806
02:44:39,340 --> 02:44:40,540
Okay.

3807
02:44:40,940 --> 02:44:42,510
- Then...
- Did you say 50,000 dollars?

3808
02:44:42,980 --> 02:44:43,980
Raise.

3809
02:44:44,950 --> 02:44:46,150
- You have more money?
- Yes.

3810
02:44:46,150 --> 02:44:47,350
- You have more money?
- Raise.

3811
02:44:47,350 --> 02:44:48,720
- You have more money?
- I'll raise the amount.

3812
02:44:48,720 --> 02:44:50,020
- I'll raise.
- You have more money?

3813
02:44:50,020 --> 02:44:52,590
Not Hong Jin Ho. I'll raise.

3814
02:44:52,590 --> 02:44:54,920
I'll use up all my money.

3815
02:44:56,630 --> 02:44:58,590
I'll give you every cent I own.

3816
02:44:58,590 --> 02:44:59,590
I have decided.

3817
02:45:01,130 --> 02:45:03,130
- I'll give it to Hong Jin Ho.
- As I thought, money is the best.

3818
02:45:03,130 --> 02:45:04,500
I'll accept the card gladly.

3819
02:45:04,500 --> 02:45:07,870
The minus five point card goes
to Hong Jin Ho.

3820
02:45:12,040 --> 02:45:16,010
(Hong Jin Ho gets the minus 5 point card.)

3821
02:45:16,180 --> 02:45:17,880
In the first place,

3822
02:45:19,250 --> 02:45:20,680
Tae Gyun was set on giving it to me.

3823
02:45:21,180 --> 02:45:25,550
Money isn't that important
in that stage of the show,

3824
02:45:25,920 --> 02:45:27,120
and there's no way he doesn't know that.

3825
02:45:27,120 --> 02:45:28,690
He just wanted...

3826
02:45:30,090 --> 02:45:32,090
to tease me and feel me out.

3827
02:45:32,590 --> 02:45:34,160
This cocky brat.

3828
02:45:34,500 --> 02:45:36,230
He was going to give it to me anyway.

3829
02:45:37,270 --> 02:45:40,840
Sadly, he gave the card to me,

3830
02:45:40,840 --> 02:45:43,740
and I started Round Two
with a big penalty...

3831
02:45:43,740 --> 02:45:45,370
in the form of minus five point card.

3832
02:45:45,670 --> 02:45:47,510
We will begin Round Two.

3833
02:45:48,180 --> 02:45:50,750
(Round 2, Xitsuh: 0, Lee Tae Gyun: 0,
Jeong Keun Woo: 0, Hong Jin Ho: minus 5)

3834
02:45:50,750 --> 02:45:52,580
- The point card of this round...
- Another minus card.

3835
02:45:52,580 --> 02:45:54,120
is minus seven.

3836
02:45:55,080 --> 02:45:58,120
It feels very burdensome
since I already have one.

3837
02:45:58,120 --> 02:46:01,260
(The Round 2 point card: Minus 7)

3838
02:46:01,260 --> 02:46:02,520
Would Jin Ho...

3839
02:46:03,430 --> 02:46:04,790
use the reverse card?

3840
02:46:04,790 --> 02:46:07,760
If he gets minus seven point card as well,
he will pretty much lose the game.

3841
02:46:07,760 --> 02:46:12,330
(The Round 2 point card: Minus 7)

3842
02:46:12,330 --> 02:46:17,010
(The Round 2 point card: Minus 7)

3843
02:46:17,010 --> 02:46:18,440
What will these guys submit?

3844
02:46:18,770 --> 02:46:20,210
Should I use the reverse card or not?

3845
02:46:20,210 --> 02:46:21,640
Will they use it?

3846
02:46:21,640 --> 02:46:27,350
(The Round 2 point card: Minus 7)

3847
02:46:27,350 --> 02:46:32,920
(The Round 2 point card: Minus 7)

3848
02:46:33,720 --> 02:46:35,320
Has everyone submitted their cards?

3849
02:46:36,060 --> 02:46:38,260
First, please reveal your special cards.

3850
02:46:38,260 --> 02:46:41,000
(They reveal the special cards.)

3851
02:46:41,000 --> 02:46:43,430
(Jeong Keun Woo, normal card)

3852
02:46:43,430 --> 02:46:46,030
(Lee Tae Gyun, normal card)

3853
02:46:46,170 --> 02:46:49,140
(Xitsuh, normal card)

3854
02:46:49,140 --> 02:46:53,740
(The Round 2 point card: Minus 7)

3855
02:46:53,740 --> 02:46:55,580
(Hong Jin Ho, normal card)

3856
02:46:55,580 --> 02:46:58,280
- Normal card again.
- Because everyone submitted normal cards,

3857
02:46:58,280 --> 02:47:00,250
the reverse effect does not apply.

3858
02:47:00,420 --> 02:47:04,250
Everyone submitted normal cards
for their special cards.

3859
02:47:04,520 --> 02:47:06,450
Jin Ho didn't use the reverse card.

3860
02:47:07,120 --> 02:47:08,320
The plan got thrown off once.

3861
02:47:09,420 --> 02:47:11,590
Please reveal the backs
of your number cards.

3862
02:47:11,590 --> 02:47:13,660
(The Round 2 point card: Minus 7)

3863
02:47:13,660 --> 02:47:15,700
(Hong Jin Ho's card)

3864
02:47:15,700 --> 02:47:18,130
(Jeong Keun Woo's card)

3865
02:47:18,130 --> 02:47:20,500
(Lee Tae Gyun's card)

3866
02:47:20,500 --> 02:47:24,670
(The Round 2 point card: Minus 7)

3867
02:47:24,670 --> 02:47:28,840
(The Round 2 point card: Minus 7)

3868
02:47:28,840 --> 02:47:30,280
- We thought of the same thing.
- You're good.

3869
02:47:30,280 --> 02:47:31,710
- You're good.
- You're good.

3870
02:47:32,880 --> 02:47:34,720
Keun Woo, you always play
similar cards as mine.

3871
02:47:36,080 --> 02:47:37,120
Exactly.

3872
02:47:37,320 --> 02:47:40,050
Jin Ho and Keun Woo played the blue card,

3873
02:47:40,660 --> 02:47:42,720
and Tae Gyun and I played the yellow card.

3874
02:47:43,730 --> 02:47:45,590
If it wasn't Tae Gyun,
then I'd take the points.

3875
02:47:46,190 --> 02:47:47,700
But something felt off.

3876
02:47:48,160 --> 02:47:51,000
Hong Jin Ho,
please flip over your number card.

3877
02:47:51,000 --> 02:47:52,000
Okay.

3878
02:47:53,970 --> 02:47:56,940
Hong Jin Ho submitted card number four.

3879
02:47:57,210 --> 02:47:58,240
You want to know, don't you?

3880
02:47:59,270 --> 02:48:00,310
Precisely.

3881
02:48:00,510 --> 02:48:03,210
Xitsuh submitted card number six.

3882
02:48:03,340 --> 02:48:05,910
Lee Tae Gyun,
please flip over your number card.

3883
02:48:06,850 --> 02:48:07,880
(Lee Tae Gyun submits card number 6.)

3884
02:48:08,820 --> 02:48:10,850
Gosh, they both...

3885
02:48:11,520 --> 02:48:13,120
equally twisted the game.

3886
02:48:13,250 --> 02:48:14,760
To the point where we reach
the same outcome.

3887
02:48:15,160 --> 02:48:16,320
Please clash!

3888
02:48:16,690 --> 02:48:18,760
No! That shouldn't happen!
Please don't do that.

3889
02:48:18,990 --> 02:48:20,900
Keun Woo, please don't do that.
This isn't right.

3890
02:48:20,900 --> 02:48:22,830
No, right? That's not it, right, Keun Woo?

3891
02:48:23,430 --> 02:48:24,430
No, right?

3892
02:48:27,540 --> 02:48:30,270
Jeong Keun Woo submitted card number five.

3893
02:48:31,710 --> 02:48:33,610
(Jeong Keun Woo has the right to attack
with minus 7 point card.)

3894
02:48:33,940 --> 02:48:38,080
Seven is iffy,
but it's a big point to win.

3895
02:48:38,210 --> 02:48:40,420
But human psychology is funny.

3896
02:48:40,420 --> 02:48:43,350
When you want to give minus 9,
you'd want to use 5.

3897
02:48:43,520 --> 02:48:45,620
Using 5 when you want to give minus 7...

3898
02:48:45,620 --> 02:48:47,190
is just about reading each other's moves.

3899
02:48:47,320 --> 02:48:50,790
I proactively bet on minus seven more.

3900
02:48:52,190 --> 02:48:53,390
Did he play poker when he was young?

3901
02:48:55,000 --> 02:48:58,300
Jeong Keun Woo, to which player
will you give the number card?

3902
02:49:00,070 --> 02:49:01,500
- You want it?
- Give it to me, Keun Woo.

3903
02:49:02,040 --> 02:49:03,040
I'll give it to him.

3904
02:49:07,110 --> 02:49:09,680
The point card goes to Xitsuh.

3905
02:49:10,910 --> 02:49:13,720
(Xitsuh gets the minus 7-point card.)

3906
02:49:13,920 --> 02:49:16,350
Keun Woo had no choice
but to give it to me.

3907
02:49:16,580 --> 02:49:17,850
That's only rationale, after all.

3908
02:49:18,020 --> 02:49:20,560
After Jin Ho and Xitsuh got minus points,

3909
02:49:20,560 --> 02:49:22,860
I realized I had a higher chance
to survive.

3910
02:49:24,390 --> 02:49:26,330
We will begin Round Three.

3911
02:49:29,100 --> 02:49:31,730
The point card of this round is ten.

3912
02:49:32,170 --> 02:49:33,430
This is my chance!

3913
02:49:34,900 --> 02:49:36,400
It's the highest card
among the plus number cards.

3914
02:49:36,400 --> 02:49:37,970
I had to take that card,

3915
02:49:37,970 --> 02:49:39,340
even if I had to use the reverse card.

3916
02:49:40,840 --> 02:49:43,610
I'm the one who is most desperate
for the ten point card.

3917
02:49:43,980 --> 02:49:45,510
I bet everyone else felt the same way,

3918
02:49:45,510 --> 02:49:48,920
but since it was the best card,
I thought I should bet my life on it.

3919
02:49:49,320 --> 02:49:52,590
All players, please submit
your number card and special card.

3920
02:49:52,590 --> 02:49:57,030
(The Round 3 point card: 10)

3921
02:49:57,030 --> 02:50:01,500
(The Round 3 point card: 10)

3922
02:50:01,500 --> 02:50:02,930
I started planning.

3923
02:50:04,000 --> 02:50:07,700
The first idea I thought of
was submitting the card number ten.

3924
02:50:07,970 --> 02:50:09,540
Then submitting the reverse card
and card number one.

3925
02:50:09,900 --> 02:50:12,070
Okay, anyone can think this far.

3926
02:50:12,410 --> 02:50:14,010
I thought,
"Should I give it a twist here?"

3927
02:50:14,840 --> 02:50:17,350
Someone might think
I'd use the reverse card...

3928
02:50:17,780 --> 02:50:19,550
and he might counter that card...

3929
02:50:20,080 --> 02:50:23,720
and submit a card with a high number.
Someone could have that strategy.

3930
02:50:24,790 --> 02:50:25,820
I thought the other way and came up...

3931
02:50:26,750 --> 02:50:29,390
with a strategy to submit one point
card without submitting the reverse card.

3932
02:50:30,060 --> 02:50:32,460
So I thought of submitting one point
card without submitting the reverse card.

3933
02:50:33,530 --> 02:50:34,560
"No."

3934
02:50:36,830 --> 02:50:38,900
"How about submitting the reverse card
and card number ten?"

3935
02:50:41,670 --> 02:50:42,870
If one of them...

3936
02:50:44,840 --> 02:50:48,310
submits the card number ten
after I used the reverse card,

3937
02:50:50,410 --> 02:50:51,510
then it'll just clash.

3938
02:50:52,380 --> 02:50:54,020
I'd lose both the reverse card
and the card number ten.

3939
02:50:56,350 --> 02:51:00,150
But I thought someone would predict that
and submit the card number nine.

3940
02:51:00,860 --> 02:51:02,220
Then I gave it another twist.

3941
02:51:02,220 --> 02:51:03,520
Why? Because Tae Gyun was there.

3942
02:51:05,090 --> 02:51:07,900
"How about submitting
the card number ten head-on?"

3943
02:51:07,900 --> 02:51:10,300
They say
the best upgrade is no upgrade at all.

3944
02:51:11,570 --> 02:51:13,800
After all the twists,

3945
02:51:14,770 --> 02:51:17,410
I thought I should submit
the highest card head-on...

3946
02:51:17,410 --> 02:51:18,410
without the reverse card.

3947
02:51:18,940 --> 02:51:20,940
That's the conclusion I reached.

3948
02:51:20,940 --> 02:51:23,440
(Xitsuh, 10, normal)

3949
02:51:23,440 --> 02:51:27,650
(The Round 3 point card: 10)

3950
02:51:27,650 --> 02:51:30,420
Will someone take the chance or not?

3951
02:51:37,190 --> 02:51:39,130
No one has used the reverse card yet.

3952
02:51:39,190 --> 02:51:40,860
That's when I considered it.

3953
02:51:41,300 --> 02:51:44,330
"Will Xitsuh use it?
Will Tae Gyun use it?"

3954
02:51:45,130 --> 02:51:46,700
I thought Keun Woo would never use it.

3955
02:51:47,000 --> 02:51:48,800
I could figure him out
after a round or two.

3956
02:51:48,970 --> 02:51:50,470
I knew Keun Woo would never use it.

3957
02:51:51,410 --> 02:51:52,540
"Let's not challenge them."

3958
02:51:53,040 --> 02:51:56,240
I could go up to second place,
but if it overlapped again,

3959
02:51:56,440 --> 02:52:00,150
I thought I could give a chance
to the opponents.

3960
02:52:00,250 --> 02:52:02,520
I thought of giving up the ten point card.

3961
02:52:03,120 --> 02:52:05,520
I had to take the points no matter what
even if I had to use the reverse card.

3962
02:52:05,520 --> 02:52:09,160
(The Round 3 point card: 10)

3963
02:52:09,160 --> 02:52:11,430
Then I reached to a conclusion...

3964
02:52:11,690 --> 02:52:12,960
that two of them
wouldn't use it at the same time.

3965
02:52:13,490 --> 02:52:16,430
I thought just one of them could use it.

3966
02:52:16,960 --> 02:52:18,130
I thought I shouldn't use it.

3967
02:52:18,130 --> 02:52:20,270
The moment I use it, there's a high chance
the cards will be even.

3968
02:52:20,330 --> 02:52:21,470
I thought it'd get twisted.

3969
02:52:21,470 --> 02:52:27,210
(The Round 3 point card: 10)

3970
02:52:27,210 --> 02:52:29,540
(Hong Jin Ho, normal)

3971
02:52:32,510 --> 02:52:34,020
Has everyone submitted their cards?

3972
02:52:34,350 --> 02:52:35,380
Yes.

3973
02:52:36,920 --> 02:52:39,150
First, please reveal your special cards.

3974
02:52:39,150 --> 02:52:45,660
(The Round 3 point card: 10)

3975
02:52:45,660 --> 02:52:47,800
Gosh, they got me.

3976
02:52:48,360 --> 02:52:49,460
I should've submitted it.

3977
02:52:49,700 --> 02:52:50,700
(Xitsuh, normal card)

3978
02:52:50,700 --> 02:52:51,700
(Jeong Keun Woo, normal card)

3979
02:52:51,700 --> 02:52:52,700
(Hong Jin Ho, normal card)

3980
02:52:56,340 --> 02:52:58,210
(Lee Tae Gyun, reverse card)

3981
02:53:01,140 --> 02:53:02,740
Xitsuh submitted the normal card.

3982
02:53:03,010 --> 02:53:05,210
I submitted the normal card,
and Keun Woo submitted the normal card.

3983
02:53:05,310 --> 02:53:07,480
But Tae Gyun submitted the reverse card.

3984
02:53:07,880 --> 02:53:08,950
It's a good start, at least.

3985
02:53:08,950 --> 02:53:10,990
As the reverse card was submitted,

3986
02:53:10,990 --> 02:53:13,760
the card advantage in this round
will be reversed.

3987
02:53:14,020 --> 02:53:15,460
Did you think I'd submit the reverse card?

3988
02:53:16,720 --> 02:53:19,060
Please reveal the backs
of your number cards.

3989
02:53:22,530 --> 02:53:24,400
(Hong Jin Ho, low number card)

3990
02:53:25,800 --> 02:53:27,030
(Jeong Keun Woo, high number card)

3991
02:53:28,900 --> 02:53:30,040
My gosh!

3992
02:53:32,170 --> 02:53:33,270
My gosh!

3993
02:53:33,780 --> 02:53:34,780
(Grunting)

3994
02:53:34,780 --> 02:53:38,180
(Laughing)

3995
02:53:38,450 --> 02:53:39,710
We revealed the cards,

3996
02:53:41,480 --> 02:53:42,550
and all three of them submitted
yellow cards.

3997
02:53:42,550 --> 02:53:44,550
After I saw that,
I knew my prediction was right.

3998
02:53:45,020 --> 02:53:48,260
I knew I'd get the points
even if the numbers weren't revealed...

3999
02:53:48,260 --> 02:53:49,290
because they all submitted yellow cards.

4000
02:53:49,420 --> 02:53:50,420
I was really glad.

4001
02:53:51,330 --> 02:53:52,590
My gosh!

4002
02:53:53,630 --> 02:53:55,430
That's why I gave it another twist!

4003
02:53:55,430 --> 02:53:57,430
I gave it another twist, Tae Gyun!

4004
02:53:57,430 --> 02:54:00,030
I knew you'd use the reverse card,
so I wondered if I should use it or not.

4005
02:54:00,030 --> 02:54:02,200
I didn't because I thought
one more person could use it.

4006
02:54:02,200 --> 02:54:03,700
I contemplated until the last minute.

4007
02:54:04,570 --> 02:54:07,540
- You should've used it!
- I twisted it one more time!

4008
02:54:07,540 --> 02:54:10,240
Tae Gyun, I thought you'd expect
a reverse card to be played!

4009
02:54:10,240 --> 02:54:11,880
He twisted it one more time!

4010
02:54:11,880 --> 02:54:14,880
I thought you wouldn't use it
after twisting it one more time!

4011
02:54:16,180 --> 02:54:17,950
When I considered every possibility,

4012
02:54:18,220 --> 02:54:20,190
