and miraculously give
the minus card number nine to Keun Woo,

4254
03:06:29,080 --> 03:06:32,820
then give the minus card number three
to Tae Gyun.

4255
03:06:33,720 --> 03:06:36,720
That was the only condition of my winning.

4256
03:06:37,190 --> 03:06:39,690
That was the only way
for me to win second place.

4257
03:06:40,390 --> 03:06:41,960
All of those had to fall into place.

4258
03:06:41,960 --> 03:06:43,030
But...

4259
03:06:44,330 --> 03:06:47,170
I managed to steal three times in a row
by pickpocketing.

4260
03:06:48,400 --> 03:06:51,270
You can't rule out that
those three coincidences won't happen.

4261
03:06:52,010 --> 03:06:53,970
Just as I stole the wallets,

4262
03:06:54,370 --> 03:06:56,840
I can just let those cards be played.

4263
03:06:56,840 --> 03:06:59,550
I have the reverse card
and the card number one,

4264
03:06:59,750 --> 03:07:03,020
and I have the card number 8 and 9,
which aren't so bad.

4265
03:07:03,380 --> 03:07:06,050
The point card of this round is two.

4266
03:07:06,520 --> 03:07:08,260
Jin Ho, take that.

4267
03:07:08,390 --> 03:07:09,520
Just give it to me.

4268
03:07:10,790 --> 03:07:14,060
All players, please submit
your number card and special card.

4269
03:07:17,060 --> 03:07:19,600
I wasn't in a good place.

4270
03:07:20,630 --> 03:07:22,600
I'll be eliminated.

4271
03:07:22,970 --> 03:07:26,270
Xitsuh was guaranteed to be in last place.

4272
03:07:27,370 --> 03:07:29,440
Nevertheless, I should do my best.

4273
03:07:31,910 --> 03:07:33,710
Out of the ten point cards,

4274
03:07:33,710 --> 03:07:36,850
getting rid of minus 1 or 2...

4275
03:07:36,850 --> 03:07:38,590
would be ideal for me.

4276
03:07:38,590 --> 03:07:40,250
But minus one is already out.

4277
03:07:40,690 --> 03:07:43,190
That means getting rid of the two
would be the best-case scenario.

4278
03:07:43,190 --> 03:07:44,460
But this round's point card
just happens to be two.

4279
03:07:45,530 --> 03:07:48,330
I'm in a really tough spot right now.

4280
03:08:01,980 --> 03:08:03,540
There's only one reverse card left.

4281
03:08:04,440 --> 03:08:06,950
(Xitsuh is the only person
who hasn't used...)

4282
03:08:06,950 --> 03:08:09,680
(his reverse card.)

4283
03:08:09,880 --> 03:08:11,180
Will he use it on the two-point card?

4284
03:08:12,050 --> 03:08:13,120
No way, absolutely not.

4285
03:08:13,120 --> 03:08:15,290
(All cards have been submitted.)

4286
03:08:15,290 --> 03:08:17,160
First, please reveal your special cards.

4287
03:08:18,830 --> 03:08:20,390
Reverse? Not happening.

4288
03:08:20,990 --> 03:08:22,130
Normal.

4289
03:08:24,100 --> 03:08:27,670
Because everyone submitted normal cards,
the reverse effect does not apply.

4290
03:08:29,700 --> 03:08:31,840
Please reveal
the backs of your number cards.

4291
03:08:32,040 --> 03:08:33,410
(Jeong Keun Woo's card)

4292
03:08:33,410 --> 03:08:35,140
(Lee Tae Gyun's card)

4293
03:08:38,780 --> 03:08:40,580
(Hong Jin Ho's card)

4294
03:08:44,250 --> 03:08:46,590
When I saw the backs of the cards,
I was shocked.

4295
03:08:47,650 --> 03:08:49,590
Jin Ho's was yellow,
and mine was yellow too.

4296
03:08:50,420 --> 03:08:52,560
Tae Gyun and Keun Woo's cards were blue.

4297
03:08:53,330 --> 03:08:55,800
What's this?
What kind of move are they making?

4298
03:08:55,960 --> 03:08:58,130
Did they think I would submit
the reverse card?

4299
03:08:59,230 --> 03:09:01,770
Or were they just taking a gamble?

4300
03:09:03,140 --> 03:09:06,610
If so, there's a good chance
Jin Ho submitted a nine.

4301
03:09:06,970 --> 03:09:10,040
Even if it's not a 9...
Would he really use his 7 here?

4302
03:09:10,240 --> 03:09:11,850
There's no point in saving it.

4303
03:09:13,180 --> 03:09:14,250
Gosh.

4304
03:09:15,350 --> 03:09:16,880
You're so greedy.

4305
03:09:17,780 --> 03:09:19,950
- Go ahead and take it, then.
- Starting with Hong Jin Ho,

4306
03:09:19,950 --> 03:09:21,320
please flip over your number cards.

4307
03:09:22,790 --> 03:09:23,890
He must be feeling pretty full.

4308
03:09:28,100 --> 03:09:29,330
Come on. Flip it already.

4309
03:09:29,560 --> 03:09:32,230
Hong Jin Ho submitted
the card number eight.

4310
03:09:32,630 --> 03:09:34,500
You're keeping things interesting
until the very end.

4311
03:09:34,800 --> 03:09:36,200
Fancy meeting you here.

4312
03:09:36,200 --> 03:09:38,810
- Xitsuh submitted the card number eight.
- I guess this is why I was conflicted.

4313
03:09:39,770 --> 03:09:40,840
He submitted an eight.

4314
03:09:41,210 --> 03:09:42,510
We matched again.

4315
03:09:44,140 --> 03:09:45,150
Another eight.

4316
03:09:45,680 --> 03:09:48,180
Lee Tae Gyun submitted
the card number three.

4317
03:09:48,450 --> 03:09:50,780
Jeong Keun Woo submitted
the card number four.

4318
03:09:51,950 --> 03:09:54,720
Forget the new generation.
The old generation gets everything.

4319
03:09:54,720 --> 03:09:56,160
- We still have a long way to go.
- The two-point card...

4320
03:09:56,160 --> 03:09:57,720
goes to Jeong Keun Woo.

4321
03:09:57,720 --> 03:10:02,730
(Jeong Keun Woo gets the 2-point card.)

4322
03:10:02,860 --> 03:10:05,470
I already had seven points...

4323
03:10:06,070 --> 03:10:08,000
and wanted to play it safe.

4324
03:10:08,200 --> 03:10:11,000
But then Hong Jin Ho submitted
the card number eight on one side,

4325
03:10:11,270 --> 03:10:13,110
and Xitsuh submitted an eight
on the other, causing a clash.

4326
03:10:13,540 --> 03:10:16,310
As a result, the two points
ended up coming to me.

4327
03:10:16,780 --> 03:10:18,810
That tied me with Hong Jin Ho...

4328
03:10:19,650 --> 03:10:21,080
at 9 to 9,

4329
03:10:22,480 --> 03:10:23,550
so I figured I was safe.

4330
03:10:24,080 --> 03:10:25,890
We will begin Round 8.

4331
03:10:26,650 --> 03:10:29,890
The point card of this round
is minus nine.

4332
03:10:29,890 --> 03:10:31,120
(The Round 8 point card: Minus 9)

4333
03:10:31,290 --> 03:10:32,590
Gosh, there it is.

4334
03:10:34,560 --> 03:10:35,560
Gosh.

4335
03:10:38,130 --> 03:10:39,530
How did we even end up here?

4336
03:10:42,840 --> 03:10:43,870
I'm getting a headache.

4337
03:10:44,740 --> 03:10:46,470
Why am I even thinking this over?

4338
03:10:48,810 --> 03:10:50,910
Xitsuh had zero chance of winning.

4339
03:10:51,340 --> 03:10:54,380
His Deathmatch defeat was inevitable.

4340
03:10:55,280 --> 03:10:57,620
But the point card was minus nine.

4341
03:10:57,920 --> 03:11:01,990
And Hong Jin Ho and I were
both at nine points.

4342
03:11:01,990 --> 03:11:05,690
So it was either going to be
Lee Tae Gyun and I tied at zero points,

4343
03:11:05,890 --> 03:11:07,890
or Hong Jin Ho and Lee Tae Gyun
tied at zero points.

4344
03:11:09,530 --> 03:11:12,400
That's why Xitsuh was conflicted
in that situation.

4345
03:11:12,400 --> 03:11:16,300
(Xitsuh: -7, Lee Tae Gyun: 0,
Jeong Keun Woo: 9, Hong Jin Ho: 9)

4346
03:11:16,540 --> 03:11:17,640
Let me think about this.

4347
03:11:51,910 --> 03:11:53,470
Gosh, I don't know.

4348
03:11:55,110 --> 03:11:56,540
Now that the minus nine was out,

4349
03:11:57,080 --> 03:12:01,550
the remaining point card was either
minus 3 or plus 6.

4350
03:12:02,180 --> 03:12:03,420
There were so many possibilities.

4351
03:12:04,480 --> 03:12:06,520
There were just so many possibilities.

4352
03:12:07,090 --> 03:12:11,090
I knew I'd already lost this game.

4353
03:12:11,320 --> 03:12:13,360
So then, what could I still protect?

4354
03:12:15,330 --> 03:12:16,660
That thought crossed my mind,

4355
03:12:17,930 --> 03:12:20,530
and I decided to eliminate
the only remaining variable.

4356
03:12:25,840 --> 03:12:28,840
So the one thing I could decide
for certain was...

4357
03:12:33,780 --> 03:12:35,520
We will begin Round 9.

4358
03:12:36,050 --> 03:12:37,850
The point card of this round...

4359
03:12:40,790 --> 03:12:42,420
is minus three.

4360
03:12:42,420 --> 03:12:43,720
(The Round 9 point card: Minus 3)

4361
03:12:45,490 --> 03:12:47,660
The Deathmatch has ended.

4362
03:12:48,330 --> 03:12:50,800
Please gather in the main hall.

4363
03:12:51,830 --> 03:12:54,170
The Deathmatch results
will now be announced.

4364
03:12:55,100 --> 03:12:57,840
The players eliminated from
Bloody Game X are...

4365
03:13:01,340 --> 03:13:03,480
Lee Tae Gyun...

4366
03:13:04,740 --> 03:13:05,810
What?

4367
03:13:09,850 --> 03:13:10,920
and...

4368
03:13:12,120 --> 03:13:15,390
Xitsuh.

4369
03:13:21,660 --> 03:13:23,400
We will begin Round Eight.

4370
03:13:24,760 --> 03:13:27,930
The point card of this round
is minus nine.

4371
03:13:27,930 --> 03:13:29,140
(Xitsuh thought it over for a long time.)

4372
03:13:30,700 --> 03:13:33,510
I decided to eliminate
the only remaining variable.

4373
03:13:33,510 --> 03:13:34,670
It was for Jin Ho.

4374
03:13:37,840 --> 03:13:41,680
If Jin Ho got the minus 9, and then...

4375
03:13:41,920 --> 03:13:43,850
also ended up with the minus 3,

4376
03:13:44,650 --> 03:13:45,790
he'd be eliminated along with me.

4377
03:13:46,320 --> 03:13:48,590
Or, if he got the minus nine this round...

4378
03:13:48,790 --> 03:13:51,020
and Tae Gyun got the plus six,

4379
03:13:51,520 --> 03:13:53,360
he'd still be eliminated with me.

4380
03:13:53,360 --> 03:13:55,300
That was the only variable.

4381
03:13:55,560 --> 03:13:57,760
If Jin Ho got the minus nine,

4382
03:14:00,230 --> 03:14:01,840
he'd be at risk of elimination.

4383
03:14:10,240 --> 03:14:13,710
By doing this, I was guaranteeing
Tae Gyun's elimination.

4384
03:14:15,280 --> 03:14:17,420
Even so,

4385
03:14:17,420 --> 03:14:20,890
he was the one who put me in
today's Deathmatch,

4386
03:14:21,620 --> 03:14:23,460
while Jin Ho...

4387
03:14:23,860 --> 03:14:26,130
was a member of Team P3 and my ally.

4388
03:14:30,300 --> 03:14:34,570
That's why I decided to use
the reverse card and the card number one.

4389
03:14:35,570 --> 03:14:36,870
I decided to take the hit myself.

4390
03:14:38,300 --> 03:14:40,040
(Xitsuh submits
the reverse card number 1.)

4391
03:14:40,040 --> 03:14:42,410
Xitsuh submitted the card number one.

4392
03:14:43,010 --> 03:14:45,310
If I take the minus nine,
Jin Ho can't end up with it.

4393
03:14:45,550 --> 03:14:47,510
I was the only one who still had
a reverse card left, anyway.

4394
03:14:49,620 --> 03:14:50,780
That's why I submitted
the reverse card number one.

4395
03:14:51,420 --> 03:14:55,120
Xitsuh gets the minus nine-point card.

4396
03:14:58,160 --> 03:14:59,830
I think Xitsuh's thought process was this.

4397
03:14:59,830 --> 03:15:03,460
By taking the minus nine himself,

4398
03:15:04,130 --> 03:15:07,670
he'd eliminate the possibility of
Hong Jin Ho ending up with it.

4399
03:15:08,000 --> 03:15:10,470
He wanted to keep Team P3 in the game.

4400
03:15:10,770 --> 03:15:12,470
We will begin Round Nine.

4401
03:15:12,470 --> 03:15:15,880
The point card of this round
is minus three.

4402
03:15:16,940 --> 03:15:19,410
Xitsuh submitted the card number nine.

4403
03:15:19,650 --> 03:15:22,050
Lee Tae Gyun submitted
the card number one.

4404
03:15:22,480 --> 03:15:25,290
Jeong Keun Woo submitted
the card number nine.

4405
03:15:25,590 --> 03:15:27,690
Hong Jin Ho submitted
the card number five.

4406
03:15:28,790 --> 03:15:29,890
I'll give it to Keun Woo.

4407
03:15:30,720 --> 03:15:34,490
The minus three-point card goes to
Jeong Keun Woo.

4408
03:15:40,600 --> 03:15:42,340
Round Nine has ended.

4409
03:15:45,210 --> 03:15:48,640
Xitsuh and Lee Tae Gyun.
Please pack your bags immediately...

4410
03:15:48,810 --> 03:15:51,480
- and leave the Bloody Mansion.
- What do I do now?

4411
03:15:51,480 --> 03:15:53,750
Eliminated players can never return...

4412
03:15:53,950 --> 03:15:55,650
to Bloody Game X.

4413
03:15:56,350 --> 03:15:58,250
I think I have...

4414
03:15:59,090 --> 03:16:01,620
a little more regret this season...

4415
03:16:02,390 --> 03:16:04,760
than I did in the others.

4416
03:16:04,890 --> 03:16:07,190
I'd gained so much more experience,

4417
03:16:07,330 --> 03:16:12,430
and I felt like I was performing well.

4418
03:16:12,600 --> 03:16:13,800
I honestly thought I could make it
much further,

4419
03:16:13,800 --> 03:16:17,340
maybe even compete for the win this time.

4420
03:16:17,740 --> 03:16:21,470
I thought I had a good chance this time.

4421
03:16:21,570 --> 03:16:22,780
I can't believe this is how it ends.

4422
03:16:23,780 --> 03:16:27,350
For me, "Bloody Game" was a place...

4423
03:16:27,910 --> 03:16:31,250
where I had to prove myself,
where I had to show what I could do.

4424
03:16:31,950 --> 03:16:33,350
I think I always thought of it that way.

4425
03:16:33,490 --> 03:16:35,560
But now,

4426
03:16:36,160 --> 03:16:39,860
it feels more like a place to learn.

4427
03:16:40,130 --> 03:16:42,030
"How can I grow from this experience?"

4428
03:16:42,030 --> 03:16:44,760
"What can I take away from it and learn?"

4429
03:16:45,230 --> 03:16:48,330
This show has become a place
that makes me reflect on those things.

4430
03:16:48,540 --> 03:16:51,570
I think these feelings, these memories,

4431
03:16:52,610 --> 03:16:54,610
will stay with me for a long time.

4432
03:16:58,650 --> 03:17:00,410
You got this. Hang in there.

4433
03:17:05,150 --> 03:17:06,490
I'm not usually the type to cry easily,

4434
03:17:07,690 --> 03:17:09,820
but the moment I saw Xitsuh's name,

4435
03:17:10,020 --> 03:17:13,060
I just burst into tears.

4436
03:17:13,730 --> 03:17:15,260
To be honest, Xitsuh and I...

4437
03:17:15,260 --> 03:17:18,060
aren't exactly compatible as players.

4438
03:17:18,060 --> 03:17:19,930
We clashed a lot back in Season 3,

4439
03:17:19,930 --> 03:17:21,600
and even early on this season.

4440
03:17:21,600 --> 03:17:23,470
It took time for us
to adjust to each other.

4441
03:17:23,570 --> 03:17:26,010
But after going through all of that...

4442
03:17:26,010 --> 03:17:27,470
and getting to really understand him,

4443
03:17:28,140 --> 03:17:31,780
I realized he's one of the most honest
and fascinating people I've met.

4444
03:17:33,250 --> 03:17:34,610
I felt very sad.

4445
03:17:34,710 --> 03:17:36,820
This isn't right.

4446
03:17:38,950 --> 03:17:40,220
I just hope someone from Team P3 wins.

4447
03:17:45,730 --> 03:17:47,160
I was so sad.

4448
03:17:47,330 --> 03:17:50,460
I really hoped
Xitsuh wouldn't be eliminated.

4449
03:17:50,460 --> 03:17:51,600
I honestly couldn't believe it.

4450
03:17:52,270 --> 03:17:53,330
Gosh.

4451
03:17:57,200 --> 03:17:58,270
Stay strong.

4452
03:17:59,140 --> 03:18:00,140
All right?

4453
03:18:06,650 --> 03:18:09,250
Jin Ho, look out for him. You got this.

4454
03:18:09,980 --> 03:18:11,480
You did great.

4455
03:18:13,290 --> 03:18:16,920
Seong Beom was bawling his eyes out
as he saw Xitsuh off.

4456
03:18:16,920 --> 03:18:19,460
I'm usually pretty rational,
so I'm not someone who cries easily.

4457
03:18:19,790 --> 03:18:21,890
But seeing him cry like that...

4458
03:18:23,630 --> 03:18:26,900
made me feel a bit choked up inside.

4459
03:18:29,300 --> 03:18:33,010
I really hope things work out well
for Xitsuh.

4460
03:18:33,010 --> 03:18:36,680
We've been on the same team
this whole time, and he worked so hard.

4461
03:18:36,680 --> 03:18:40,710
I know he's not someone
who should be eliminated here.

4462
03:18:40,710 --> 03:18:42,150
So it's even more unfortunate,

4463
03:18:42,150 --> 03:18:44,350
but I hope he keeps competing for the win
with an even cooler head,

4464
03:18:44,550 --> 03:18:47,320
and goes on
to achieve much greater things.

4465
03:18:49,320 --> 03:18:50,390
You did great.

4466
03:18:51,260 --> 03:18:52,290
Great work.

4467
03:18:56,160 --> 03:18:57,530
You're making me tear up.

4468
03:19:00,170 --> 03:19:02,040
Of course, I'm disappointed.

4469
03:19:02,140 --> 03:19:05,540
Honestly, it's tough.

4470
03:19:05,610 --> 03:19:08,340
This is actually my first time ever
being eliminated in a survival show.

4471
03:19:08,910 --> 03:19:10,840
At the end of the day,
this survival show...

4472
03:19:12,010 --> 03:19:14,010
is about having one winner,

4473
03:19:14,010 --> 03:19:16,080
so everyone else has to leave eventually.

4474
03:19:16,280 --> 03:19:17,620
Even though you know that's how it works,

4475
03:19:18,650 --> 03:19:19,890
when you actually face it,

4476
03:19:20,820 --> 03:19:22,660
it still hits pretty hard.

4477
03:19:24,720 --> 03:19:29,030
I think bittersweet is the right way
to put it.

4478
03:19:29,230 --> 03:19:30,260
Of course, I'm disappointed.

4479
03:19:30,260 --> 03:19:32,370
This season, Bloody Game X,

4480
03:19:32,370 --> 03:19:34,670
was played mostly as a team competition.

4481
03:19:34,870 --> 03:19:36,600
Everyone created an environment...

4482
03:19:37,200 --> 03:19:39,070
where I could do what I wanted.

4483
03:19:39,370 --> 03:19:42,480
So I have no regrets.
I got to play the kind of games I wanted,

4484
03:19:43,340 --> 03:19:44,810
and I got to play them
the way I wanted to.

4485
03:19:46,350 --> 03:19:47,750
And Keun Woo survived.

4486
03:19:48,050 --> 03:19:51,480
We simply played a fair and fun game,

4487
03:19:52,420 --> 03:19:54,390
and that's just
how the results turned out.

4488
03:19:54,650 --> 03:19:56,420
Seeing him blame himself so much...

4489
03:19:56,820 --> 03:19:59,430
and hold back his tears...

4490
03:19:59,690 --> 03:20:01,560
really showed his sincerity.

4491
03:20:01,930 --> 03:20:04,860
It's just a shame
that my journey ends here.

4492
03:20:07,070 --> 03:20:08,170
But I can always come back someday...

4493
03:20:10,070 --> 03:20:11,640
and win anytime.

4494
03:20:12,270 --> 03:20:14,210
I learned so much here,

4495
03:20:14,210 --> 03:20:17,410
and I'm leaving
with so many great memories.

4496
03:20:18,850 --> 03:20:21,810
What am I going to do without you
starting tomorrow?

4497
03:20:21,810 --> 03:20:22,950
Don't cry, Ji Min.

4498
03:20:23,750 --> 03:20:24,950
What am I going to do without you?

4499
03:20:27,290 --> 03:20:30,120
Don't cry, Ji Min.
You're going to make me cry.

4500
03:20:32,060 --> 03:20:35,700
I was only able to get this far
because of you.

4501
03:20:35,700 --> 03:20:37,730
That's not true at all.

4502
03:20:37,860 --> 03:20:40,430
Seeing him like that
made me cry even more...

4503
03:20:40,430 --> 03:20:44,270
because I know how much he wanted to win,

4504
03:20:44,470 --> 03:20:47,640
how much he prepared for this show,

4505
03:20:47,970 --> 03:20:50,210
and how much he genuinely...

4506
03:20:50,210 --> 03:20:52,850
loves survival shows like this.

4507
03:20:52,850 --> 03:20:54,850
I care about him a lot.

4508
03:20:58,050 --> 03:21:00,020
I felt sorry. I felt really bad.

4509
03:21:00,290 --> 03:21:02,560
If I had been a better player,

4510
03:21:02,560 --> 03:21:05,560
maybe that situation
wouldn't have happened.

4511
03:21:06,060 --> 03:21:08,730
I just wanted to applaud Tae Gyun,
who gave it his all.

4512
03:21:10,630 --> 03:21:12,030
I had a great time!

4513
03:21:12,030 --> 03:21:14,630
Just go to prison. Just go to prison
and come back.

4514
03:21:15,000 --> 03:21:16,070
Thank you for everything.

4515
03:21:16,270 --> 03:21:17,870
I had such a great time here.

4516
03:21:17,870 --> 03:21:19,610
- Great job.
- See you soon.

4517
03:21:20,740 --> 03:21:21,810
Bye.

4518
03:21:22,210 --> 03:21:24,210
- They were awesome.
- They were awesome.

4519
03:21:26,010 --> 03:21:27,010
Take care.

4520
03:21:27,580 --> 03:21:28,610
I'm off.

4521
03:21:33,450 --> 03:21:34,520
Such a shame.

4522
03:21:34,520 --> 03:21:35,860
(Bloody Game X eliminated player:
Lee Tae Gyun)

4523
03:21:35,860 --> 03:21:39,030
(Bloody Game X eliminated player:
Lee Tae Gyun, Xitsuh)

4524
03:21:43,700 --> 03:21:45,160
I'm so sad.

4525
03:21:45,530 --> 03:21:48,330
Xitsuh really did his best today,
even while helping us.

4526
03:21:52,240 --> 03:21:54,870
No, I don't mean
that I'm not happy you came.

4527
03:21:55,740 --> 03:21:57,840
You guys, I...

4528
03:21:57,840 --> 03:22:00,810
Hey, you didn't even say a word
about me still being here.

4529
03:22:00,810 --> 03:22:02,550
Are you not happy to see me?

4530
03:22:02,750 --> 03:22:05,320
Keun Woo, did you pretend
not to know the rules this whole time?

4531
03:22:05,490 --> 03:22:07,850
He was a genius in disguise all along.

4532
03:22:07,850 --> 03:22:09,590
Keun Woo is scary.

4533
03:22:10,090 --> 03:22:13,230
Have any of you ever beaten
Xitsuh or Lee Tae Gyun?

4534
03:22:14,260 --> 03:22:16,060
What can I say? I played well.

4535
03:22:16,330 --> 03:22:18,130
I'm sorry. Take care.

4536
03:22:19,830 --> 03:22:21,770
Gosh, Keun Woo is so cool.

4537
03:22:25,100 --> 03:22:27,170
He's way out of my league.

4538
03:22:27,540 --> 03:22:29,540
Xitsuh, Lee Tae Gyun,

4539
03:22:30,940 --> 03:22:32,010
Hong Jin Ho.

4540
03:22:32,410 --> 03:22:33,450
Goodness, Keun Woo.

4541
03:22:33,680 --> 03:22:35,720
I survived against them.

4542
03:22:35,720 --> 03:22:37,920
- What?
- How is that even possible?

4543
03:22:37,920 --> 03:22:40,590
Bloody Game X is fun.

4544
03:22:40,790 --> 03:22:41,850
He's seriously good.

4545
03:22:41,850 --> 03:22:43,120
Bloody Game X is...

4546
03:22:43,120 --> 03:22:45,320
- He's seriously good.
- The probability is...

4547
03:22:46,260 --> 03:22:48,390
Jin Ho's win just proved...

4548
03:22:48,390 --> 03:22:50,530
that he's still the same Hong Jin Ho.

4549
03:22:50,630 --> 03:22:53,500
He wasn't some washed-up veteran.
He's still got it.

4550
03:22:53,670 --> 03:22:55,330
And Keun Woo. Gosh.

4551
03:22:55,540 --> 03:22:58,040
Did he play baseball here or something?

4552
03:22:58,370 --> 03:23:01,510
He seems like
a completely different person.

4553
03:23:01,610 --> 03:23:03,010
I'm thankful.

4554
03:23:03,440 --> 03:23:04,540
They were all potential winners.

4555
03:23:04,540 --> 03:23:06,450
I just needed any 2 of those 3
to get eliminated.

4556
03:23:06,450 --> 03:23:09,080
Since Keun Woo survived, I'm thankful.
The others can figure it out themselves.

4557
03:23:12,790 --> 03:23:13,850
Are you going to sleep right away?

4558
03:23:13,850 --> 03:23:15,860
No. Let's grab a beer.

4559
03:23:15,890 --> 03:23:16,960
Okay.

4560
03:23:17,190 --> 03:23:19,490
Gosh, the number of remaining people...

4561
03:23:19,860 --> 03:23:21,260
has really shrunk drastically.

4562
03:23:21,960 --> 03:23:24,000
Two potential winners just got eliminated.

4563
03:23:24,000 --> 03:23:25,030
- Right.
- Yes.

4564
03:23:25,900 --> 03:23:27,500
Right now, Team R is really...

4565
03:23:29,000 --> 03:23:30,940
They're really hanging in there.

4566
03:23:32,610 --> 03:23:34,170
You're technically Team R, right?

4567
03:23:34,570 --> 03:23:38,040
As of today, our bond is stronger
than Team P2's.

4568
03:23:38,080 --> 03:23:40,280
- So come back then.
- All right.

4569
03:23:40,550 --> 03:23:43,620
We've got to rebuild that bond again.

4570
03:23:44,780 --> 03:23:45,820
Should I go get my things?

4571
03:23:46,190 --> 03:23:47,620
- Yes, go get them.
- Before I get drunk.

4572
03:23:47,620 --> 03:23:49,020
- Hurry up.
- Okay.

4573
03:23:49,020 --> 03:23:54,830
(Sung Joo goes to get his belongings
from Team R's room.)

4574
03:23:55,230 --> 03:23:59,600
I'm only sleeping there. I'm still Team R.

4575
03:24:00,100 --> 03:24:03,240
If you go over there,
we'll cut ties with you.

4576
03:24:04,640 --> 03:24:05,640
I'm still Team R.

4577
03:24:05,640 --> 03:24:07,470
Do you even know
where you're going back to?

4578
03:24:07,970 --> 03:24:09,440
It's Team P2.

4579
03:24:10,080 --> 03:24:11,680
Don't do anything weird to me tomorrow.

4580
03:24:11,940 --> 03:24:13,310
Don't do anything.

4581
03:24:13,450 --> 03:24:15,850
Your play today was definitely
Team P2's style.

4582
03:24:16,420 --> 03:24:18,120
- What?
- We're disappointed in you.

4583
03:24:18,350 --> 03:24:19,420
Did I do something wrong?

4584
03:24:23,290 --> 03:24:26,890
How does it make sense that the two of us
are the only ones left here?

4585
03:24:26,890 --> 03:24:28,190
I've already packed everything.

4586
03:24:30,600 --> 03:24:32,900
(Neatly packed)

4587
03:24:33,700 --> 03:24:34,770
I packed everything.

4588
03:24:37,300 --> 03:24:40,210
- I've already packed everything.
- This is so funny.

4589
03:24:40,210 --> 03:24:42,910
- You made your bed too.
- I made my bed.

4590
03:24:43,140 --> 03:24:45,540
He didn't pack his bag.

4591
03:24:45,750 --> 03:24:46,750
Of course.

4592
03:24:49,520 --> 03:24:52,490
Tae Gyun didn't have his bag packed.

4593
03:24:54,120 --> 03:24:56,820
Why did he beat Lee Tae Gyun?

4594
03:24:57,160 --> 03:24:59,060
Now the weight on my shoulders
has gotten so heavy.

4595
03:24:59,930 --> 03:25:01,860
Whenever we got a new set of rules,

4596
03:25:02,160 --> 03:25:04,000
Tae Gyun was always the one...

4597
03:25:04,100 --> 03:25:07,270
who explained them again
like a private tutor.

4598
03:25:07,570 --> 03:25:09,970
Now I think I'm going
to have to take over that role.

4599
03:25:10,940 --> 03:25:13,440
I have to guide Keun Woo well,

4600
03:25:14,910 --> 03:25:16,480
but honestly, I feel lost.

4601
03:25:16,880 --> 03:25:18,740
- I packed everything.
- That's impressive.

4602
03:25:18,940 --> 03:25:20,350
Keun Woo.

4603
03:25:20,980 --> 03:25:22,880
If you think about it,

4604
03:25:23,450 --> 03:25:24,620
we might actually win.

4605
03:25:24,620 --> 03:25:25,650
That's right.

4606
03:25:25,650 --> 03:25:27,550
Gosh, if things go on like this,

4607
03:25:27,550 --> 03:25:29,390
- I hope we keep getting games like this.
- Right.

4608
03:25:29,460 --> 03:25:30,490
So tomorrow,

4609
03:25:32,090 --> 03:25:33,860
who should we...

4610
03:25:33,860 --> 03:25:36,130
- Tomorrow, we're taking Seung Yong out.
- Team C and...

4611
03:25:36,400 --> 03:25:38,030
We have to get rid of them.

4612
03:25:38,200 --> 03:25:39,770
There are so many possible scenarios.

4613
03:25:39,770 --> 03:25:41,230
The winner picks someone,

4614
03:25:41,230 --> 03:25:44,370
and the eliminated player like Tae Gyun
picks someone too.

4615
03:25:44,600 --> 03:25:47,410
And whether I get eliminated or not,

4616
03:25:47,410 --> 03:25:49,240
- I'm picking Seung Yong.
- Me too.

4617
03:25:49,240 --> 03:25:51,210
Even if I end up going home,

4618
03:25:51,210 --> 03:25:52,880
I want to go with the option that...

4619
03:25:52,880 --> 03:25:55,010
gives me even the slightest chance
of sending him home.

4620
03:25:55,010 --> 03:25:56,020
Let's get revenge.

4621
03:25:56,250 --> 03:25:59,950
Now that Tae Gyun's gone,
the target has become much clearer.

4622
03:25:59,950 --> 03:26:01,850
It's like a twist of fate.

4623
03:26:01,850 --> 03:26:05,160
Ever since the Heist Game
and the Killer Game before that,

4624
03:26:05,160 --> 03:26:07,560
we kept getting divided into factions.

4625
03:26:07,730 --> 03:26:10,830
So there's no love for the other side.

4626
03:26:14,230 --> 03:26:16,770
By the way, Seung Yong was the one
who insisted on picking you.

4627
03:26:16,770 --> 03:26:18,070
- Really?
- Yes.

4628
03:26:18,270 --> 03:26:19,470
Those snakes.

4629
03:26:19,640 --> 03:26:22,110
- At first, to set the public opinion,
- It was like...

4630
03:26:22,210 --> 03:26:24,240
I said we should find the justification
strictly within the game.

4631
03:26:24,240 --> 03:26:26,010
And I said that the biggest mistake...

4632
03:26:26,010 --> 03:26:27,650
I saw during the game was Tae Gyun's,

4633
03:26:27,650 --> 03:26:29,450
and that I thought
Jin Ho made a mistake too.

4634
03:26:30,050 --> 03:26:31,680
But they were already saying,

4635
03:26:31,920 --> 03:26:34,250
"No, we're sending out
the strongest player no matter what."

4636
03:26:34,390 --> 03:26:36,390
I know this is a survival show,
I know this is a game,

4637
03:26:36,390 --> 03:26:37,790
and I get
that this was a unique situation. But...

4638
03:26:43,260 --> 03:26:45,600
Tomorrow, the target is obviously him.

4639
03:26:45,660 --> 03:26:47,700
- Who?
- It's obviously Seung Yong.

4640
03:26:49,300 --> 03:26:51,500
Tomorrow's target is marked
for elimination.

4641
03:26:51,770 --> 03:26:55,140
The phrase "karma comes around"
couldn't be more fitting.

4642
03:26:55,140 --> 03:26:56,180
He's going to be eliminated tomorrow?

4643
03:26:56,480 --> 03:26:58,540
Yes. Everyone's going to gang up on him.

4644
03:26:59,980 --> 03:27:03,050
In a survival show, nothing is more
important than having a justification.

4645
03:27:07,690 --> 03:27:10,590
I wonder what kind of game
we'll be playing tomorrow.

4646
03:27:12,260 --> 03:27:13,830
Whatever it is, it'll be fun tomorrow too.

4647
03:28:18,390 --> 03:28:20,390
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
